\s1 God Instructs Joshua
\r (\ref Deuteronomy 11:8–17|DEU 11:8-17\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Now|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֛י\rb* \rb the death|מ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of His|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb servant|עֶ֣בֶד\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb spoke|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֣עַ\rb* \rb son|בִּן־\rb* \rb of Nun|נ֔וּן\rb*, \rb Moses’|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb assistant|מְשָׁרֵ֥ת\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb* \rb My servant|עַבְדִּ֖י\rb* \rb is dead|מֵ֑ת\rb*. \rb Now therefore|וְעַתָּה֩\rb* \rb arise|ק֨וּם\rb*, \rb you|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb these people|הָעָ֣ם\rb*, \rb and cross over|עֲבֹ֜ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֣ן\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֗ה\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֕רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb am giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb to|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb the children|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb I have given you|נְתַתִּ֑יו\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb place|מָק֗וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the sole|כַּֽף־\rb* \rb of your foot|רַגְלְכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb will tread|תִּדְרֹ֧ךְ\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I promised|דִּבַּ֖רְתִּי\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb Your territory|גְּבוּלְכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb shall extend|יִֽהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb from the wilderness|מֵהַמִּדְבָּר֩\rb* \rb and Lebanon|וְהַלְּבָנ֨וֹן\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb to|וְֽעַד־\rb* \rb the great|הַגָּד֣וֹל\rb* \rb River|נְהַר־\rb* \rb Euphrates|פְּרָ֗ת\rb*\rb |הַנָּהָ֧ר\rb*— \rb all|כֹּ֚ל\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Hittites|הַֽחִתִּ֔ים\rb*— \rb and west|מְב֣וֹא\rb*\rb |הַשָּׁ֑מֶשׁ\rb* \rb as far as|וְעַד־\rb* \rb the Great|הַגָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb Sea|הַיָּ֥ם\rb*.\f + \fr 1:4 \ft That is, the Mediterranean Sea\f*
\p \v 5 \rb No|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb one|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb shall stand|יִתְיַצֵּ֥ב\rb* \rb against you|לְפָנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of your life|חַיֶּ֑יךָ\rb*. \rb As|כַּֽאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I was|אֶהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb with|עִמָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb*, \rb so will I be|הָיִ֤יתִי\rb* \rb with you|עִם־\rb*; \rb I will never|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb leave you|אַרְפְּךָ֖\rb* \rb nor|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb forsake you|אֶעֶזְבֶֽךָּ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 1:5 \ft Cited in \ref Hebrews 13:5|HEB 13:5\ref*\f*
\p \v 6 \rb Be strong|חֲזַ֖ק\rb* \rb and courageous|וֶאֱמָ֑ץ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb shall give these people the inheritance|תַּנְחִיל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הָעָ֣ם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֕רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I swore|נִשְׁבַּ֥עְתִּי\rb* \rb to their fathers|לַאֲבוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb I would give|לָתֵ֥ת\rb* \rb them|לָהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Above all|רַק֩\rb*, \rb be strong|חֲזַ֨ק\rb* \rb and very|מְאֹ֗ד\rb* \rb courageous|וֶֽאֱמַ֜ץ\rb*. \rb Be careful|לִשְׁמֹ֤ר\rb* \rb to observe|לַעֲשׂוֹת֙\rb* \rb all|כְּכָל־\rb* \rb the law|הַתּוֹרָ֗ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb My servant|עַבְדִּ֔י\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb commanded you|צִוְּךָ֙\rb*. \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb turn|תָּס֥וּר\rb* \rb from|מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb it to the right|יָמִ֣ין\rb* \rb or to the left|וּשְׂמֹ֑אול\rb*, \rb so that|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb you may prosper|תַּשְׂכִּ֔יל\rb* \rb wherever|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you go|תֵּלֵֽךְ׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb This|הַזֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb Book|סֵפֶר֩\rb* \rb of the Law|הַתּוֹרָ֨ה\rb* \rb must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb depart|יָמ֡וּשׁ\rb* \rb from your mouth|מִפִּ֗יךָ\rb*; \rb meditate|וְהָגִ֤יתָ\rb* \rb on it|בּוֹ֙\rb* \rb day|יוֹמָ֣ם\rb* \rb and night|וָלַ֔יְלָה\rb*, \rb so that|לְמַ֙עַן֙\rb* \rb you may be careful|תִּשְׁמֹ֣ר\rb* \rb to do|לַעֲשׂ֔וֹת\rb* \rb everything|כְּכָל־\rb* \rb written|הַכָּת֖וּב\rb* \rb in it|בּ֑וֹ\rb*. \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb then|אָ֛ז\rb* \rb you will prosper|תַּצְלִ֥יחַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and succeed|תַּשְׂכִּֽיל׃\rb* \rb in all you do|דְּרָכֶ֖ךָ\rb*\rb |וְאָ֥ז\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Have I not|הֲל֤וֹא\rb* \rb commanded you|צִוִּיתִ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb to be strong|חֲזַ֣ק\rb* \rb and courageous|וֶאֱמָ֔ץ\rb*? \rb Do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תַּעֲרֹ֖ץ\rb*;\rb |וְאַל־\rb* \rb do not be discouraged|תֵּחָ֑ת\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb is with|עִמְּךָ֙\rb* \rb you wherever|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you go|תֵּלֵֽךְ׃פ\rb*.”
\s1 Joshua Takes Charge
\p \v 10 \rb Then Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb commanded|וַיְצַ֣ו\rb* \rb the officers|שֹׁטְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*: \v 11 “\rb Go|עִבְר֣וּ׀\rb* \rb through|בְּקֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֗ה\rb* \rb and tell|וְצַוּ֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֙\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* ‘\rb Prepare|הָכִ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb your|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb provisions|צֵידָ֑ה\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֞י\rb* \rb within|בְּע֣וֹד׀\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֗ים\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb will cross|עֹֽבְרִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb to go in|לָבוֹא֙\rb* \rb and take possession of|לָרֶ֣שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to possess|לְרִשְׁתָּֽהּ׃ס\rb*.’”
\p \v 12 \rb But to the Reubenites|וְלָרֽאוּבֵנִי֙\rb*, \rb the Gadites|וְלַגָּדִ֔י\rb*, \rb and the half-tribe|וְלַחֲצִ֖י\rb*\rb |שֵׁ֣בֶט\rb* \rb of Manasseh|הַֽמְנַשֶּׁ֑ה\rb*, \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֥ר\rb*, \v 13 “\rb Remember|זָכוֹר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb* \rb the servant|עֶֽבֶד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb when he said|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, ‘\rb The LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb will give you rest|מֵנִ֣יחַ\rb*, \rb and He will give|וְנָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֥רֶץ\rb*.’ \v 14 \rb Your wives|נְשֵׁיכֶ֣ם\rb*, \rb your young children|טַפְּכֶם֮\rb*, \rb and your livestock|וּמִקְנֵיכֶם֒\rb* \rb may remain|יֵשְׁב֕וּ\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֕רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb gave|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb on this side|בְּעֵ֣בֶר\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֑ן\rb*.\rb |וְאַתֶּם֩\rb* \rb But all|כֹּ֚ל\rb* \rb your mighty men|גִּבּוֹרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of valor|הַחַ֔יִל\rb* \rb must be armed for battle|חֲמֻשִׁ֜ים\rb* \rb to cross over|תַּעַבְר֨וּ\rb* \rb ahead of|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb your brothers|אֲחֵיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb and help them|וַעֲזַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אוֹתָֽם׃\rb*, \v 15 \rb until|עַ֠ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה׀\rb* \rb gives them rest|יָנִ֨יחַ\rb*\rb |לַֽאֲחֵיכֶם֮\rb* \rb as He has done for you|כָּכֶם֒\rb*, \rb and your brothers|הֵ֔מָּה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb also|גַם־\rb* \rb possess|וְיָרְשׁ֣וּ\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֕רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֣ן\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Then you may return|וְשַׁבְתֶּ֞ם\rb* \rb to the land|לְאֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb of your inheritance|יְרֻשַּׁתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb and take possession of|וִֽירִשְׁתֶּ֣ם\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb that which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר׀\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb the servant|עֶ֣בֶד\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb gave|נָתַ֣ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb on the east|מִזְרַ֥ח\rb*\rb |הַשָּֽׁמֶשׁ׃\rb* \rb side|בְּעֵ֥בֶר\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֖ן\rb*.”
\p \v 16 \rb So they answered|וַֽיַּעֲנ֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Everything|כֹּ֤ל\rb* \rb you have commanded us|צִוִּיתָ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb we will do|נַֽעֲשֶׂ֔ה\rb*, \rb and everywhere|וְאֶֽל־\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you send us|תִּשְׁלָחֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb we will go|נֵלֵֽךְ׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb Just as|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb we obeyed|נִשְׁמַ֣ע\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֑יךָ\rb*\rb |רַ֠ק\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*\rb |כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb in all things|כְּכֹ֤ל\rb*, \rb so we will obey you|שָׁמַ֙עְנוּ֙\rb*.\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb And may the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb be|יִֽהְיֶ֞ה\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּ֔ךְ\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He was|הָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb Anyone|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אִ֞ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb rebels|יַמְרֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb against your order|פִּ֗יךָ\rb* \rb and does not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb obey|יִשְׁמַ֧ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your words|דְּבָרֶ֛יךָ\rb*, \rb all|לְכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you command him|תְּצַוֶּ֖נּוּ\rb*, \rb will be put to death|יוּמָ֑ת\rb*. \rb Above all|רַ֖ק\rb*, \rb be strong|חֲזַ֥ק\rb* \rb and courageous|וֶאֱמָֽץ׃פ\rb*!”
\c 2
\s1 Rahab Welcomes the Spies
\r (\ref Hebrews 11:30–31|HEB 11:30-31\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Then Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֣עַ־\rb* \rb son|בִּן־\rb* \rb of Nun|נ֠וּן\rb* \rb secretly|חֶ֣רֶשׁ\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb two|שְׁנַֽיִם־\rb*\rb |אֲנָשִׁ֤ים\rb* \rb spies|מְרַגְּלִים֙\rb* \rb from|מִֽן־\rb* \rb Shittim|הַשִּׁטִּ֞ים\rb*,\f + \fr 2:1 \ft Or \fqa Acacia Grove\f* \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Go|לְכ֛וּ\rb*, \rb inspect|רְא֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb especially Jericho|יְרִיח֑וֹ\rb*.” \rb So they went|וַיֵּ֨לְכ֜וּ\rb* \rb and entered|וַ֠יָּבֹאוּ\rb* \rb the house|בֵּית־\rb*\rb |אִשָּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb of a prostitute|זוֹנָ֛ה\rb* \rb named|וּשְׁמָ֥הּ\rb* \rb Rahab|רָחָ֖ב\rb* \rb and stayed|וַיִּשְׁכְּבוּ־\rb* \rb there|שָֽׁמָּה׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb And it was reported|וַיֵּ֣אָמַ֔ר\rb* \rb to the king|לְמֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Jericho|יְרִיח֖וֹ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*: “\rb Behold|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb*, \rb some men|אֲ֠נָשִׁים\rb*\rb |מִבְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb have come|בָּ֣אוּ\rb* \rb here|הֵ֧נָּה\rb* \rb tonight|הַלַּ֛יְלָה\rb* \rb to spy out|לַחְפֹּ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb So the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Jericho|יְרִיח֔וֹ\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַח֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Rahab|רָחָ֖ב\rb* \rb and said|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Bring out|ה֠וֹצִיאִי\rb* \rb the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֨ים\rb* \rb who came|הַבָּאִ֤ים\rb* \rb to|אֵלַ֙יִךְ֙\rb* \rb you|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb and entered|בָּ֣אוּ\rb* \rb your house|לְבֵיתֵ֔ךְ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb they have come|בָּֽאוּ׃\rb* \rb to spy out|לַחְפֹּ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb But the woman|הָֽאִשָּׁ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had taken|וַתִּקַּ֧ח\rb* \rb the two|שְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb and hidden them|וַֽתִּצְפְּנ֑וֹ\rb*. \rb So she said|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר׀\rb*, “\rb Yes|כֵּ֗ן\rb*, \rb the men|הָֽאֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb did come|בָּ֤אוּ\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַי֙\rb*, \rb but I did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֖עְתִּי\rb* \rb where|מֵאַ֥יִן\rb* \rb they had come from|הֵֽמָּה׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb At dusk|בַּחֹ֙שֶׁךְ֙\rb*, \rb when the gate|הַשַּׁ֜עַר\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֨י\rb* \rb about to close|לִסְגּ֗וֹר\rb*, \rb the men|וְהָאֲנָשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb went out|יָצָ֔אוּ\rb*, \rb and I do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֔עְתִּי\rb* \rb which way|אָ֥נָה\rb* \rb they|הָֽאֲנָשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb went|הָלְכ֖וּ\rb*. \rb Pursue|רִדְפ֥וּ\rb* \rb them|אַחֲרֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb quickly|מַהֵ֛ר\rb*, \rb and|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you may catch them|תַשִּׂיגֽוּם׃\rb*!” \v 6 (\rb But Rahab|וְהִ֖יא\rb* \rb had taken them up|הֶעֱלָ֣תַם\rb* \rb to the roof|הַגָּ֑גָה\rb* \rb and hidden them|וַֽתִּטְמְנֵם֙\rb* \rb among the stalks|הָעֵ֔ץ\rb* \rb of flax|בְּפִשְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb that she had laid out|הָעֲרֻכ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb there|הַגָּֽג׃\rb*.)
\p \v 7 \rb So the king’s men|וְהָאֲנָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb set out in pursuit|רָדְפ֤וּ\rb* \rb of the spies|אַֽחֲרֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb along the road|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the fords|הַֽמַּעְבְּר֑וֹת\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb*, \rb and as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb soon as they|יָצְא֥וּ\rb* \rb had gone out|הָרֹדְפִ֖ים\rb*,\rb |אַחֲרֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb the gate|וְהַשַּׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb was shut|סָגָ֔רוּ\rb*.\rb |אַחֲרֵ֕י\rb*
\s1 The Promise to Rahab
\p \v 8 \rb Before|טֶ֣רֶם\rb* \rb the spies|וְהֵ֖מָּה\rb* \rb lay down for the night|יִשְׁכָּב֑וּן\rb*, \rb Rahab|וְהִ֛יא\rb* \rb went up|עָלְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb on|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the roof|הַגָּֽג׃\rb* \v 9 \rb and said|וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to them|אֶל־\rb*\rb |הָ֣אֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb*, “\rb I know|יָדַ֕עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb has given|נָתַ֧ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb this land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb and that|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb the fear of you|אֵֽימַתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb has fallen|נָפְלָ֤ה\rb* \rb on us|עָלֵ֔ינוּ\rb*, \rb so that|וְכִ֥י\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who dwell|יֹשְׁבֵ֥י\rb* \rb in the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb are melting in fear|נָמֹ֛גוּ\rb* \rb of you|מִפְּנֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb we have heard|שָׁמַ֗עְנוּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֠ת\rb* \rb how|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb dried up|הוֹבִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb the waters|מֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the Red|סוּף֙\rb* \rb Sea|יַם־\rb*\f + \fr 2:10 \ft Or \fqa the Sea of Reeds\f* \rb before you|מִפְּנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb when you came out|בְּצֵאתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִמִּצְרָ֑יִם\rb*, \rb and what|וַאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you did|עֲשִׂיתֶ֡ם\rb* \rb to Sihon|לְסִיחֹ֣ן\rb* \rb and Og|וּלְע֔וֹג\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the two|לִשְׁנֵי֩\rb* \rb kings|מַלְכֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the Amorites|הָאֱמֹרִ֜י\rb* \rb across|בְּעֵ֤בֶר\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּן֙\rb*, \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you devoted to destruction|הֶחֱרַמְתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אוֹתָֽם׃\rb*.\f + \fr 2:10 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering.\f* \v 11 \rb When we heard this|וַנִּשְׁמַע֙\rb*, \rb our hearts|לְבָבֵ֔נוּ\rb* \rb melted|וַיִּמַּ֣ס\rb* \rb and everyone’s|בְּאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb courage|ר֛וּחַ\rb* \rb failed|וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |קָ֨מָה\rb*\rb |ע֥וֹד\rb* \rb because of you|מִפְּנֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |ה֤וּא\rb* \rb is God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb in the heavens|בַּשָּׁמַ֣יִם\rb* \rb above|מִמַּ֔עַל\rb* \rb and on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb below|מִתָּֽחַת׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Now therefore|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb*, \rb please|נָ֥א\rb* \rb swear|הִשָּֽׁבְעוּ־\rb* \rb to me|לִי֙\rb* \rb by the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb that you|אַתֶּ֜ם\rb* \rb will indeed|גַּם־\rb* \rb show|וַעֲשִׂיתֶ֨ם\rb* \rb kindness|חֶ֔סֶד\rb* \rb to|עִם־\rb* \rb my family|בֵּ֤ית\rb*\rb |אָבִי֙\rb*, \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb I showed|עָשִׂ֥יתִי\rb* \rb kindness|חָ֑סֶד\rb* \rb to you|עִמָּכֶ֖ם\rb*. \rb Give|וּנְתַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb me|לִ֖י\rb* \rb a sure|אֱמֶֽת׃\rb* \rb sign|א֥וֹת\rb* \v 13 \rb that you will spare the lives|וְהַחֲיִתֶ֞ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of my father|אָבִ֣י\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb mother|אִמִּ֗י\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb my brothers|אַחַי֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb sisters|אַחוֹתַי\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who belong|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and that you will deliver|וְהִצַּלְתֶּ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb us|נַפְשֹׁתֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb from death|מִמָּֽוֶת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 14 “\rb Our lives|נַפְשֵׁ֤נוּ\rb* \rb for your|תַחְתֵּיכֶם֙\rb* \rb lives|לָמ֔וּת\rb*!” \rb the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb agreed|וַיֹּ֧אמְרוּ\rb*. “\rb If|אִ֚ם\rb* \rb you do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb report|תַגִּ֔ידוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb our mission|דְּבָרֵ֖נוּ\rb*,\rb |זֶ֑ה\rb*\rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb we will show|וְעָשִׂ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb you|עִמָּ֖ךְ\rb* \rb kindness|חֶ֥סֶד\rb* \rb and faithfulness|וֶאֱמֶֽת׃\rb* \rb when the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb gives|בְּתֵת־\rb* \rb us|לָ֙נוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb Then Rahab let them down|וַתּוֹרִדֵ֥ם\rb* \rb by a rope|בַּחֶ֖בֶל\rb* \rb through|בְּעַ֣ד\rb* \rb the window|הַֽחַלּ֑וֹן\rb*, \rb since|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the house|בֵיתָהּ֙\rb* \rb where she|הִ֥יא\rb* \rb lived|יוֹשָֽׁבֶת׃\rb* \rb was built into the wall|בְּקִ֣יר\rb* \rb of the city|הַֽחוֹמָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וּבַֽחוֹמָ֖ה\rb*. \v 16 “\rb Go|לֵּ֔כוּ\rb* \rb to the hill country|הָהָ֣רָה\rb*,” \rb she said|וַתֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, “\rb so that your pursuers|הָרֹדְפִ֑ים\rb* \rb will not|פֶּֽן־\rb* \rb find|יִפְגְּע֥וּ\rb* \rb you|בָכֶ֖ם\rb*. \rb Hide yourselves|וְנַחְבֵּתֶ֨ם\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֜מָּה\rb* \rb for three|שְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֗ים\rb* \rb until|עַ֚ד\rb* \rb they|הָרֹֽדְפִ֔ים\rb* \rb have returned|שׁ֣וֹב\rb*; \rb then|וְאַחַ֖ר\rb* \rb go|תֵּלְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb on your way|לְדַרְכְּכֶֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 17 \rb The men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמְר֥וּ\rb* \rb to her|אֵלֶ֖יהָ\rb*, “\rb We|אֲנַ֔חְנוּ\rb* \rb will not be bound|נְקִיִּ֣ם\rb* \rb by this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb oath|מִשְּׁבֻעָתֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb you made us swear|הִשְׁבַּעְתָּֽנוּ׃\rb* \v 18 \rb unless|הִנֵּ֛ה\rb*, \rb when we|אֲנַ֥חְנוּ\rb* \rb enter|בָאִ֖ים\rb* \rb the land|בָּאָ֑רֶץ\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb you have tied|תִּקְשְׁרִ֗י\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb scarlet|הַשָּׁנִ֨י\rb* \rb cord|תִּקְוַ֡ת\rb*\rb |חוּט֩\rb* \rb in the window|בַּֽחַלּוֹן֙\rb* \rb through which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you let us down|הוֹרַדְתֵּ֣נוּ\rb*, \rb and unless|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb you have brought|תַּאַסְפִ֥י\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֖יִךְ\rb* \rb your father|אָבִ֨יךְ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb mother|אִמֵּ֜ךְ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb brothers|אַחַ֗יִךְ\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אָבִ֔יךְ\rb* \rb your family|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb into your house|הַבָּֽיְתָה׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb |וְהָיָ֡ה\rb* \rb If anyone|כֹּ֣ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb goes out|יֵצֵא֩\rb* \rb the door|מִדַּלְתֵ֨י\rb* \rb of your house|בֵיתֵ֧ךְ׀\rb* \rb into the street|הַח֛וּצָה\rb*, \rb his blood will be|דָּמ֥וֹ\rb* \rb on his own head|בְרֹאשׁ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb and we|וַאֲנַ֣חְנוּ\rb* \rb will be innocent|נְקִיִּ֑ם\rb*. \rb But if|אִם־\rb* \rb a hand|יָ֖ד\rb* \rb is laid|תִּֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb on|בּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb anyone|וְ֠כֹל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb with you|אִתָּךְ֙\rb* \rb in the house|בַּבַּ֔יִת\rb*\rb |יִֽהְיֶ֤ה\rb*, \rb his blood|דָּמ֣וֹ\rb* \rb will be on our heads|בְרֹאשֵׁ֔נוּ\rb*. \v 20 \rb And if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you report|תַּגִּ֖ידִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb our mission|דְּבָרֵ֣נוּ\rb*,\rb |זֶ֑ה\rb* \rb we will be|וְהָיִ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb released|נְקִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb from the oath|מִשְּׁבֻעָתֵ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you made us swear|הִשְׁבַּעְתָּֽנוּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 21 “\rb Let it|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb be as you say|כְּדִבְרֵיכֶ֣ם\rb*\rb |כֶּן־\rb*,” \rb she replied|וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, \rb and she sent them away|וַֽתְּשַׁלְּחֵ֖ם\rb*. \rb And when they had gone|וַיֵּלֵ֑כוּ\rb*, \rb she tied|וַתִּקְשֹׁ֛ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the scarlet|הַשָּׁנִ֖י\rb* \rb cord|תִּקְוַ֥ת\rb* \rb in the window|בַּחַלּֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb |וַיֵּלְכוּ֙\rb* \rb So the spies went out|וַיָּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb into the hill country|הָהָ֔רָה\rb* \rb and stayed|וַיֵּ֤שְׁבוּ\rb* \rb there|שָׁם֙\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֔ים\rb*, \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb their pursuers|הָרֹדְפִ֑ים\rb* \rb had returned|שָׁ֖בוּ\rb* \rb without|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb finding them|מָצָֽאוּ׃\rb*,\rb |הָרֹדְפִ֛ים\rb* \rb having searched|וַיְבַקְשׁ֧וּ\rb* \rb all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb along the road|הַדֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb*. \v 23 \rb Then the two men|הָֽאֲנָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb started back|וַיָּשֻׁ֜בוּ\rb*,\rb |שְׁנֵ֤י\rb* \rb came down|וַיֵּרְד֣וּ\rb* \rb from the hill country|מֵֽהָהָ֔ר\rb*, \rb and crossed the river|וַיַּעַבְרוּ֙\rb*. \rb So they came|וַיָּבֹ֔אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb* \rb son|בִּן־\rb* \rb of Nun|נ֑וּן\rb* \rb and reported|וַיְסַ֨פְּרוּ־\rb*\rb |ל֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that had happened|הַמֹּצְא֖וֹת\rb* \rb to them|אוֹתָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 “\rb The LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb has surely|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb delivered|נָתַ֧ן\rb* \rb the entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb into our hands|בְּיָדֵ֖נוּ\rb*,” \rb they said|וַיֹּאמְרוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* “\rb Indeed|וְגַם־\rb*, \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who dwell|יֹשְׁבֵ֥י\rb* \rb in the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb are melting in fear|נָמֹ֛גוּ\rb* \rb of us|מִפָּנֵֽינוּ׃ס\rb*.”
\c 3
\s1 Crossing the Jordan
\p \v 1 \rb Early the next morning|בַּבֹּ֜קֶר\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֨עַ\rb* \rb got up|וַיַּשְׁכֵּם֩\rb* \rb and left|וַיִּסְע֣וּ\rb* \rb Shittim|מֵֽהַשִּׁטִּ֗ים\rb*\f + \fr 3:1 \ft Or \fqa Acacia Grove\f* \rb with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb They went|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb as|עַד־\rb* \rb far as the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb*, \rb where they camped|וַיָּלִ֥נוּ\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb before|טֶ֥רֶם\rb* \rb crossing over|יַעֲבֹֽרוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb |וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb After|מִקְצֵ֖ה\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb the officers|הַשֹּׁטְרִ֖ים\rb* \rb went|וַיַּעַבְר֥וּ\rb* \rb through|בְּקֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶֽה׃\rb* \v 3 \rb and commanded|וַיְצַוּוּ֮\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֣ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹר֒\rb*: “\rb When you see|כִּרְאֽוֹתְכֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֤וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹ֣הֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb being carried|נֹשְׂאִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb by the Levitical|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb priests|וְהַכֹּֽהֲנִים֙\rb*, \rb you|וְאַתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb are to set out|תִּסְעוּ֙\rb* \rb from your positions|מִמְּק֣וֹמְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and follow|וַהֲלַכְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb it|אַחֲרָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb But|אַ֣ךְ׀\rb* \rb keep a distance|רָח֣וֹק\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֗ה\rb* \rb of about two thousand|כְּאַלְפַּ֥יִם\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 3:4 \fqa 2,000 cubits \ft is approximately 3,000 feet or 914.4 meters.\f*\rb |בַּמִּדָּ֑ה\rb* \rb between yourselves|בֵּֽינֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb and the ark|וּבֵינוֹ\rb*. \rb Do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb go near it|תִּקְרְב֣וּ\rb*,\rb |אֵלָ֗יו\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֤עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you can see|תֵּֽדְעוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the way|הַדֶּ֙רֶךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb to go|תֵּֽלְכוּ־\rb*, \rb since|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you have never|לֹ֧א\rb* \rb traveled|עֲבַרְתֶּ֛ם\rb* \rb this way|בַּדֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb before|מִתְּמ֥וֹל\rb*\rb |שִׁלְשֽׁוֹם׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb Then Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֛עַ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb*, “\rb Consecrate yourselves|הִתְקַדָּ֑שׁוּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb tomorrow|מָחָ֗ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb will do|יַעֲשֶׂ֧ה\rb* \rb wonders|נִפְלָאֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb among you|בְּקִרְבְּכֶ֖ם\rb*.” \v 6 \rb And he|יְהוֹשֻׁ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֣ים\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* “\rb Take|שְׂאוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|הַבְּרִ֔ית\rb* \rb and go on|וְעִבְר֖וּ\rb* \rb ahead of|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb*.” \rb So they carried|וַיִּשְׂאוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|הַבְּרִ֔ית\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb ahead|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of them|הָעָֽם׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Now the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb*, “\rb Today|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֗ה\rb* \rb I will begin|אָחֵל֙\rb* \rb to exalt you|גַּדֶּלְךָ֔\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb so|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb they may know|יֵֽדְע֔וּן\rb* \rb that|כִּ֗י\rb* \rb I am|הָיִ֛יתִי\rb* \rb with you|עִם־\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I was|אֶהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb with|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb*. \v 8 \rb |וְאַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb Command|תְּצַוֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb carrying|נֹשְׂאֵ֥י\rb* \rb the ark|אֲרֽוֹן־\rb* \rb of the covenant|הַבְּרִ֖ית\rb*:\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* ‘\rb When you reach|כְּבֹאֲכֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb the edge|קְצֵה֙\rb* \rb of the waters|מֵ֣י\rb*,\rb |הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb stand|תַּעֲמֹֽדוּ׃פ\rb* \rb in the Jordan|בַּיַּרְדֵּ֖ן\rb*.’”
\p \v 9 \rb So Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, “\rb Come|גֹּ֣שׁוּ\rb* \rb here|הֵ֔נָּה\rb* \rb and listen|וְשִׁמְע֕וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the words|דִּבְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.” \v 10 \rb He|יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb* \rb continued|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb This is how|בְּזֹאת֙\rb* \rb you will know|תֵּֽדְע֔וּן\rb* \rb that|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb the living|חַ֖י\rb* \rb God is|אֵ֥ל\rb* \rb among you|בְּקִרְבְּכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and that He will surely drive out|וְהוֹרֵ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |יוֹרִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb before you|מִ֠פְּנֵיכֶם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Canaanites|הַכְּנַעֲנִ֨י\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Hittites|הַחִתִּ֜י\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Hivites|הַחִוִּ֗י\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Perizzites|הַפְּרִזִּי֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Girgashites|הַגִּרְגָּשִׁ֔י\rb*, \rb Amorites|וְהָאֱמֹרִ֖י\rb*, \rb and Jebusites|וְהַיְבוּסִֽי׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb Behold|הִנֵּה֙\rb*, \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|הַבְּרִ֔ית\rb* \rb of the Lord|אֲד֖וֹן\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb will go|עֹבֵ֥ר\rb* \rb ahead of you|לִפְנֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb into the Jordan|בַּיַּרְדֵּֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb choose|קְח֤וּ\rb* \rb twelve|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֣ר\rb* \rb men|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb from the tribes|מִשִּׁבְטֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֥ד\rb*\rb |אִישׁ־\rb*\rb |אֶחָ֖ד\rb*\rb |אִישׁ־\rb* \rb from each tribe|לַשָּֽׁבֶט׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb |וְהָיָ֡ה\rb* \rb When the feet|כַּפּ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |רַגְלֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֡ים\rb* \rb who carry|נֹשְׂאֵי֩\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֨וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* — \rb the Lord|אֲד֤וֹן\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* — \rb touch down|כְּנ֣וֹחַ\rb* \rb in the waters|בְּמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb*, \rb its|הַיַּרְדֵּן֙\rb* \rb flowing|הַיֹּרְדִ֖ים\rb*\rb |מִלְמָ֑עְלָה\rb* \rb waters|מֵ֤י\rb* \rb will be cut off|יִכָּ֣רֵת֔וּן\rb* \rb and|הַמַּ֥יִם\rb* \rb will stand up|וְיַעַמְד֖וּ\rb* \rb in a|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb heap|נֵ֥ד\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb So|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb when the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb broke camp|בִּנְסֹ֤עַ\rb*\rb |מֵאָ֣הֳלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to cross|לַעֲבֹ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֑ן\rb*, \rb the priests|וְהַכֹּהֲנִ֗ים\rb* \rb carried|נֹֽשְׂאֵ֛י\rb* \rb the ark|הָאָר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|הַבְּרִ֖ית\rb* \rb ahead of|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb them|הָעָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Now the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb overflows|מָלֵא֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb its banks|גְּדוֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb throughout|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the harvest|קָצִֽיר׃\rb* \rb season|יְמֵ֥י\rb*. \rb But as soon as the priests|הַכֹּֽהֲנִים֙\rb*\rb |נֹשְׂאֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הָֽאָר֔וֹן\rb* \rb carrying|נֹשְׂאֵ֤י\rb* \rb the ark|הָֽאָרוֹן֙\rb* \rb reached|וּכְב֞וֹא\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb the Jordan|וְהַיַּרְדֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb and their feet|וְרַגְלֵ֤י\rb* \rb touched|נִטְבְּל֖וּ\rb* \rb the water’s|הַמָּ֑יִם\rb* \rb edge|בִּקְצֵ֣ה\rb*, \v 16 \rb the flowing|הַיֹּרְדִ֨ים\rb*\rb |מִלְמַ֜עְלָה\rb* \rb water|הַמַּיִם֩\rb* \rb stood still|וַיַּעַמְד֡וּ\rb*. \rb It backed up|קָ֣מוּ\rb*\rb |אֶחָ֗ד\rb*\rb |נֵד־\rb* \rb as far upstream|הַרְחֵ֨ק\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֜ד\rb* \rb as Adam|בָאָדָם\rb*, \rb a city|הָעִיר֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb in the area|מִצַּ֣ד\rb* \rb of Zarethan|צָֽרְתָ֔ן\rb*, \rb while the water flowing|וְהַיֹּרְדִ֗ים\rb* \rb toward|עַ֣ל\rb* \rb the Sea|יָ֧ם\rb* \rb of the Arabah|הָעֲרָבָ֛ה\rb* (\rb the Salt Sea|יָם־\rb*\f + \fr 3:16 \ft That is, the Dead Sea\f*)\rb |הַמֶּ֖לַח\rb* \rb was completely|תַּ֣מּוּ\rb* \rb cut off|נִכְרָ֑תוּ\rb*. \rb So the people|וְהָעָ֥ם\rb* \rb crossed over|עָבְר֖וּ\rb* \rb opposite|נֶ֥גֶד\rb* \rb Jericho|יְרִיחֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb The priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֡ים\rb* \rb carrying|נֹ֠שְׂאֵי\rb* \rb the ark|הָאָר֨וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb stood|וַיַּעַמְד֣וּ\rb* \rb firm|הָכֵ֑ן\rb* \rb on dry ground|בֶּחָֽרָבָ֛ה\rb* \rb in the middle|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֖ן\rb*, \rb while all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb crossed over|עֹֽבְרִים֙\rb* \rb the dry ground|בֶּחָ֣רָבָ֔ה\rb*, \rb until|עַ֤ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb nation|הַגּ֔וֹי\rb*\rb |תַּ֙מּוּ֙\rb* \rb had crossed|לַעֲבֹ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּֽן׃\rb*.
\c 4
\s1 Twelve Stones from the Jordan
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb When|כַּאֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the whole|כָל־\rb* \rb nation|הַגּ֔וֹי\rb* \rb had finished|תַּ֣מּוּ\rb* \rb crossing|לַעֲב֖וֹר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֑ן פ\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Choose|קְח֤וּ\rb* \rb twelve|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֲנָשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb men|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb from among|מִן־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֥ד\rb*\rb |אִישׁ־\rb*\rb |אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb from each tribe|מִשָּֽׁבֶט׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb and command them|וְצַוּ֣וּ\rb*:\rb |אוֹתָם֮\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹר֒\rb* ‘\rb Take up|שְׂאֽוּ־\rb* \rb for yourselves|לָכֶ֨ם\rb* \rb twelve|שְׁתֵּים־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֣ה\rb* \rb stones|אֲבָנִ֑ים\rb* \rb from|מִזֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb the middle|מִתּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֗ן\rb*\rb |מִמַּצַּב֙\rb*\rb |רַגְלֵ֣י\rb* \rb where the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb were standing|הָכִ֖ין\rb*, \rb carry|וְהַעֲבַרְתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and set them down|וְהִנַּחְתֶּ֣ם\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb in the place|בַּמָּל֕וֹן\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you spend|תָּלִ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb the night|הַלָּֽיְלָה׃ס\rb*.’”
\p \v 4 \rb So Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֗עַ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb the twelve|שְׁנֵ֤ים\rb*\rb |הֶֽעָשָׂר֙\rb* \rb men|אִ֔ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had appointed|הֵכִ֖ין\rb* \rb from the Israelites|מִבְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֥ד\rb*\rb |אִישׁ־\rb*\rb |אֶחָ֖ד\rb*\rb |אִישׁ־\rb* \rb from each tribe|מִשָּֽׁבֶט׃\rb*, \v 5 \rb and said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶם֙\rb*,\rb |יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb* “\rb Cross over|עִ֠בְרוּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֧וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the middle|תּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֑ן\rb*. \rb Each|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of you is to take|וְהָרִ֨ימוּ\rb* \rb a|אַחַת֙\rb* \rb stone|אֶ֤בֶן\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb his shoulder|שִׁכְמ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb according to the number|לְמִסְפַּ֖ר\rb* \rb of the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֥י\rb*\rb |בְנֵי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*, \v 6 \rb to|לְמַ֗עַן\rb*\rb |זֹ֥את\rb* \rb serve as|תִּֽהְיֶ֛ה\rb* \rb a sign|א֖וֹת\rb* \rb among you|בְּקִרְבְּכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb In the future|מָחָר֙\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb your children|בְּנֵיכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb ask|יִשְׁאָל֨וּן\rb*, ‘\rb What|מָ֛ה\rb* \rb do these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb stones|הָאֲבָנִ֥ים\rb* \rb mean to you|לָכֶֽם׃\rb*?’ \v 7 \rb you are to tell|וַאֲמַרְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb*, ‘\rb The waters|מֵימֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּן֙\rb* \rb were cut off|נִכְרְת֜וּ\rb* \rb before|מִפְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*. \rb When it crossed|בְּעָבְרוֹ֙\rb* \rb the Jordan|בַּיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb*, \rb the|הַיַּרְדֵּ֑ן\rb* \rb waters|מֵ֣י\rb* \rb were cut off|נִכְרְת֖וּ\rb*.’ \rb Therefore these|הָאֵ֧לֶּה\rb* \rb stones|הָאֲבָנִ֨ים\rb* \rb will be|וְ֠הָיוּ\rb* \rb a memorial|לְזִכָּר֛וֹן\rb* \rb to the Israelites|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb forever|עוֹלָֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb Thus the Israelites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֘ל\rb* \rb did|וַיַּעֲשׂוּ־\rb*\rb |כֵ֣ן\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁעַ֒\rb* \rb had commanded them|צִוָּ֣ה\rb*. \rb They took up|וַיִּשְׂא֡וּ\rb* \rb twelve|שְׁתֵּֽי־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֨ה\rb* \rb stones|אֲבָנִ֜ים\rb* \rb from the middle|מִתּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֗ן\rb*, \rb one for each|לְמִסְפַּ֖ר\rb* \rb tribe|שִׁבְטֵ֣י\rb*\rb |בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb had told|דִּבֶּ֤ר\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb*; \rb and they carried|וַיַּעֲבִר֤וּם\rb* \rb them|עִמָּם֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the camp|הַמָּל֔וֹן\rb*, \rb where they set them down|וַיַּנִּח֖וּם\rb*\rb |שָֽׁם׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Joshua also|יְהוֹשֻׁעַ֮\rb* \rb set up|הֵקִ֣ים\rb* \rb twelve|וּשְׁתֵּ֧ים\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֣ה\rb* \rb stones|אֲבָנִ֗ים\rb* \rb in the middle|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּן֒\rb*,\f + \fr 4:9 \ft Some translators \fqa And Joshua set up the twelve stones that had been in the middle of the Jordan\f* \rb in the place|תַּ֗חַת\rb* \rb where the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb who carried|נֹשְׂאֵ֖י\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|הַבְּרִ֑ית\rb* \rb stood|מַצַּב֙\rb*\rb |רַגְלֵ֣י\rb*. \rb And the stones are|וַיִּ֣הְיוּ\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Now the priests|וְהַכֹּהֲנִ֞ים\rb* \rb who carried|נֹשְׂאֵ֣י\rb* \rb the ark|הָאָר֗וֹן\rb* \rb remained standing|עֹמְדִים֮\rb* \rb in the middle|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּן֒\rb* \rb until|עַ֣ד\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb had completed|תֹּ֣ם\rb* \rb everything|כָּֽל־\rb*\rb |הַ֠דָּבָר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֨ה\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb to tell|לְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb them|אֶל־\rb*, \rb just as|כְּכֹ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had directed|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֑עַ\rb*. \rb The people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb hurried|וַיְמַהֲר֥וּ\rb* \rb across|וַֽיַּעֲבֹֽרוּ׃\rb*, \v 11 \rb |וַיְהִ֛י\rb* \rb and after|כַּֽאֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb everyone|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb had finished|תַּ֥ם\rb* \rb crossing|לַֽעֲב֑וֹר\rb*, \rb the priests|וְהַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb with the ark|אֲרוֹן־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb crossed|וַיַּעֲבֹ֧ר\rb* \rb in the sight of|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the people|הָעָֽם׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb The Reubenites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |רְאוּבֵ֨ן\rb*, \rb the Gadites|וּבְנֵי־\rb*\rb |גָ֜ד\rb*, \rb and the half-tribe|וַחֲצִ֨י\rb*\rb |שֵׁ֤בֶט\rb* \rb of Manasseh|הַֽמְנַשֶּׁה֙\rb* \rb crossed over|וַ֠יַּעַבְרוּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb armed for battle|חֲמֻשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb* \rb had instructed them|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*. \v 13 \rb About 40,000|כְּאַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb troops armed|חֲלוּצֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הַצָּבָ֑א\rb* \rb for battle|לַמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb crossed over|עָבְר֞וּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb into|אֶ֖ל\rb* \rb the plains|עַֽרְב֥וֹת\rb* \rb of Jericho|יְרִיחֽוֹ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb On that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb exalted|גִּדַּ֤ל\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and they revered|וַיִּֽרְא֣וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of his life|חַיָּֽיו׃פ\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb they had revered|יָרְא֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb said to|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 16 “\rb Command|צַוֵּה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb who carry|נֹשְׂאֵ֖י\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the Testimony|הָעֵד֑וּת\rb*\f + \fr 4:16 \ft That is, \fqa the ark of the covenant\f* \rb to come up|וְיַעֲל֖וּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּֽן׃\rb*.”
\p \v 17 \rb So Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb commanded|וַיְצַ֣ו\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* “\rb Come up|עֲל֖וּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּֽן׃\rb*.”
\p \v 18 \rb |וַ֠יְהִי\rb* \rb When the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֜ים\rb* \rb carrying|נֹשְׂאֵ֨י\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֤וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb came up|בַּעֲלוֹת\rb* \rb out|מִתּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb and their|הַכֹּהֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb feet|כַּפּוֹת֙\rb*\rb |רַגְלֵ֣י\rb* \rb touched|נִתְּק֗וּ\rb* \rb the dry land|הֶחָרָבָ֑ה\rb*, \rb the waters|מֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּן֙\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּשֻׁ֤בוּ\rb* \rb to their course|לִמְקוֹמָ֔ם\rb* \rb and overflowed|וַיֵּלְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the banks|גְּדוֹתָֽיו׃\rb* \rb as before|כִתְמוֹל־\rb*\rb |שִׁלְשׁ֖וֹם\rb*.
\s1 The Camp at Gilgal
\p \v 19 \rb On the tenth|בֶּעָשׂ֖וֹר\rb* \rb day of the first|הָרִאשׁ֑וֹן\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb the people|וְהָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb went up|עָלוּ֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb and camped|וַֽיַּחֲנוּ֙\rb* \rb at Gilgal|בַּגִּלְגָּ֔ל\rb* \rb on the eastern|מִזְרַ֥ח\rb* \rb border|בִּקְצֵ֖ה\rb* \rb of Jericho|יְרִיחֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb And|וְאֵת֩\rb* \rb there at Gilgal|בַּגִּלְגָּֽל׃\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb* \rb set up|הֵקִ֥ים\rb* \rb the|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb twelve|שְׁתֵּ֨ים\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֤ה\rb* \rb stones|הָֽאֲבָנִים֙\rb* \rb they had taken|לָקְח֖וּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֑ן\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb Then Joshua said|וַיֹּ֛אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* “\rb In the future|מָחָר֙\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb when|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb your children|בְּנֵיכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb ask|יִשְׁאָל֨וּן\rb* \rb their fathers|אֲבוֹתָ֣ם\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* ‘\rb What|מָ֖ה\rb* \rb is the meaning of these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb stones|הָאֲבָנִ֥ים\rb*?’ \v 22 \rb you are to tell|וְהוֹדַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb them|בְּנֵיכֶ֣ם\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* ‘\rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb crossed|עָבַ֣ר\rb* \rb the|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb on dry ground|בַּיַּבָּשָׁה֙\rb*.’ \v 23 \rb For|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֜ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb dried up|הוֹבִישׁ֩\rb* \rb the waters|מֵ֧י\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֛ן\rb* \rb before you|מִפְּנֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb until|עַֽד־\rb* \rb you had crossed over|עָבְרְכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He|יְהוָ֨ה\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֧ם\rb* \rb did|עָשָׂה֩\rb* \rb to the Red|ס֛וּף\rb* \rb Sea|לְיַם־\rb*,\f + \fr 4:23 \ft Or \fqa the Sea of Reeds\f* \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb He dried up|הוֹבִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb before us|מִפָּנֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb we had crossed over|עָבְרֵֽנוּ׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb He did this so that|לְ֠מַעַן\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the peoples|עַמֵּ֤י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb may know|דַּ֜עַת\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the hand|יַ֣ד\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb is mighty|חֲזָקָ֖ה\rb*,\rb |הִ֑יא\rb* \rb and so that|לְמַ֧עַן\rb* \rb you may always|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִֽים׃ס\rb* \rb fear|יְרָאתֶ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*.”
\c 5
\s1 The Circumcision and Passover at Gilgal
\p \v 1 \rb Now|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb when all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Amorite|הָאֱמֹרִ֡י\rb* \rb kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb*\rb |בְּעֵ֨בֶר\rb* \rb west of|יָ֗מָּה\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֜ן\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the Canaanite|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִי֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb kings|מַלְכֵ֤י\rb* \rb along|עַל־\rb* \rb the coast|הַיָּ֔ם\rb*\f + \fr 5:1 \ft That is, along the Mediterranean coast; literally \fqa along the sea\f*\rb |אֵ֠ת\rb* \rb heard|כִשְׁמֹ֣עַ\rb* \rb how|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had dried up|הוֹבִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb the waters|מֵ֧י\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֛ן\rb* \rb before|מִפְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb they had crossed over|עָבְרָנוּ\rb*,\f + \fr 5:1 \ft Or \fqa until we had crossed over\f* \rb their hearts|לְבָבָ֗ם\rb* \rb melted|וַיִּמַּ֣ס\rb* \rb and their spirits|ר֔וּחַ\rb* \rb failed|וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |הָ֨יָה\rb*\rb |עוֹד֙\rb* \rb for fear of|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb At that|הַהִ֗יא\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb*, “\rb Make|עֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \rb flint|צֻרִ֑ים\rb* \rb knives|חַֽרְב֣וֹת\rb* \rb and circumcise|מֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb once again|וְשׁ֛וּב\rb*\rb |שֵׁנִֽית׃\rb*.\f + \fr 5:2 \ft Literally \fqa again the second time\f*” \v 3 \rb So Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb* \rb made|וַיַּעַשׂ־\rb* \rb flint|צֻרִ֑ים\rb* \rb knives|חַֽרְב֣וֹת\rb* \rb and circumcised|וַיָּ֙מָל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb Gibeath-haaraloth|גִּבְעַ֖ת\rb*\rb |הָעֲרָלֽוֹת׃\rb*.\f + \fr 5:3 \fqa Gibeath-haaraloth \ft means \fqa the hill of the foreskins\ft .\f*
\p \v 4 \rb Now this|וְזֶ֥ה\rb* \rb is why|הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֑עַ\rb* \rb circumcised them|מָ֣ל\rb*: \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb those|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb who came out|הַיֹּצֵא֩\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֨יִם\rb*—\rb |הַזְּכָרִ֜ים\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of war|הַמִּלְחָמָ֗ה\rb*— \rb had died|מֵ֤תוּ\rb* \rb on the journey|בַּדֶּ֔רֶךְ\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַמִּדְבָּר֙\rb* \rb after they had left|בְּצֵאתָ֖ם\rb* \rb Egypt|מִמִּצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb Though|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb who had come out|הַיֹּֽצְאִ֑ים\rb* \rb were|הָי֔וּ\rb* \rb circumcised|מֻלִ֣ים\rb*, \rb none|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb of those|הָ֠עָם\rb* \rb born|הַיִּלֹּדִ֨ים\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֥ר\rb* \rb on the journey|בַּדֶּ֛רֶךְ\rb*\rb |בְּצֵאתָ֥ם\rb* \rb from Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb had been circumcised|מָֽלוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb For|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֮\rb* \rb had wandered|הָלְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּר֒\rb* \rb forty|אַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֗ה\rb*, \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the nation’s|הַגּ֜וֹי\rb* \rb men|אַנְשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb of war|הַמִּלְחָמָה֙\rb* \rb who had come out|הַיֹּצְאִ֣ים\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb had died|תֹּ֨ם\rb*, \rb since|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb obey|שָׁמְע֖וּ\rb*\rb |בְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb So|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb vowed|נִשְׁבַּ֤ע\rb* \rb never|לְבִלְתִּ֞י\rb* \rb to let them see|הַרְאוֹתָ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb He|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb had sworn|נִשְׁבַּ֨ע\rb* \rb to their fathers|לַֽאֲבוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb to give|לָ֣תֶת\rb* \rb us|לָ֔נוּ\rb*, \rb a land|אֶ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb flowing|זָבַ֥ת\rb* \rb with milk|חָלָ֖ב\rb* \rb and honey|וּדְבָֽשׁ׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb And|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb He raised up|הֵקִ֣ים\rb* \rb their sons|בְּנֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb in their place|תַּחְתָּ֔ם\rb*, \rb and these were the ones|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֑עַ\rb* \rb circumcised|מָ֣ל\rb*. \rb Until this time they were|הָי֔וּ\rb*\rb |כִּ֛י\rb* \rb still uncircumcised|עֲרֵלִ֣ים\rb*, \rb since|כִּי־\rb* \rb they had not|לֹא־\rb* \rb been circumcised|מָ֥לוּ\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb along the way|בַּדָּֽרֶךְ׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb And|וַיְהִ֛י\rb* \rb after|כַּאֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |תַּ֥מּוּ\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb the nation|הַגּ֖וֹי\rb* \rb had been circumcised|לְהִמּ֑וֹל\rb*, \rb they stayed|וַיֵּשְׁב֥וּ\rb* \rb there|תַחְתָּ֛ם\rb* \rb in the camp|בַּֽמַּחֲנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb until|עַ֥ד\rb* \rb they were healed|חֲיוֹתָֽם׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb*, “\rb Today|הַיּ֗וֹם\rb* \rb I have rolled away|גַּלּ֛וֹתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the reproach|חֶרְפַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb from you|מֵעֲלֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*.” \rb So that|הַהוּא֙\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֤וֹם\rb* \rb has been called|וַיִּקְרָ֞א\rb*\rb |שֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb Gilgal|גִּלְגָּ֔ל\rb*\f + \fr 5:9 \fqa Gilgal \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa roll\ft .\f* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb On the evening|בָּעֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb of the fourteenth|בְּאַרְבָּעָה֩\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֨ר\rb* \rb day|י֥וֹם\rb* \rb of the month|לַחֹ֛דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb while the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb were camped|וַיַּחֲנ֥וּ\rb* \rb at Gilgal|בַּגִּלְגָּ֑ל\rb* \rb on the plains|בְּעַֽרְב֥וֹת\rb* \rb of Jericho|יְרִיחֽוֹ׃\rb*, \rb they kept|וַיַּעֲשׂ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Passover|הַפֶּ֡סַח\rb*. \v 11 \rb The day after|מִמָּֽחֳרַ֥ת\rb* \rb the Passover|הַפֶּ֖סַח\rb*, \rb on that very|בְּעֶ֖צֶם\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*,\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb they ate|וַיֹּ֨אכְל֜וּ\rb* \rb unleavened bread|מַצּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb and roasted grain|וְקָל֑וּי\rb* \rb from the produce|מֵעֲב֥וּר\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֛רֶץ\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb And the day|מִֽמָּחֳרָ֗ת\rb* \rb after they had eaten|בְּאָכְלָם֙\rb* \rb from the produce|מֵעֲב֣וּר\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb the manna|הַמָּ֜ן\rb* \rb ceased|וַיִּשְׁבֹּ֨ת\rb*. \rb There was|הָ֥יָה\rb* \rb no|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb more|ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb manna|מָ֑ן\rb* \rb for the Israelites|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb so that|הַהִֽיא׃ס\rb* \rb year|בַּשָּׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb they began to eat|וַיֹּאכְל֗וּ\rb* \rb the crops|מִתְּבוּאַת֙\rb* \rb of the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנַ֔עַן\rb*.
\s1 The Commander of the LORD’s Army
\p \v 13 \rb Now when Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁעַ֮\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֗י\rb*\rb |בִּֽהְי֣וֹת\rb* \rb near Jericho|בִּירִיחוֹ֒\rb*, \rb he looked up|וַיִּשָּׂ֤א\rb*\rb |עֵינָיו֙\rb* \rb and saw|וַיַּ֔רְא\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb a man|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb standing|עֹמֵ֣ד\rb* \rb in front of him|לְנֶגְדּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb with a drawn|שְׁלוּפָ֖ה\rb* \rb sword|וְחַרְבּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb in His hand|בְּיָד֑וֹ\rb*. \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֤עַ\rb* \rb approached|וַיֵּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb Him|אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb and asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Are You|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb for us|הֲלָ֥נוּ\rb* \rb or|אִם־\rb* \rb for our enemies|לְצָרֵֽינוּ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 14 “\rb Neither|לֹ֗א\rb*,”\rb |כִּ֛י\rb* \rb He replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר׀\rb*. “\rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb have now|עַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb come|בָ֑אתִי\rb* \rb as Commander|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb army|צְבָֽא־\rb*.”
\p \rb Then Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֨עַ\rb* \rb fell|וַיִּפֹּל֩\rb* \rb facedown|אֶל־\rb*\rb |פָּנָ֥יו\rb*\rb |אַ֙רְצָה֙\rb* \rb in reverence|וַיִּשְׁתָּ֔חוּ\rb*\f + \fr 5:14 \ft Or \fqa and paid homage \ft or \fqa and worshiped\f* \rb and asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb Him|ל֔וֹ\rb*, “\rb What|מָ֥ה\rb* \rb does my Lord|אֲדֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb have to say|מְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb His servant|עַבְדּֽוֹ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 15 \rb The Commander|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of the LORD’s|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb army|צְבָ֨א\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |יְהוֹשֻׁ֗עַ\rb*, “\rb Take off|שַׁל־\rb* \rb your sandals|נַֽעַלְךָ֙\rb*\rb |מֵעַ֣ל\rb*\rb |רַגְלֶ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֗וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb are standing|עֹמֵ֥ד\rb*\rb |עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb is holy|קֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |ה֑וּא\rb*.”
\p \rb And Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb so|כֵּֽן׃\rb*.
\c 6
\s1 The Walls of Jericho
\p \v 1 \rb Now Jericho|וִֽירִיחוֹ֙\rb* \rb was tightly shut up|סֹגֶ֣רֶת\rb*\rb |וּמְסֻגֶּ֔רֶת\rb* \rb because of|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb No one|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb went out|יוֹצֵ֖א\rb* \rb and no one|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb came in|בָּֽא׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb*, “\rb Behold|רְאֵה֙\rb*, \rb I have delivered|נָתַ֣תִּי\rb* \rb Jericho|יְרִיח֖וֹ\rb* \rb into your hand|בְיָֽדְךָ֔\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*, \rb along with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb its king|מַלְכָּ֑הּ\rb* \rb and its mighty men|גִּבּוֹרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of valor|הֶחָֽיִל׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb March around|וְסַבֹּתֶ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֗יר\rb* \rb with all|כֹּ֚ל\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of war|הַמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb*, \rb circling|הַקֵּ֥יף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֑ת\rb* \rb time|פַּ֣עַם\rb*. \rb Do|תַעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb this|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb for six|שֵׁ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִֽים׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb Have seven|וְשִׁבְעָ֣ה\rb* \rb priests|כֹהֲנִ֡ים\rb* \rb carry|יִשְׂאוּ֩\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעָ֨ה\rb*\rb |שׁוֹפְר֤וֹת\rb* \rb rams’ horns|הַיּֽוֹבְלִים֙\rb* \rb in front|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the ark|הָאָר֔וֹן\rb*. \rb Then on the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֔י\rb* \rb day|וּבַיּוֹם֙\rb*, \rb march around|תָּסֹ֥בּוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִ֑ים\rb*, \rb while the priests|וְהַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb blow|יִתְקְע֖וּ\rb* \rb the horns|בַּשּׁוֹפָרֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb And when|וְהָיָ֞ה\rb* \rb there is a long blast|בִּמְשֹׁ֣ךְ׀\rb* \rb of the ram’s|הַיּוֹבֵ֗ל\rb* \rb horn|בְּקֶ֣רֶן\rb* \rb and you hear|בְּשָׁמְעֲכֶם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its|הַשּׁוֹפָ֔ר\rb* \rb sound|ק֣וֹל\rb*, \rb have all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb give a mighty|גְדוֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb shout|יָרִ֥יעוּ\rb*\rb |תְּרוּעָ֣ה\rb*. \rb Then the wall|חוֹמַ֤ת\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִיר֙\rb*\rb |תַּחְתֶּ֔יהָ\rb* \rb will collapse|וְנָ֨פְלָ֜ה\rb*\f + \fr 6:5 \ft Or \fqa fall under itself \ft or \fqa fall flat\ft ; similarly in verse 20\f* \rb and all your people|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb will charge|וְעָל֥וּ\rb* \rb straight into the city|נֶגְדּֽוֹ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 6:5 \ft Literally \fqa and the people will go up, every man straight ahead\ft ; similarly in verse 20\f*”
\p \v 6 \rb So Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֤עַ\rb* \rb son|בִּן־\rb* \rb of Nun|נוּן֙\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֞א\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*, “\rb Take up|שְׂא֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|הַבְּרִ֑ית\rb* \rb and have seven|וְשִׁבְעָ֣ה\rb* \rb priests|כֹֽהֲנִ֗ים\rb* \rb carry|יִשְׂאוּ֙\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעָ֤ה\rb*\rb |שֽׁוֹפְרוֹת֙\rb* \rb rams’ horns|יוֹבְלִ֔ים\rb* \rb in front|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the ark|אֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb And he told|וַיֹּאמְרוּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb*, “\rb Advance|עִבְר֖וּ\rb* \rb and march around|וְסֹ֣בּוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb*, \rb with the armed troops|וְהֶ֣חָל֔וּץ\rb* \rb going|יַעֲבֹ֕ר\rb* \rb ahead of|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb After Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁעַ֮\rb* \rb had spoken|כֶּאֱמֹ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֒\rb*, \rb seven|וְשִׁבְעָ֣ה\rb* \rb priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֡ים\rb* \rb carrying|נֹשְׂאִים֩\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעָ֨ה\rb*\rb |שׁוֹפְר֤וֹת\rb* \rb rams’ horns|הַיּֽוֹבְלִים֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb advanced|עָבְר֕וּ\rb* \rb and blew|וְתָקְע֖וּ\rb* \rb the horns|בַּשּֽׁוֹפָר֑וֹת\rb*, \rb and the ark|וַֽאֲרוֹן֙\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb followed|הֹלֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb them|אַחֲרֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb While the horns|הַשּֽׁוֹפָר֑וֹת\rb* \rb continued to sound|תָּקְעוּ\rb*, \rb the armed troops|וְהֶחָל֣וּץ\rb* \rb marched|הֹלֵ֔ךְ\rb* \rb ahead|לִפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb of the priests|הַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb*\rb |הָל֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb who blew|וְתָק֥וֹעַ\rb* \rb the horns|בַּשּׁוֹפָרֽוֹת׃\rb*, \rb and the rear guard|וְהַֽמְאַסֵּ֗ף\rb* \rb followed|הֹלֵךְ֙\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb the ark|הָאָר֔וֹן\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb But Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֜עַ\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֨ה\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֩\rb*: “\rb Do not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb give a battle cry|תָרִ֙יעוּ֙\rb* \rb or let your voice|קוֹלְכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְלֹא־\rb* \rb be heard|תַשְׁמִ֣יעוּ\rb*;\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb do not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb let one word|דָּבָ֑ר\rb* \rb come out|יֵצֵ֥א\rb* \rb of your mouth|מִפִּיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb until|עַ֠ד\rb* \rb the day|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb I tell|אָמְרִ֧י\rb* \rb you|אֲלֵיכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb to shout|הָרִ֖יעוּ\rb*. \rb Then you are to shout|וַהֲרִיעֹתֶֽם׃\rb*!” \v 11 \rb So he had the ark|אֲרוֹן־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb carried around|וַיַּסֵּ֤ב\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb*, \rb circling|הַקֵּ֖ף\rb* \rb it once|פַּ֣עַם\rb*\rb |אֶחָ֑ת\rb*. \rb And the people returned|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb to the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֔ה\rb* \rb and spent the night there|וַיָּלִ֖ינוּ\rb*\rb |בַּֽמַּחֲנֶֽה׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb* \rb got up early|וַיַּשְׁכֵּ֥ם\rb* \rb the next morning|בַּבֹּ֑קֶר\rb*, \rb and the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּשְׂא֥וּ\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb And the seven|וְשִׁבְעָ֣ה\rb* \rb priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֡ים\rb* \rb carrying|נֹשְׂאִים֩\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעָ֨ה\rb*\rb |שׁוֹפְר֜וֹת\rb* \rb rams’ horns|הַיֹּבְלִ֗ים\rb* \rb kept marching|הֹלְכִ֣ים\rb*\rb |הָל֔וֹךְ\rb* \rb ahead|לִפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb of the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and blowing|וְתָקְע֖וּ\rb* \rb the horns|בַּשּׁוֹפָר֑וֹת\rb*. \rb The armed troops|וְהֶחָלוּץ֙\rb* \rb went|הֹלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb in front of them|לִפְנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and the rear guard|וְהַֽמְאַסֵּ֗ף\rb* \rb followed|הֹלֵךְ֙\rb*\rb |אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb while the horns|בַּשּׁוֹפָרֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb kept|הוֹלֵךְ\rb* \rb sounding|וְתָק֥וֹעַ\rb*. \v 14 \rb So on the second|הַשֵּׁנִי֙\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֤וֹם\rb* \rb they marched around|וַיָּסֹ֨בּוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֜יר\rb* \rb once|פַּ֣עַם\rb*\rb |אַחַ֔ת\rb* \rb and returned|וַיָּשֻׁ֖בוּ\rb* \rb to the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֑ה\rb*. \rb They did|עָשׂ֖וּ\rb* \rb this|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb for six|שֵׁ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Then|וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb on the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֗י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb they got up|וַיַּשְׁכִּ֙מוּ֙\rb* \rb at dawn|כַּעֲל֣וֹת\rb*\rb |הַשַּׁ֔חַר\rb* \rb and marched around|וַיָּסֹ֧בּוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֛יר\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb in the same|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb manner|כַּמִּשְׁפָּ֥ט\rb*. \rb That|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb was the only|רַ֚ק\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb they circled|סָבְב֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִֽים׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb |וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb After the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֔ית\rb* \rb time around|בַּפַּ֣עַם\rb*, \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb blew|תָּקְע֥וּ\rb* \rb the horns|בַּשּׁוֹפָר֑וֹת\rb*, \rb and Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֤עַ\rb* \rb commanded|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֙\rb*, “\rb Shout|הָרִ֔יעוּ\rb*! \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has given|נָתַ֧ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb the city|הָעִֽיר׃\rb*! \v 17 \rb Now the city|הָעִ֥יר\rb* \rb and everything|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in it|בָּ֖הּ\rb* \rb must be|וְהָיְתָ֨ה\rb* \rb devoted|חֵ֛רֶם\rb* \rb to the LORD for destruction|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb*.\f + \fr 6:17 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering; also in verses 18 and 21.\f*\rb |הִ֥יא\rb* \rb Only|רַק֩\rb* \rb Rahab|רָחָ֨ב\rb* \rb the prostitute|הַזּוֹנָ֜ה\rb* \rb and all those|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb with her|אִתָּ֣הּ\rb* \rb in her house|בַּבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb will live|תִּֽחְיֶ֗ה\rb*,\rb |הִ֚יא\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb she hid|הֶחְבְּאַ֔תָה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the spies|הַמַּלְאָכִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb we sent|שָׁלָֽחְנוּ׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb But|וְרַק־\rb*\rb |אַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb keep away|שִׁמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the things devoted to destruction|הַחֵ֔רֶם\rb*, \rb lest|פֶּֽן־\rb* \rb you yourself be set apart for destruction|תַּחֲרִ֖ימוּ\rb*. \rb If you take|וּלְקַחְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb any of|מִן־\rb* \rb these|הַחֵ֑רֶם\rb*, \rb you will set|וְשַׂמְתֶּ֞ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb apart the camp|מַחֲנֵ֤ה\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb for destruction|לְחֵ֔רֶם\rb* \rb and bring disaster upon it|וַעֲכַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb*.\rb |אוֹתֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 19 \rb For all|וְכֹ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the silver|כֶּ֣סֶף\rb* \rb and gold|וְזָהָ֗ב\rb* \rb and all the articles|וּכְלֵ֤י\rb* \rb of bronze|נְחֹ֙שֶׁת֙\rb* \rb and iron|וּבַרְזֶ֔ל\rb* \rb are holy|קֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb*; \rb they must go into|יָבֽוֹא׃\rb* \rb His|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb treasury|אוֹצַ֥ר\rb*.”
\p \v 20 \rb So when the rams’ horns|בַּשֹּֽׁפָר֑וֹת\rb*\rb |וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb sounded|וַֽיִּתְקְע֖וּ\rb*, \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb shouted|וַיָּ֣רַע\rb*. \rb When they|הָעָ֜ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb heard|כִשְׁמֹ֨עַ\rb* \rb the blast|ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of the horn|הַשּׁוֹפָ֗ר\rb*, \rb the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb gave a great|גְדוֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb shout|וַיָּרִ֤יעוּ\rb*\rb |תְּרוּעָ֣ה\rb*, \rb and the wall|הַֽחוֹמָ֜ה\rb* \rb collapsed|וַתִּפֹּ֨ל\rb*\rb |תַּחְתֶּ֗יהָ\rb*. \rb Then all the people|הָעָ֤ם\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb charged|וַיַּ֨עַל\rb* \rb straight|נֶגְדּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb into the city|הָעִ֙ירָה֙\rb* \rb and captured|וַֽיִּלְכְּד֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb it|הָעִֽיר׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb With the edge|לְפִי־\rb* \rb of the sword|חָֽרֶב׃\rb* \rb they devoted to destruction|וַֽיַּחֲרִ֙ימוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in the city|בָּעִ֔יר\rb*— \rb man|מֵאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb and woman|אִשָּׁ֔ה\rb*, \rb young|מִנַּ֖עַר\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb*\rb |וְעַד־\rb* \rb old|זָקֵ֑ן\rb*,\rb |וְעַ֨ד\rb* \rb oxen|שׁ֥וֹר\rb*, \rb sheep|וָשֶׂ֛ה\rb*, \rb and donkeys|וַחֲמ֖וֹר\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb Meanwhile, Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb* \rb told|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb the two|וְלִשְׁנַ֨יִם\rb* \rb men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֜ים\rb* \rb who had spied out|הַֽמְרַגְּלִ֤ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb*, “\rb Go into|בֹּ֖אוּ\rb* \rb the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the prostitute|הַזּוֹנָ֑ה\rb* \rb and bring out|וְהוֹצִ֨יאוּ\rb* \rb the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |מִשָּׁ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הָֽאִשָּׁה֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who are|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb with her|לָ֔הּ\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you promised|נִשְׁבַּעְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb her|לָֽהּ׃\rb*.” \v 23 \rb So the young|הַנְּעָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb spies|הַֽמְרַגְּלִ֗ים\rb* \rb went in|וַיָּבֹ֜אוּ\rb* \rb and brought out|וַיֹּצִ֡יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Rahab|רָ֠חָב\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb her father|אָבִ֨יהָ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb mother|אִמָּ֤הּ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb brothers|אַחֶ֙יהָ֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who belonged|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb to her|לָ֔הּ\rb*.\rb |וְאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb They brought out|הוֹצִ֑יאוּ\rb* \rb her whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb family|מִשְׁפְּחוֹתֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb and settled them|וַיַּ֨נִּיח֔וּם\rb* \rb outside|מִח֖וּץ\rb* \rb the camp|לְמַחֲנֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb Then the Israelites burned up|שָׂרְפ֥וּ\rb*\rb |בָאֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb the city|וְהָעִ֛יר\rb* \rb and everything|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in it|בָּ֑הּ\rb*. \rb However|רַ֣ק׀\rb*, \rb they put|נָתְנ֖וּ\rb* \rb the silver|הַכֶּ֣סֶף\rb* \rb and gold|וְהַזָּהָ֗ב\rb* \rb and articles|וּכְלֵ֤י\rb* \rb of bronze|הַנְּחֹ֙שֶׁת֙\rb* \rb and iron|וְהַבַּרְזֶ֔ל\rb* \rb into the treasury|אוֹצַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the LORD’s|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb house|בֵּית־\rb*. \v 25 \rb And|וְֽאֶת־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb* \rb spared|הֶחֱיָ֣ה\rb* \rb Rahab|רָחָ֣ב\rb* \rb the prostitute|הַ֠זּוֹנָה\rb*, \rb with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb her father’s|אָבִ֤יהָ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb household|בֵּ֨ית\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who belonged|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb to her|לָהּ֙\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb she hid|הֶחְבִּ֙יאָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the men|הַמַּלְאָכִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb* \rb had sent|שָׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb to spy out|לְרַגֵּ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jericho|יְרִיחֽוֹ׃פ\rb*. \rb So she has lived|וַתֵּ֙שֶׁב֙\rb* \rb among|בְּקֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*.
