\c 7
\s1 The Defeat at Ai
\p \v 1 \rb The Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*, \rb however|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb*, \rb acted|וַיִּמְעֲל֧וּ\rb* \rb unfaithfully|מַ֖עַל\rb* \rb regarding the things devoted to destruction|בַּחֵ֑רֶם\rb*.\f + \fr 7:1 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering; also in verses 11, 12, 13, and 15.\f* \rb Achan|עָכָ֣ן\rb*\f + \fr 7:1 \fqa Achan \ft means \fqa troubler\ft ; also called \fqa Achar\ft in \ref 1 Chronicles 2:7|1CH 2:7\ref*.\f* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Carmi|כַּרְמִי֩\rb*, \rb the son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Zabdi|זַבְדִּ֨י\rb*,\f + \fr 7:1 \fqa Zabdi \ft is a variant of \fqa Zimri\ft ; also in verses 17 and 18; see LXX and \ref 1 Chronicles 2:6|1CH 2:6\ref*.\f* \rb the son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Zerah|זֶ֜רַח\rb*, \rb of the tribe|לְמַטֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb*, \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֡ח\rb* \rb some of|מִן־\rb* \rb what was set apart|הַחֵ֔רֶם\rb*. \rb So the anger|אַ֥ף\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb burned|וַיִּֽחַר־\rb* \rb against the Israelites|בִּבְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb Meanwhile, Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֨עַ\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַח֩\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֜ים\rb* \rb from Jericho|מִֽירִיח֗וֹ\rb* \rb to Ai|הָעַ֞י\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb is near|עִם־\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb Beth-aven|אָ֙וֶן֙\rb* \rb to the east|מִקֶּ֣דֶם\rb*\rb |לְבֵֽית־\rb* \rb of Bethel|אֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb and told them|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*,\rb |אֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* “\rb Go up|עֲל֖וּ\rb* \rb and spy out|וְרַגְּל֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*.” \rb So the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb went up|וַֽיַּעֲלוּ֙\rb* \rb and spied out|וַֽיְרַגְּל֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Ai|הָעָֽי׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb On returning|וַיָּשֻׁ֣בוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֗עַ\rb*, \rb they reported|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָיו֮\rb*, “\rb There is no need|אַל־\rb*\rb |יַ֣עַל\rb* \rb to send all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֒\rb*; \rb two|כְּאַלְפַּ֣יִם\rb*\rb |אִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb or|א֚וֹ\rb* \rb three|כִּשְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִ֣ים\rb* \rb men are enough|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb to go up|יַעֲל֖וּ\rb* \rb and attack|וְיַכּ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Ai|הָעָ֑י\rb*. \rb Since|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the people of Ai|הֵֽמָּה׃\rb* \rb are so few|מְעַ֖ט\rb*, \rb you need not|אַל־\rb* \rb wear out|תְּיַגַּע־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb our people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֙מָּה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb So about three|כִּשְׁלֹ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb* \rb men|אִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּעֲל֤וּ\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb*\rb |הָעָם֙\rb*\rb |שָׁ֔מָּה\rb*, \rb but they fled|וַיָּנֻ֕סוּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of Ai|הָעָֽי׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb And the men|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb of Ai|הָעַ֗י\rb* \rb struck down|וַיַּכּ֨וּ\rb*\rb |מֵהֶ֜ם\rb*\rb |אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb about thirty-six of them|כִּשְׁלֹשִׁ֤ים\rb*,\rb |וְשִׁשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb chasing them|וַֽיִּרְדְּפ֞וּם\rb* \rb from|לִפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb the gate|הַשַּׁ֙עַר֙\rb* \rb as far as|עַד־\rb* \rb the quarries|הַשְּׁבָרִ֔ים\rb*\f + \fr 7:5 \ft Or \fqa as far as Shebarim\f* \rb and striking them down|וַיַּכּ֖וּם\rb* \rb on the slopes|בַּמּוֹרָ֑ד\rb*. \rb So the hearts|לְבַב־\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb melted|וַיִּמַּ֥ס\rb* \rb and became|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb like water|לְמָֽיִם׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Then Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֜עַ\rb* \rb tore|וַיִּקְרַ֨ע\rb* \rb his clothes|שִׂמְלֹתָ֗יו\rb* \rb and fell|וַיִּפֹּל֩\rb* \rb facedown|לִפְנֵ֨י\rb*\rb |אַ֜רְצָה\rb* \rb before|פָּנָ֨יו\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֤וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעֶ֔רֶב\rb*,\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb as did the elders|וְזִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*; \rb and they all sprinkled|וַיַּעֲל֥וּ\rb* \rb dust|עָפָ֖ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb their heads|רֹאשָֽׁם׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 “\rb O|אֲהָ֣הּ׀\rb*, \rb Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֗ה\rb*,” \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֜עַ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*, “\rb why|לָ֠מָה\rb* \rb did You ever bring|הֵעֲבַ֨רְתָּ\rb*\rb |הַעֲבִ֜יר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֤ם\rb* \rb across the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb to deliver|לָתֵ֥ת\rb* \rb us|אֹתָ֛נוּ\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֥ד\rb* \rb of the Amorites|הָאֱמֹרִ֖י\rb* \rb to be destroyed|לְהַאֲבִידֵ֑נוּ\rb*? \rb If only|וְלוּ֙\rb* \rb we had been content|הוֹאַ֣לְנוּ\rb* \rb to stay|וַנֵּ֔שֶׁב\rb* \rb on the other side|בְּעֵ֖בֶר\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּֽן׃\rb*! \v 8 \rb O|בִּ֖י\rb* \rb Lord|אֲדֹנָ֑י\rb*, \rb what|מָ֣ה\rb* \rb can I say|אֹמַ֔ר\rb*, \rb now that|אַ֠חֲרֵי\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb has turned|הָפַ֧ךְ\rb* \rb its back|עֹ֖רֶף\rb* \rb and run from|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb its enemies|אֹיְבָֽיו׃\rb*? \v 9 \rb When the Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb and all|וְכֹל֙\rb* \rb who live|יֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb in the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb hear about this|וְיִשְׁמְע֣וּ\rb*, \rb they will surround|וְנָסַ֣בּוּ\rb* \rb us|עָלֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb and wipe out|וְהִכְרִ֥יתוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb our name|שְׁמֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*. \rb Then what|וּמַֽה־\rb* \rb will You do|תַּעֲשֵׂ֖ה\rb* \rb for Your great|הַגָּדֽוֹל׃ס\rb* \rb name|לְשִׁמְךָ֥\rb*?”
\p \v 10 \rb But the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb*, “\rb Stand up|קֻ֣ם\rb*! \rb Why|לָ֣מָּה\rb*\rb |זֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb have you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb fallen|נֹפֵ֥ל\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb your face|פָּנֶֽיךָ׃\rb*? \v 11 \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb has sinned|חָטָא֙\rb*;\rb |וְגַם֙\rb* \rb they have transgressed|עָבְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My covenant|בְּרִיתִ֔י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I commanded|צִוִּ֖יתִי\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and they|וְגַ֤ם\rb* \rb have taken|לָֽקְחוּ֙\rb* \rb some of|מִן־\rb* \rb what was devoted to destruction|הַחֵ֔רֶם\rb*. \rb Indeed|וְגַ֤ם\rb*, \rb they have stolen|גָּֽנְבוּ֙\rb* \rb and|וְגַ֣ם\rb* \rb lied|כִּֽחֲשׁ֔וּ\rb*, \rb and|וְגַ֖ם\rb* \rb they have put these things|שָׂ֥מוּ\rb* \rb with their own possessions|בִכְלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb This is why the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb cannot|וְלֹ֨א\rb*\rb |יֻכְל֜וּ\rb* \rb stand|לָקוּם֙\rb* \rb against|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb their enemies|אֹיְבֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*. \rb They will turn|יִפְנוּ֙\rb* \rb their backs|עֹ֗רֶף\rb* \rb and run from|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb their enemies|אֹֽיְבֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they themselves have been|הָי֖וּ\rb* \rb set apart for destruction|לְחֵ֑רֶם\rb*. \rb I will no|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb longer|אוֹסִיף֙\rb* \rb be|לִֽהְי֣וֹת\rb* \rb with|עִמָּכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb you unless|אִם־\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb you remove|תַשְׁמִ֛ידוּ\rb* \rb from among you|מִֽקִּרְבְּכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb whatever is devoted to destruction|הַחֵ֖רֶם\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Get up|קֻ֚ם\rb* \rb and consecrate|קַדֵּ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb*, \rb saying|וְאָמַרְתָּ֖\rb*, ‘\rb Consecrate yourselves|הִתְקַדְּשׁ֣וּ\rb* \rb for tomorrow|לְמָחָ֑ר\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this is what|כֹה֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*, \rb says|אָמַ֨ר\rb*: \rb Among you|בְּקִרְבְּךָ֙\rb*, \rb O Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb there are things devoted to destruction|חֵ֤רֶם\rb*. \rb You cannot|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |תוּכַ֗ל\rb* \rb stand|לָקוּם֙\rb* \rb against|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb your enemies|אֹיְבֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb you remove|הֲסִירְכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb them|הַחֵ֖רֶם\rb*\rb |מִֽקִּרְבְּכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb In the morning|בַּבֹּ֖קֶר\rb* \rb you must present yourselves|וְנִקְרַבְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb tribe by tribe|לְשִׁבְטֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*.\rb |וְהָיָ֡ה\rb* \rb The tribe|הַשֵּׁבֶט֩\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb selects|יִלְכְּדֶ֨נּוּ\rb* \rb shall come forward|יִקְרַ֣ב\rb* \rb clan by clan|לַמִּשְׁפָּח֗וֹת\rb*, \rb and the clan|וְהַמִּשְׁפָּחָ֞ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb selects|יִלְכְּדֶ֤נָּה\rb* \rb shall come forward|תִּקְרַ֣ב\rb* \rb family by family|לַבָּתִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb and the family|וְהַבַּ֙יִת֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb selects|יִלְכְּדֶ֣נּוּ\rb* \rb shall come forward|יִקְרַ֖ב\rb* \rb man by man|לַגְּבָרִֽים׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb |וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb The one who is caught|הַנִּלְכָּ֣ד\rb* \rb with the things devoted to destruction|בַּחֵ֔רֶם\rb* \rb must be burned|יִשָּׂרֵ֣ף\rb*\rb |בָּאֵ֔שׁ\rb*,\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb along with all|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb that belongs to him|כָּל־\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |ל֑וֹ\rb* \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb he has transgressed|עָבַר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the covenant|בְּרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb committed|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb an outrage|נְבָלָ֖ה\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.’”
\s1 The Sin of Achan
\p \v 16 \rb So Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb arose early|וַיַּשְׁכֵּ֤ם\rb* \rb the next morning|בַּבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb and had Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb come forward|וַיַּקְרֵ֥ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb tribe by tribe|לִשְׁבָטָ֑יו\rb*, \rb and the tribe|שֵׁ֥בֶט\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \rb was selected|וַיִּלָּכֵ֖ד\rb*. \v 17 \rb He had the clans|מִשְׁפַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb come forward|וַיַּקְרֵב֙\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and the clan|מִשְׁפַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb of the Zerahites|הַזַּרְחִ֑י\rb* \rb was selected|וַיִּלְכֹּ֕ד\rb*.\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb He had the clan|מִשְׁפַּ֤חַת\rb* \rb of the Zerahites|הַזַּרְחִי֙\rb* \rb come forward|וַיַּקְרֵ֞ב\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and the family|לַגְּבָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb of Zabdi|זַבְדִּֽי׃\rb* \rb was selected|וַיִּלָּכֵ֖ד\rb*. \v 18 \rb And he had the family of Zabdi|בֵּית֖וֹ\rb* \rb come forward|וַיַּקְרֵ֥ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb man by man|לַגְּבָרִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and Achan|עָכָ֞ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Carmi|כַּרְמִ֧י\rb*, \rb the son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Zabdi|זַבְדִּ֛י\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zerah|זֶ֖רַח\rb*, \rb of the tribe|לְמַטֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*, \rb was selected|וַיִּלָּכֵ֗ד\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb So Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֜עַ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Achan|עָכָ֗ן\rb*, “\rb My son|בְּנִי֙\rb*, \rb give|שִֽׂים־\rb* \rb glory|כָב֗וֹד\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֛ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb and make|וְתֶן־\rb* \rb a confession|תוֹדָ֑ה\rb* \rb to Him|ל֣וֹ\rb*. \rb I urge you|נָ֣א\rb* \rb to tell|וְהַגֶּד־\rb*\rb |נָ֥א\rb* \rb me|לִי֙\rb* \rb what|מֶ֣ה\rb* \rb you have done|עָשִׂ֔יתָ\rb*; \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb hide it|תְּכַחֵ֖ד\rb* \rb from me|מִמֶּֽנִּי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 20 “\rb It is true|אָמְנָ֗ה\rb*,” \rb Achan|עָכָ֛ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb replied|וַיַּ֧עַן\rb*\rb |יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb*,\rb |וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb* “\rb I|אָנֹכִ֤י\rb* \rb have sinned|חָטָ֙אתִי֙\rb* \rb against the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*. \rb This|וְכָזֹ֥את\rb*\rb |וְכָזֹ֖את\rb* \rb is what I did|עָשִֽׂיתִי׃\rb*: \v 21 \rb When I saw|וָאֶרְאֶה\rb* \rb among the spoils|בַשָּׁלָ֡ל\rb* \rb a|אַחַ֨ת\rb* \rb beautiful|טוֹבָ֜ה\rb* \rb cloak|אַדֶּ֣רֶת\rb* \rb from Shinar|שִׁנְעָר֩\rb*,\f + \fr 7:21 \ft That is, Babylonia \f* \rb two hundred|וּמָאתַ֧יִם\rb* \rb shekels|שְׁקָלִ֣ים\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֗סֶף\rb*,\f + \fr 7:21 \fqa 200 shekels \ft is approximately 5 pounds or 2.3 kilograms of silver.\f* \rb and a|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb bar|וּלְשׁ֨וֹן\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָ֤ב\rb* \rb weighing|מִשְׁקָל֔וֹ\rb* \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֤ים\rb* \rb shekels|שְׁקָלִים֙\rb*,\f + \fr 7:21 \fqa 50 shekels \ft is approximately 1.26 pounds or 569.8 grams of gold.\f* \rb I coveted them|וָֽאֶחְמְדֵ֖ם\rb* \rb and took them|וָֽאֶקָּחֵ֑ם\rb*. \rb They are|וְהִנָּ֨ם\rb* \rb hidden|טְמוּנִ֥ים\rb* \rb in the ground|בָּאָ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb inside|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb my tent|הָאָֽהֳלִ֖י\rb*, \rb with the silver|וְהַכֶּ֥סֶף\rb* \rb underneath|תַּחְתֶּֽיהָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 22 \rb So Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֔ים\rb* \rb who ran|וַיָּרֻ֖צוּ\rb* \rb to the tent|הָאֹ֑הֱלָה\rb*, \rb and there it all was|וְהִנֵּ֧ה\rb*, \rb hidden|טְמוּנָ֛ה\rb* \rb in his tent|בְּאָהֳל֖וֹ\rb*, \rb with the silver|וְהַכֶּ֥סֶף\rb* \rb underneath|תַּחְתֶּֽיהָ׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb They took the things|וַיִּקָּחוּם֙\rb* \rb from inside|מִתּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the tent|הָאֹ֔הֶל\rb*, \rb brought them|וַיְבִאוּם֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb*\rb |וְאֶ֖ל\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and spread them out|וַיַּצִּקֻ֖ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb Then Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֣עַ\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb together with|עִמּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb Achan|עָכָ֣ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zerah|זֶ֡רַח\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the silver|הַכֶּ֣סֶף\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the cloak|הָאַדֶּ֣רֶת\rb*,\rb |וְֽאֶת־\rb* \rb the bar|לְשׁ֣וֹן\rb* \rb of gold|הַזָּהָ֡ב\rb*,\rb |וְֽאֶת־\rb* \rb his sons|בָּנָ֡יו\rb*\rb |וְֽאֶת־\rb* \rb and daughters|בְּנֹתָ֡יו\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb his oxen|שׁוֹרוֹ֩\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb donkeys|חֲמֹר֨וֹ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb sheep|צֹאנ֤וֹ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb his tent|אָהֳלוֹ֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and everything else|כָּל־\rb* \rb he owned|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*, \rb and brought them|וַיַּעֲל֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb to the Valley|עֵ֥מֶק\rb* \rb of Achor|עָכֽוֹר׃\rb*.
\p \v 25 “\rb Why|מֶ֣ה\rb* \rb have you brought this trouble upon us|עֲכַרְתָּ֔נוּ\rb*?” \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֙עַ֙\rb*. “\rb Today|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb will bring trouble upon you|יַעְכֳּרְךָ֥\rb*!” \rb And all|כָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb stoned him to death|וַיִּרְגְּמ֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֤וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶ֔בֶן\rb*. \rb Then they stoned the others|וַיִּסְקְל֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb*\rb |בָּאֲבָנִֽים׃\rb* \rb and burned their bodies|וַיִּשְׂרְפ֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתָם֙\rb*\rb |בָּאֵ֔שׁ\rb*. \v 26 \rb And they heaped|וַיָּקִ֨ימוּ\rb* \rb over Achan|עָלָ֜יו\rb* \rb a large|גָּד֗וֹל\rb* \rb pile|גַּל־\rb* \rb of rocks|אֲבָנִ֣ים\rb* \rb that remains to|עַ֚ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*. \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb turned|וַיָּ֥שָׁב\rb* \rb from His burning anger|מֵחֲר֣וֹן\rb*\rb |אַפּ֑וֹ\rb*. \rb Therefore|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֠ן\rb* \rb that|הַהוּא֙\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֤וֹם\rb* \rb is called|קָרָ֞א\rb*\rb |שֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb the Valley|עֵ֣מֶק\rb* \rb of Achor|עָכ֔וֹר\rb*\f + \fr 7:26 \fqa Achor \ft means \fqa trouble\ft .\f* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃פ\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*.
\c 8
\s1 The Conquest of Ai
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֙עַ֙\rb*, “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָ֣א\rb*\rb |וְאַל־\rb* \rb or discouraged|תֵּחָ֔ת\rb*. \rb Take|קַ֣ח\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb army|הַמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb*\rb |עַ֣ם\rb* \rb with you|עִמְּךָ֗\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb*, \rb and go up|וְק֖וּם\rb* \rb and attack|עֲלֵ֣ה\rb* \rb Ai|הָעָ֑י\rb*. \rb See|רְאֵ֣ה׀\rb*, \rb I have delivered|נָתַ֣תִּי\rb* \rb into your hand|בְיָדְךָ֗\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Ai|הָעַי֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb his people|עַמּ֔וֹ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb his city|עִיר֖וֹ\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb his land|אַרְצֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb And you shall do|וְעָשִׂ֨יתָ\rb* \rb to Ai|לָעַ֜י\rb* \rb and its king|וּלְמַלְכָּ֗הּ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you did|עָשִׂ֤יתָ\rb* \rb to Jericho|לִֽירִיחוֹ֙\rb* \rb and its king|וּלְמַלְכָּ֔הּ\rb*, \rb except that|רַק־\rb* \rb you may carry off|תָּבֹ֣זּוּ\rb* \rb their plunder|שְׁלָלָ֥הּ\rb* \rb and livestock|וּבְהֶמְתָּ֖הּ\rb* \rb for yourselves|לָכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Set up|שִׂים־\rb* \rb an ambush|אֹרֵ֛ב\rb* \rb behind|מֵאַחֲרֶֽיהָ׃\rb* \rb the city|לָעִ֖יר\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb So Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֛עַ\rb* \rb and the whole|וְכָל־\rb* \rb army|הַמִּלְחָמָ֖ה\rb*\rb |עַ֥ם\rb* \rb set out|וַיָּ֧קָם\rb* \rb to attack|לַעֲל֣וֹת\rb* \rb Ai|הָעָ֑י\rb*. \rb Joshua|יְ֠הוֹשֻׁעַ\rb* \rb chose|וַיִּבְחַ֣ר\rb* \rb 30,000|שְׁלֹשִׁ֨ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֤לֶף\rb*\rb |אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb mighty men|גִּבּוֹרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of valor|הַחַ֔יִל\rb* \rb and sent them out|וַיִּשְׁלָחֵ֖ם\rb* \rb at night|לָֽיְלָה׃\rb* \v 4 \rb with these orders|וַיְצַ֨ו\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֜ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb*: “\rb Pay attention|רְ֠אוּ\rb*. \rb You|אַתֶּ֞ם\rb* \rb are to lie in ambush|אֹרְבִ֤ים\rb* \rb behind|מֵאַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb the city|לָעִיר֙\rb*,\rb |מִן־\rb*\rb |הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb not|אַל־\rb* \rb too|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb far|תַּרְחִ֥יקוּ\rb* \rb from it|הָעִ֔יר\rb*. \rb All of you|כֻּלְּכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb must be|וִהְיִיתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb ready|נְכֹנִֽים׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb Then I|וַאֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּ֔י\rb* \rb will advance|נִקְרַ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb on the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb*.\rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they come out|יֵצְא֤וּ\rb* \rb against us|לִקְרָאתֵ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they did the first time|בָּרִֽאשֹׁנָ֔ה\rb*, \rb we will flee|וְנַ֖סְנוּ\rb* \rb from them|לִפְנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb They will pursue us|וְיָצְא֣וּ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb until|עַ֣ד\rb* \rb we have drawn them away|הַתִּיקֵ֤נוּ\rb*\rb |אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they will say|יֹֽאמְר֔וּ\rb*, ‘\rb The Israelites are running away|נָסִ֣ים\rb* \rb from us|לְפָנֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb as they did before|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb*\rb |בָּרִֽאשֹׁנָ֑ה\rb*.’ \rb So as we flee|וְנַ֖סְנוּ\rb* \rb from them|לִפְנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*, \v 7 \rb you|וְאַתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb are to rise|תָּקֻ֙מוּ֙\rb* \rb from the ambush|מֵהָ֣אוֹרֵ֔ב\rb* \rb and seize|וְהוֹרַשְׁתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb*, \rb for the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb will deliver it|וּנְתָנָ֛הּ\rb* \rb into your hand|בְּיֶדְכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb And|וְהָיָ֞ה\rb* \rb when you have taken|כְּתָפְשְׂכֶ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֗יר\rb*, \rb set it|הָעִיר֙\rb* \rb on fire|תַּצִּ֤יתוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |בָּאֵ֔שׁ\rb*. \rb Do|תַּעֲשׂ֑וּ\rb* \rb as the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has commanded|כִּדְבַ֥ר\rb*! \rb See|רְא֖וּ\rb*, \rb I have given you orders|צִוִּ֥יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb So Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֗עַ\rb* \rb sent them out|וַיִּשְׁלָחֵ֣ם\rb*, \rb and they went|וַיֵּֽלְכוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the place of ambush|הַמַּאְרָ֔ב\rb* \rb and lay in wait|וַיֵּשְׁב֗וּ\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֧ין\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel|אֵ֛ל\rb* \rb and|וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb Ai|הָעַ֖י\rb*, \rb to the west|מִיָּ֣ם\rb* \rb of Ai|לָעָ֑י\rb*. \rb But Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֛עַ\rb* \rb spent|וַיָּ֧לֶן\rb* \rb that|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb night|בַּלַּ֥יְלָה\rb* \rb among|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the people|הָעָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb got up early|וַיַּשְׁכֵּ֤ם\rb* \rb the next morning|בַּבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb and mobilized|וַיִּפְקֹ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his men|הָעָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and he|ה֜וּא\rb* \rb and the elders|וְזִקְנֵ֧י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb marched|וַיַּ֨עַל\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb them|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb up to Ai|הָעָֽי׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb Then all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָ֨ם\rb*\rb |הַמִּלְחָמָ֜ה\rb* \rb who were|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb marched up|עָלוּ֙\rb* \rb and approached|וַֽיִּגְּשׁ֔וּ\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb*. \rb They arrived|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb in front of Ai|נֶ֣גֶד\rb* \rb and camped|וַֽיַּחֲנוּ֙\rb* \rb to the north|מִצְּפ֣וֹן\rb* \rb of it|לָעַ֔י\rb*, \rb with the valley|וְהַגַּ֖י\rb* \rb between them|בֵּינוֹ\rb*\rb |וּבֵין־\rb* \rb and the city|הָעָֽי׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Now Joshua had taken|וַיִּקַּ֕ח\rb* \rb about five|כַּחֲמֵ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb* \rb men|אִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb and set up|וַיָּ֨שֶׂם\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֜ם\rb* \rb an ambush|אֹרֵ֗ב\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֧ין\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel|אֵ֛ל\rb* \rb and|וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb Ai|הָעַ֖י\rb*, \rb to the west|מִיָּ֥ם\rb* \rb of the city|לָעִֽיר׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb So the forces|הָעָ֜ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb were stationed|וַיָּשִׂ֨ימוּ\rb* \rb with the main|כָּל־\rb* \rb camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb to the north|מִצְּפ֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the city|לָעִ֔יר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the rear guard|עֲקֵב֖וֹ\rb* \rb to the west|מִיָּ֣ם\rb* \rb of the city|לָעִ֑יר\rb*. \rb And that|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb night|בַּלַּ֥יְלָה\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֛עַ\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb into|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the valley|הָעֵֽמֶק׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb |וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb When the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Ai|הָעַ֗י\rb* \rb saw the Israelites|כִּרְא֣וֹת\rb*, \rb he hurried|וַֽיְמַהֲר֡וּ\rb* \rb out|וַיֵּצְא֣וּ\rb* \rb early in the morning|וַיַּשְׁכִּ֡ימוּ\rb* \rb with the men|אַנְשֵֽׁי־\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֣יר\rb*\rb |ה֧וּא\rb*\rb |וְכָל־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb to engage|לִקְרַֽאת־\rb* \rb them|יִ֠שְׂרָאֵל\rb* \rb in battle|לַֽמִּלְחָמָ֞ה\rb* \rb at an appointed place|לַמּוֹעֵ֖ד\rb* \rb overlooking|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the Arabah|הָֽעֲרָבָ֑ה\rb*. \rb But he|וְהוּא֙\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֔ע\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb an ambush|אֹרֵ֥ב\rb* \rb had been set up against him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb behind|מֵאַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb the city|הָעִֽיר׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֥עַ\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb let themselves be beaten back|וַיִּנָּֽגְע֛וּ\rb* \rb before them|לִפְנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and they fled|וַיָּנֻ֖סוּ\rb* \rb toward|דֶּ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb the wilderness|הַמִּדְבָּֽר׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb Then all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the men|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb of Ai|בָּעִיר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb were summoned|וַיִּזָּעֲק֗וּ\rb* \rb to pursue them|לִרְדֹּ֖ף\rb*,\rb |אַחֲרֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and they followed|וַֽיִּרְדְּפוּ֙\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb* \rb and were drawn away|וַיִּנָּתְק֖וּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִֽיר׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb Not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb was left|נִשְׁאַ֣ר\rb* \rb in Ai|בָּעַי֙\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb or Bethel|אֵ֔ל\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb go out|יָצְא֖וּ\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb leaving|וַיַּעַזְב֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִיר֙\rb* \rb wide open|פְּתוּחָ֔ה\rb* \rb while they pursued|וַֽיִּרְדְּפ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֗עַ\rb*, “\rb Hold out|נְ֠טֵה\rb* \rb your battle lance|בַּכִּיד֤וֹן\rb*\f + \fr 8:18 \ft Or \fqa javelin\ft ; twice in this verse, and also in verse 26\f*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |בְּיָֽדְךָ֙\rb* \rb toward|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ai|הָעַ֔י\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb into your hand|בְיָדְךָ֖\rb* \rb I will deliver the city|אֶתְּנֶ֑נָּה\rb*.” \rb So Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֛עַ\rb* \rb held out|וַיֵּ֧ט\rb* \rb his battle lance|בַּכִּיד֥וֹן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |בְּיָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb toward|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ai|הָעִֽיר׃\rb*, \v 19 \rb and as soon as he did so|כִּנְט֣וֹת\rb*\rb |יָד֔וֹ\rb*, \rb the men in ambush|וְהָאוֹרֵ֡ב\rb* \rb rose|קָם֩\rb* \rb quickly|מְהֵרָ֨ה\rb* \rb from their position|מִמְּקוֹמ֤וֹ\rb*. \rb They rushed forward|וַיָּר֙וּצוּ֙\rb*, \rb entered|וַיָּבֹ֥אוּ\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֖יר\rb*, \rb captured it|וַֽיִּלְכְּד֑וּהָ\rb*, \rb and immediately|וַֽיְמַהֲר֔וּ\rb* \rb set it|הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb on fire|וַיַּצִּ֥יתוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |בָּאֵֽשׁ׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb When the men|אַנְשֵׁי֩\rb* \rb of Ai|הָעַ֨י\rb* \rb turned|וַיִּפְנ֣וּ\rb* \rb and looked|וַיִּרְא֗וּ\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb back|אַחֲרֵיהֶ֜ם\rb*, \rb the smoke|עֲשַׁ֤ן\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִיר֙\rb* \rb was rising|עָלָ֜ה\rb* \rb into the sky|הַשָּׁמַ֔יְמָה\rb*. \rb They could not|וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |הָיָ֨ה\rb*\rb |בָהֶ֥ם\rb*\rb |יָדַ֛יִם\rb* \rb escape|לָנ֖וּס\rb* \rb in any direction|הֵ֣נָּה\rb*\rb |וָהֵ֑נָּה\rb*, \rb and the troops|וְהָעָם֙\rb* \rb who had fled|הַנָּ֣ס\rb* \rb to the wilderness|הַמִּדְבָּ֔ר\rb* \rb now turned|נֶהְפַּ֖ךְ\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb their pursuers|הָרוֹדֵֽף׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb When Joshua|וִיהוֹשֻׁ֨עַ\rb* \rb and all|וְכָֽל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb saw|רָא֗וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the men in ambush|הָֽאֹרֵב֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had captured|לָכַ֤ד\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb and that|וְכִ֥י\rb* \rb smoke|עֲשַׁ֣ן\rb* \rb was rising from|עָלָ֖ה\rb* \rb it|הָעִ֑יר\rb*, \rb they turned around|וַיָּשֻׁ֕בוּ\rb* \rb and struck down|וַיַּכּ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of Ai|הָעָֽי׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb Meanwhile, those in the ambush|וְאֵ֨לֶּה\rb* \rb came out|יָצְא֤וּ\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִיר֙\rb* \rb against them|לִקְרָאתָ֔ם\rb*, \rb and the men of Ai were|וַיִּֽהְי֤וּ\rb* \rb trapped between|בַּתָּ֔וֶךְ\rb* \rb the Israelite|לְיִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb forces|אֵ֥לֶּה\rb* \rb on|מִזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb both sides|וְאֵ֣לֶּה\rb*\rb |מִזֶּ֑ה\rb*. \rb So Israel struck them down|וַיַּכּ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb no|בִּלְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb survivor|שָׂרִ֥יד\rb* \rb or fugitive|וּפָלִֽיט׃\rb* \rb remained|הִשְׁאִֽיר־\rb*. \v 23 \rb But|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb they took|תָּ֣פְשׂוּ\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Ai|הָעַ֖י\rb* \rb alive|חָ֑י\rb* \rb and brought|וַיַּקְרִ֥בוּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻֽׁעַ׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb When Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֡ל\rb* \rb had finished|כְּכַלּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb killing|לַהֲרֹג֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the men|יֹשְׁבֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Ai|הָעַ֜י\rb* \rb who had pursued|רְדָפ֣וּם\rb* \rb them|בּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb into the field|בַּשָּׂדֶ֗ה\rb* \rb and wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּר֙\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb and when every|כֻלָּ֛ם\rb* \rb last one of them had fallen|וַֽיִּפְּל֥וּ\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb by the sword|חֶ֖רֶב\rb*,\rb |עַד־\rb*\rb |תֻּמָּ֑ם\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּשֻׁ֤בוּ\rb* \rb to Ai|הָעַ֔י\rb* \rb and put|וַיַּכּ֥וּ\rb* \rb it|אֹתָ֖הּ\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb to the sword as well|חָֽרֶב׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb |וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb A total|כָל־\rb* \rb of twelve|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb thousand|אָ֑לֶף\rb* \rb men|מֵאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb* \rb women|אִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb fell|הַנֹּ֨פְלִ֜ים\rb* \rb that|הַהוּא֙\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֤וֹם\rb*— \rb all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the people|אַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of Ai|הָעָֽי׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb Joshua|וִיהוֹשֻׁ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb draw back|הֵשִׁ֣יב\rb* \rb the hand|יָד֔וֹ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb held|נָטָ֖ה\rb* \rb his battle lance|בַּכִּיד֑וֹן\rb* \rb until|עַ֚ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he had devoted to destruction|הֶחֱרִ֔ים\rb*\f + \fr 8:26 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering.\f* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who lived|יֹשְׁבֵ֥י\rb* \rb in Ai|הָעָֽי׃\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb*. \v 27 \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb took|בָּזְז֥וּ\rb* \rb for themselves|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb only|רַ֣ק\rb* \rb the cattle|הַבְּהֵמָ֗ה\rb* \rb and plunder|וּשְׁלַל֙\rb* \rb of that|הַהִ֔יא\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֣יר\rb*, \rb as the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |כִּדְבַ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻֽׁעַ׃\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb So Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb burned|וַיִּשְׂרֹ֥ף\rb* \rb Ai|הָעָ֑י\rb*\f + \fr 8:28 \fqa Ai \ft means \fqa ruin\ft .\f* \rb and made it|וַיְשִׂימֶ֤הָ\rb* \rb a permanent|עוֹלָם֙\rb* \rb heap of ruins|תֵּל־\rb*, \rb a desolation|שְׁמָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*. \v 29 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb He hung|תָּלָ֥ה\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Ai|הָעַ֛י\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb a tree|הָעֵ֖ץ\rb*\f + \fr 8:29 \ft Or \fqa He impaled the king of Ai on a pole\f* \rb until|עַד־\rb*\rb |עֵ֣ת\rb* \rb evening|הָעָ֑רֶב\rb*, \rb and at sunset|וּכְב֣וֹא\rb*\rb |הַשֶּׁמֶשׁ֩\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֜עַ\rb* \rb commanded|צִוָּ֨ה\rb* \rb that they take down the body|נִבְלָת֣וֹ\rb*\rb |וַיֹּרִ֧ידוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the tree|הָעֵ֗ץ\rb* \rb and throw it down|וַיַּשְׁלִ֤יכוּ\rb*\rb |אוֹתָהּ֙\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the entrance|פֶּ֙תַח֙\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb*. \rb And over it|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb they raised|וַיָּקִ֤ימוּ\rb* \rb a large|גָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb pile|גַּל־\rb* \rb of rocks|אֲבָנִ֣ים\rb*, \rb which remains to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃פ\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*.
\s1 Joshua Renews the Covenant
\r (\ref Deuteronomy 27:1–10|DEU 27:1-10\ref*)
\p \v 30 \rb At that time|אָ֣ז\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb built|יִבְנֶ֤ה\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb* \rb on Mount|בְּהַ֖ר\rb* \rb Ebal|עֵיבָֽל׃\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \v 31 \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֨ה\rb* \rb the servant|עֶֽבֶד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּה֩\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*. \rb He built it according to what is written|כַּכָּתוּב֙\rb* \rb in the Book|בְּסֵ֙פֶר֙\rb* \rb of the Law|תּוֹרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*: “\rb an altar|מִזְבַּח֙\rb* \rb of uncut|שְׁלֵמ֔וֹת\rb* \rb stones|אֲבָנִ֣ים\rb* \rb on|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ן\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb iron tool|בַּרְזֶ֑ל\rb* \rb has been used|הֵנִ֥יף\rb*.”\f + \fr 8:31 \ft \ref Exodus 20:25|EXO 20:25\ref*; Deuteronomy 27:5\f* \rb And on it|עָלָ֤יו\rb* \rb they offered|וַיַּעֲל֨וּ\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹלוֹת֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and they sacrificed|וַֽיִּזְבְּח֖וּ\rb* \rb peace offerings|שְׁלָמִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 32 \rb And there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*, \rb Joshua inscribed|וַיִּכְתָּב־\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the stones|הָאֲבָנִ֑ים\rb*\rb |אֵ֗ת\rb* \rb a copy|מִשְׁנֵה֙\rb* \rb of the law|תּוֹרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he had written|כָּתַ֔ב\rb*. \v 33 \rb All|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֡ל\rb*, \rb foreigners|כַּגֵּר֙\rb* \rb and citizens alike|כָּֽאֶזְרָ֔ח\rb*, \rb with their elders|וּזְקֵנָ֡יו\rb*, \rb officers|וְשֹׁטְרִ֣ים׀\rb*, \rb and judges|וְשֹׁפְטָ֡יו\rb*, \rb stood|עֹמְדִ֣ים\rb* \rb on both sides|מִזֶּ֣ה׀\rb*\rb |וּמִזֶּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb of the ark|לָאָר֡וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb facing|נֶגֶד֩\rb* \rb the Levitical|הַלְוִיִּ֜ם\rb* \rb priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֨ים\rb* \rb who carried|נֹשְׂאֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb it|אֲר֣וֹן\rb*. \rb Half of the people stood|חֶצְיוֹ֙\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb front|מ֣וּל\rb* \rb of Mount|הַר־\rb* \rb Gerizim|גְּרִזִ֔ים\rb* \rb and half of them|וְהַֽחֶצְי֖וֹ\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb front|מ֣וּל\rb* \rb of Mount|הַר־\rb* \rb Ebal|עֵיבָ֑ל\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb the servant|עֶֽבֶד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֜ה\rb* \rb earlier|בָּרִאשֹׁנָֽה׃\rb*, \rb to bless|לְבָרֵ֛ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֥ם\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*.
\p \v 34 \rb Afterward|וְאַֽחֲרֵי־\rb*\rb |כֵ֗ן\rb*, \rb Joshua read aloud|קָרָא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the law|הַתּוֹרָ֔ה\rb*— \rb the blessings|הַבְּרָכָ֖ה\rb* \rb and the curses|וְהַקְּלָלָ֑ה\rb*— \rb according to all|כְּכָל־\rb* \rb that is written|הַכָּת֖וּב\rb* \rb in the Book|בְּסֵ֥פֶר\rb* \rb of the Law|הַתּוֹרָֽה׃\rb*. \v 35 \rb There was|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb a word|דָבָ֔ר\rb* \rb of all|מִכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֣ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֗עַ\rb* \rb failed|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb to read|קָרָ֜א\rb* \rb before|נֶ֣גֶד\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb assembly|קְהַ֤ל\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*, \rb including the women|וְהַנָּשִׁ֣ים\rb*, \rb the little ones|וְהַטַּ֔ף\rb*, \rb and the foreigners|וְהַגֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb who lived|הַהֹלֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb among them|בְּקִרְבָּֽם׃פ\rb*.
\c 9
\s1 The Deceit of the Gibeonites
\p \v 1 \rb Now when|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb news of this reached|כִשְׁמֹ֣עַ\rb* \rb all|כָּֽל־\rb* \rb the kings|הַמְּלָכִ֡ים\rb* \rb west|בְּעֵ֨בֶר\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֜ן\rb* — \rb those|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb in the hill country|בָּהָ֣ר\rb*, \rb the foothills|וּבַשְּׁפֵלָ֗ה\rb*,\f + \fr 9:1 \ft Hebrew \fqa Shephelah \ft or \fqa lowlands\ft ; that is, the western foothills of Judea\f* \rb and all|וּבְכֹל֙\rb* \rb along the coast|ח֚וֹף\rb* \rb of the Great|הַגָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb Sea|הַיָּ֣ם\rb*\f + \fr 9:1 \ft That is, the Mediterranean Sea\f* \rb toward|אֶל־\rb*\rb |מ֖וּל\rb* \rb Lebanon|הַלְּבָנ֑וֹן\rb* (\rb the Hittites|הַֽחִתִּי֙\rb*, \rb Amorites|וְהָ֣אֱמֹרִ֔י\rb*, \rb Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִי֙\rb*, \rb Perizzites|הַפְּרִזִּ֔י\rb*, \rb Hivites|הַחִוִּ֖י\rb*, \rb and Jebusites|וְהַיְבוּסִֽי׃\rb*)— \v 2 \rb they came|וַיִּֽתְקַבְּצ֣וּ\rb* \rb together|יַחְדָּ֔ו\rb*\rb |פֶּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶחָֽד׃פ\rb* \rb to wage war|לְהִלָּחֵ֥ם\rb* \rb against|עִם־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb*\rb |וְעִם־\rb* \rb and Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb But the people|וְיֹשְׁבֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Gibeon|גִבְע֜וֹן\rb*, \rb having heard|שָׁמְע֗וּ\rb*\rb |אֵת֩\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֛עַ\rb* \rb had done|עָשָׂ֧ה\rb* \rb to Jericho|לִֽירִיח֖וֹ\rb* \rb and Ai|וְלָעָֽי׃\rb*, \v 4 \rb acted deceptively|וַיַּעֲשׂ֤וּ\rb*\rb |גַם־\rb*\rb |הֵ֙מָּה֙\rb*\rb |בְּעָרְמָ֔ה\rb* \rb and set out|וַיֵּלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb as envoys|וַיִּצְטַיָּ֑רוּ\rb*,\f + \fr 9:4 \ft Or \fqa set out with provisions\f* \rb carrying|וַיִּקְח֞וּ\rb* \rb on their donkeys|לַחֲמ֣וֹרֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb worn-out|בָּלִים֙\rb* \rb sacks|שַׂקִּ֤ים\rb* \rb and old|בָּלִ֔ים\rb* \rb wineskins|וְנֹאד֥וֹת\rb*\rb |יַ֙יִן֙\rb*, \rb cracked|וּמְבֻקָּעִ֖ים\rb* \rb and mended|וּמְצֹרָרִֽים׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb They put worn|בָּל֤וֹת\rb*, \rb patched|וּמְטֻלָּאוֹת֙\rb* \rb sandals|וּנְעָל֨וֹת\rb* \rb on their feet|בְּרַגְלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and threadbare|בָּל֖וֹת\rb* \rb clothing|וּשְׂלָמ֥וֹת\rb* \rb on their bodies|עֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and their whole|וְכֹל֙\rb* \rb supply|צֵידָ֔ם\rb* \rb of bread|לֶ֣חֶם\rb* \rb was dry|יָבֵ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb and moldy|נִקֻּדִֽים׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb They went|וַיֵּלְכ֧וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֛עַ\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb at Gilgal|הַגִּלְגָּ֑ל\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּאמְר֨וּ\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֜יו\rb* \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*, “\rb We have come|בָּ֔אנוּ\rb*\rb |וְעַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb from a distant|רְחוֹקָה֙\rb* \rb land|מֵאֶ֤רֶץ\rb*; \rb please make|כִּרְתוּ־\rb* \rb a treaty|בְרִֽית׃\rb*\f + \fr 9:6 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa berit \ft are translated in most passages as \fqa covenant\ft ; also in verses 7, 11, 15, and 16.\f* \rb with us|לָ֥נוּ\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb But the men|אִֽישׁ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמְרוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Hivites|הַחִוִּ֑י\rb*, “\rb Perhaps|אוּלַ֗י\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb dwell|יוֹשֵׁ֔ב\rb* \rb near us|בְּקִרְבִּי֙\rb*. \rb How|וְאֵ֖יךְ\rb* \rb can we make|אֶכְרוֹת\rb*\rb |לְךָ֥\rb* \rb a treaty with you|בְרִֽית׃\rb*?”
\p \v 8 “\rb We|אֲנָ֑חְנוּ\rb* \rb are your servants|עֲבָדֶ֣יךָ\rb*,” \rb they said|וַיֹּאמְר֥וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb*.
\p \rb Then Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֛עַ\rb* \rb asked them|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*,\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֧ם\rb* “\rb Who|מִ֥י\rb* \rb are you|אַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb and where|וּמֵאַ֥יִן\rb* \rb have you come from|תָּבֹֽאוּ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 9 “\rb Your servants|עֲבָדֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb have come|בָּ֣אוּ\rb* \rb from a very|מְאֹד֙\rb* \rb distant|רְחוֹקָ֤ה\rb* \rb land|מֵאֶ֨רֶץ\rb*,” \rb they replied|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֗יו\rb*, “\rb because of the fame|לְשֵׁ֖ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb*. \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb we have heard|שָׁמַ֣עְנוּ\rb* \rb the reports about Him|שָׁמְע֔וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֛ת\rb*: \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He did|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb in Egypt|בְּמִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*, \v 10 \rb and|וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He did|עָשָׂ֗ה\rb* \rb to the two|לִשְׁנֵי֙\rb* \rb kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Amorites|הָאֱמֹרִ֔י\rb* \rb beyond|בְּעֵ֣בֶר\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֑ן\rb*— \rb Sihon|לְסִיחוֹן֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Heshbon|חֶשְׁבּ֔וֹן\rb* \rb and Og|וּלְע֥וֹג\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Bashan|הַבָּשָׁ֖ן\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb reigned in Ashtaroth|בְּעַשְׁתָּרֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb So the elders|זְֽקֵינֵינוּ֩\rb* \rb and|וְכָל־\rb* \rb inhabitants|יֹשְׁבֵ֨י\rb* \rb of our land|אַרְצֵ֜נוּ\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb us|אֵלֵ֡ינוּ\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* ‘\rb Take|קְח֨וּ\rb*\rb |בְיֶדְכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb provisions|צֵידָה֙\rb* \rb for your journey|לַדֶּ֔רֶךְ\rb*; \rb go|וּלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb to meet them|לִקְרָאתָ֑ם\rb* \rb and say|וַאֲמַרְתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb*: \rb We|אֲנַ֔חְנוּ\rb*\rb |וְעַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb are your servants|עַבְדֵיכֶ֣ם\rb*. \rb Please make|כִּרְתוּ־\rb* \rb a treaty|בְרִֽית׃\rb* \rb with us|לָ֥נוּ\rb*.’
\p \v 12 \rb This|זֶ֣ה׀\rb* \rb bread|לַחְמֵ֗נוּ\rb* \rb of ours was warm|חָ֞ם\rb* \rb when we packed|הִצְטַיַּ֤דְנוּ\rb* \rb it|אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb at home|מִבָּ֣תֵּ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb on the day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb* \rb we left|צֵאתֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb to come|לָלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb to you|אֲלֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb But look|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb*, \rb it is now|וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb dry|יָבֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb and|וְהָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb moldy|נִקֻּדִֽים׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb These|וְאֵ֨לֶּה\rb* \rb wineskins|נֹאד֤וֹת\rb*\rb |הַיַּ֙יִן֙\rb* \rb were new|חֲדָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb when we filled|מִלֵּ֣אנוּ\rb* \rb them|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*, \rb but look|וְהִנֵּ֖ה\rb*, \rb they are cracked|הִתְבַּקָּ֑עוּ\rb*. \rb And these|וְאֵ֤לֶּה\rb* \rb clothes|שַׂלְמוֹתֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb and sandals|וּנְעָלֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb are worn out|בָּל֕וּ\rb* \rb from our very|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb long|מֵרֹ֥ב\rb* \rb journey|הַדֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb Then the men of Israel|הָֽאֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb sampled|וַיִּקְח֥וּ\rb* \rb their provisions|מִצֵּידָ֑ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb but did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb seek|שָׁאָֽלוּ׃\rb* \rb the counsel|פִּ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*. \v 15 \rb And Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb made|וַיַּ֨עַשׂ\rb* \rb a treaty|בְּרִ֖ית\rb* \rb of peace|שָׁל֔וֹם\rb* \rb with them|לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb to let them live|לְחַיּוֹתָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and the leaders|נְשִׂיאֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the congregation|הָעֵדָֽה׃\rb* \rb swore an oath|וַיִּשָּׁבְע֣וּ\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb*\rb |מִקְצֵה֙\rb* \rb Three|שְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֕י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they had made|כָּרְת֥וּ\rb* \rb the treaty|בְּרִ֑ית\rb* \rb with the Gibeonites|לָהֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb the Israelites learned|וַֽיִּשְׁמְע֗וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb they were|הֵם֙\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb neighbors|קְרֹבִ֥ים\rb*, \rb living|יֹשְׁבִֽים׃\rb* \rb among them|וּבְקִרְבּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |הֵ֥ם\rb*. \v 17 \rb So the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb set out|וַיִּסְע֣וּ\rb* \rb and on the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֑י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb arrived|וַיָּבֹ֛אוּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb at their cities|עָרֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* —\rb |וְעָרֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb Gibeon|גִּבְע֣וֹן\rb*, \rb Chephirah|וְהַכְּפִירָ֔ה\rb*, \rb Beeroth|וּבְאֵר֖וֹת\rb*,\rb |וְקִרְיַ֥ת\rb* \rb and Kiriath-jearim|יְעָרִֽים׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb But the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb attack them|הִכּוּם֙\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the leaders|נְשִׂיאֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the congregation|הָֽעֵדָ֔ה\rb* \rb had sworn an oath|נִשְׁבְּע֤וּ\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb by the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb And the whole|כָל־\rb* \rb congregation|הָעֵדָ֖ה\rb* \rb grumbled|וַיִּלֹּ֥נוּ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the leaders|הַנְּשִׂיאִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb All|כָל־\rb* \rb the leaders|הַנְּשִׂיאִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּאמְר֤וּ\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |הָ֣עֵדָ֔ה\rb*, “\rb We|אֲנַ֙חְנוּ֙\rb* \rb have sworn an oath|נִשְׁבַּ֣עְנוּ\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb by the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and now|וְעַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb we cannot|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |נוּכַ֖ל\rb* \rb touch|לִנְגֹּ֥עַ\rb* \rb them|בָּהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb This|זֹ֛את\rb* \rb is how we will treat|נַעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb*: \rb We will let them live|וְהַחֲיֵ֣ה\rb*,\rb |אוֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb so that no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb wrath|קֶ֔צֶף\rb* \rb will fall|יִֽהְיֶ֤ה\rb* \rb on us|עָלֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb because of|עַל־\rb* \rb the oath|הַשְּׁבוּעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb we swore|נִשְׁבַּ֥עְנוּ\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶֽם׃\rb*.” \v 21 \rb They|הַנְּשִׂיאִ֖ים\rb* \rb continued|וַיֹּאמְר֧וּ\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֛ם\rb*, “\rb Let them live|יִֽחְי֑וּ\rb*, \rb but let them be|וַ֠יִּֽהְיוּ\rb* \rb woodcutters|חֹטְבֵ֨י\rb*\rb |עֵצִ֤ים\rb* \rb and water|מַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb carriers|וְשֹֽׁאֲבֵי־\rb* \rb for the whole|לְכָל־\rb* \rb congregation|הָ֣עֵדָ֔ה\rb*.” \rb So|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the leaders|הַנְּשִׂיאִֽים׃\rb* \rb kept their promise|דִּבְּר֥וּ\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb Then Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb* \rb the Gibeonites|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb and said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*, “\rb Why|לָמָּה֩\rb* \rb did you deceive|רִמִּיתֶ֨ם\rb* \rb us|אֹתָ֜נוּ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb by telling us|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb you live far away|רְחוֹקִ֨ים\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb from|מִכֶּם֙\rb* \rb us|אֲנַ֤חְנוּ\rb*, \rb when in fact you|וְאַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb live|יֹשְׁבִֽים׃\rb* \rb among us|בְּקִרְבֵּ֥נוּ\rb*? \v 23 \rb Now therefore|וְעַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֑ם\rb* \rb are under a curse|אֲרוּרִ֣ים\rb* \rb and will perpetually|וְלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |יִכָּרֵ֨ת\rb*\rb |מִכֶּ֜ם\rb* \rb serve|עֶ֗בֶד\rb* \rb as woodcutters|וְחֹטְבֵ֥י\rb*\rb |עֵצִ֛ים\rb* \rb and water|מַ֖יִם\rb* \rb carriers|וְשֹֽׁאֲבֵי־\rb* \rb for the house|לְבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of my God|אֱלֹהָֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 24 \rb The Gibeonites answered|וַיַּעֲנ֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |יְהוֹשֻׁ֜עַ\rb*,\rb |וַיֹּאמְר֗וּ\rb*\rb |כִּי֩\rb* “\rb Your servants|לַעֲבָדֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֵת֩\rb*\rb |הֻגַּ֤ד\rb* \rb were told clearly|הֻגֵּ֨ד\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֜ה\rb* \rb His servant|עַבְדּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb to give|לָתֵ֤ת\rb* \rb you|לָכֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb and wipe out|וּלְהַשְׁמִ֛יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its inhabitants|יֹשְׁבֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb before you|מִפְּנֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb So we greatly|מְאֹ֤ד\rb* \rb feared|וַנִּירָ֨א\rb* \rb for our lives|לְנַפְשֹׁתֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb because of you|מִפְּנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and that is why we have done|וַֽנַּעֲשֵׂ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |הִנְנ֣וּ\rb* \rb we are in your hands|בְיָדֶ֑ךָ\rb*. \rb Do|עֲשֵֽׂה׃\rb* \rb to us|לָ֖נוּ\rb* \rb whatever seems|בְּעֵינֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb good|כַּטּ֨וֹב\rb* \rb and right|וְכַיָּשָׁ֧ר\rb* \rb to you|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb*.”
\p \v 26 \rb So|כֵּ֑ן\rb* \rb Joshua did this|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb and delivered|וַיַּצֵּ֥ל\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb from the hands|מִיַּ֥ד\rb*\rb |בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb and they did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb kill the Gibeonites|הֲרָגֽוּם׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb On that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb he|יְהוֹשֻׁ֜עַ\rb* \rb made them|וַיִּתְּנֵ֨ם\rb* \rb woodcutters|חֹטְבֵ֥י\rb*\rb |עֵצִ֛ים\rb* \rb and water|מַ֖יִם\rb* \rb carriers|וְשֹׁ֥אֲבֵי\rb*, \rb as they are to this day|עַד־\rb*\rb |הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb for the congregation|לָֽעֵדָ֑ה\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb and for the altar|וּלְמִזְבַּ֤ח\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֖וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He would choose|יִבְחָֽר׃פ\rb*.
\c 10
\s1 The Day the Sun Stood Still
\p \v 1 \rb Now|וַיְהִי֩\rb*\rb |אֲדֹֽנִי־\rb* \rb Adoni-zedek|צֶ֜דֶק\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֗ם\rb* \rb heard|כִשְׁמֹ֨עַ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֣עַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had captured|לָכַ֨ד\rb* \rb Ai|הָעַי֮\rb* \rb and devoted it to destruction|וַיַּחֲרִימָהּ֒\rb*\f + \fr 10:1 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering; also in verses 28, 35, 37, 39, and 40.\f* — \rb doing to|עָשָׂ֤ה\rb* \rb Ai|לָעַ֖י\rb* \rb and its king|וּלְמַלְכָּ֔הּ\rb*\rb |כֵּן־\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb he had done to|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb Jericho|לִֽירִיחוֹ֙\rb* \rb and its king|וּלְמַלְכָּ֑הּ\rb* — \rb and that|וְכִ֨י\rb* \rb the people|יֹשְׁבֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Gibeon|גִבְעוֹן֙\rb* \rb had made peace|הִשְׁלִ֜ימוּ\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and were living|וַיִּֽהְי֖וּ\rb* \rb near them|בְּקִרְבָּֽם׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb So Adoni-zedek and his people were greatly|מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb alarmed|וַיִּֽירְא֣וּ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Gibeon|גִּבְע֔וֹן\rb* \rb was a great|גְּדוֹלָה֙\rb* \rb city|עִ֤יר\rb*, \rb like one|כְּאַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the royal|הַמַּמְלָכָ֑ה\rb*\rb |וְכִ֨י\rb* \rb cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb*; \rb it|הִ֤יא\rb* \rb was larger|גְדוֹלָה֙\rb* \rb than|מִן־\rb* \rb Ai|הָעַ֔י\rb*, \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb its men|אֲנָשֶׁ֖יהָ\rb* \rb were mighty|גִּבֹּרִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb |אֲדֹנִי־\rb* \rb Therefore Adoni-zedek|צֶ֜דֶק\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֗ם\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb word to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Hoham|הוֹהָ֣ם\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Hebron|חֶ֠בְרוֹן\rb*,\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb Piram|פִּרְאָ֨ם\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Jarmuth|יַרְמ֜וּת\rb*,\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb Japhia|יָפִ֧יעַ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Lachish|לָכִ֛ישׁ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and Debir|דְּבִ֥יר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Eglon|עֶגְל֖וֹן\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 4 “\rb Come up|עֲלֽוּ־\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֣י\rb* \rb and help me|וְעִזְרֻ֔נִי\rb*. \rb We will attack|וְנַכֶּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Gibeon|גִּבְע֑וֹן\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they have made peace|הִשְׁלִ֥ימָה\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb So the five|חֲמֵ֣שֶׁת׀\rb* \rb kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Amorites|הָאֱמֹרִ֗י\rb*— \rb the kings|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֜ם\rb*,\rb |מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb Hebron|חֶבְר֤וֹן\rb*,\rb |מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb Jarmuth|יַרְמוּת֙\rb*,\rb |מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb Lachish|לָכִ֣ישׁ\rb*,\rb |מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb and Eglon|עֶגְל֔וֹן\rb*—\rb |הֵ֖ם\rb* \rb joined forces|וַיֵּאָסְפ֨וּ\rb* \rb and advanced|וַֽיַּעֲל֜וּ\rb* \rb with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb their armies|מַֽחֲנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb They camped|וַֽיַּחֲנוּ֙\rb* \rb before|עַל־\rb* \rb Gibeon|גִּבְע֔וֹן\rb* \rb and made war|וַיִּֽלָּחֲמ֖וּ\rb* \rb against it|עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Then the men|אַנְשֵׁי֩\rb* \rb of Gibeon|גִבְע֨וֹן\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלְח֣וּ\rb* \rb word to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֤עַ\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶה֙\rb* \rb at Gilgal|הַגִּלְגָּ֣לָה\rb*:\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb abandon|תֶּ֥רֶף\rb*\rb |יָדֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb your servants|מֵֽעֲבָדֶ֑יךָ\rb*. \rb Come|עֲלֵ֧ה\rb* \rb quickly|מְהֵרָ֗ה\rb* \rb and save|וְהוֹשִׁ֤יעָה\rb* \rb us|לָּ֙נוּ֙\rb*! \rb Help us|וְעָזְרֵ֔נוּ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Amorites|הָאֱמֹרִ֖י\rb* \rb from|יֹשְׁבֵ֥י\rb* \rb the hill country|הָהָֽר׃\rb* \rb have joined forces|נִקְבְּצ֣וּ\rb* \rb against us|אֵלֵ֔ינוּ\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb So Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֜עַ\rb* \rb and his whole|וְכָל־\rb* \rb army|הַמִּלְחָמָה֙\rb*\rb |עִמּ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |עַ֤ם\rb*, \rb including all|וְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the mighty men|גִּבּוֹרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of valor|הֶחָֽיִל׃פ\rb*, \rb came|וַיַּ֨עַל\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb Gilgal|הַגִּלְגָּ֗ל\rb*\rb |ה֚וּא\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֙עַ֙\rb*, “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָ֣א\rb* \rb of them|מֵהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I have delivered them|נְתַתִּ֑ים\rb* \rb into your hand|בְיָדְךָ֖\rb*. \rb Not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb one|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb of them|מֵהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb shall stand|יַעֲמֹ֥ד\rb* \rb against you|בְּפָנֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb After marching|עָלָ֖ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb night|הַלַּ֕יְלָה\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb Gilgal|הַגִּלְגָּֽל׃\rb*, \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb* \rb caught|וַיָּבֹ֧א\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb by surprise|פִּתְאֹ֑ם\rb*. \v 10 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb threw them into confusion|וַיְהֻמֵּ֤ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb who defeated them|וַיַּכֵּ֥ם\rb* \rb in a great|גְדוֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb slaughter|מַכָּֽה־\rb* \rb at Gibeon|בְּגִבְע֑וֹן\rb*, \rb pursued them|וַֽיִּרְדְּפֵ֗ם\rb* \rb along|דֶּ֚רֶךְ\rb* \rb the ascent|מַעֲלֵ֣ה\rb*\rb |בֵית־\rb* \rb to Beth-horon|חוֹרֹ֔ן\rb*, \rb and struck them down|וַיַּכֵּ֥ם\rb* \rb as|עַד־\rb* \rb far as Azekah|עֲזֵקָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְעַד־\rb* \rb and Makkedah|מַקֵּדָֽה׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb |וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb As they fled|בְּנֻסָ֣ם׀\rb* \rb before|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*\rb |הֵ֞ם\rb* \rb along the descent|בְּמוֹרַ֤ד\rb*\rb |בֵּית־\rb* \rb from Beth-horon|חוֹרֹן֙\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb Azekah|עֲזֵקָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֡ה\rb* \rb cast down|הִשְׁלִ֣יךְ\rb* \rb on them|עֲלֵיהֶם֩\rb* \rb large|גְּדֹל֧וֹת\rb* \rb hailstones|אֲבָנִ֨ים\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the sky|הַשָּׁמַ֛יִם\rb*,\rb |וַיָּמֻ֑תוּ\rb* \rb and more|רַבִּ֗ים\rb* \rb of them|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb were killed|מֵ֙תוּ֙\rb* \rb by|בְּאַבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the hailstones|הַבָּרָ֔ד\rb* \rb than|מֵאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |הָרְג֛וּ\rb* \rb by the swords|בֶּחָֽרֶב׃ס\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb |אָ֣ז\rb* \rb On the day that|בְּי֗וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb gave the Amorites|הָ֣אֱמֹרִ֔י\rb* \rb over|תֵּ֤ת\rb* \rb to|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*,\rb |וַיֹּ֣אמֶר׀\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁעַ֙\rb* \rb spoke|יְדַבֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in the presence|לְעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb O sun|שֶׁ֚מֶשׁ\rb*, \rb stand still|דּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb over Gibeon|בְּגִבְע֣וֹן\rb*,
\q2 \rb O moon|וְיָרֵ֖חַ\rb*, \rb over the Valley|בְּעֵ֥מֶק\rb* \rb of Aijalon|אַיָּלֽוֹן׃\rb*.”\f + \fr 10:12 \ft See \ref Jasher 88:63|88:63\ref*.\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb So the sun|הַשֶּׁ֜מֶשׁ\rb* \rb stood still|וַיִּדֹּ֨ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and the moon|וְיָרֵ֣חַ\rb* \rb stopped|עָמָ֗ד\rb*
\q1 \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the nation|גּוֹי֙\rb* \rb took vengeance|יִקֹּ֥ם\rb*
\q2 \rb upon its enemies|אֹֽיְבָ֔יו\rb*.\f + \fr 10:13 \ft Or \fqa triumphed over its enemies\f*
\p \rb Is this|הִ֥יא\rb* \rb not|הֲלֹא־\rb* \rb written|כְתוּבָ֖ה\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֣פֶר\rb* \rb of Jashar|הַיָּשָׁ֑ר\rb*?\f + \fr 10:13 \ft Or \fqa the Book of the Upright One\ft , commonly cited as \fqa Jasher\f*
\b 
\q1 “\rb So the sun|הַשֶּׁ֙מֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb stopped|וַיַּעֲמֹ֤ד\rb*
\q2 \rb in the middle|בַּחֲצִ֣י\rb* \rb of the sky|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb*
\q1 \rb and delayed|וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |אָ֥ץ\rb* \rb going down|לָב֖וֹא\rb*
\q2 \rb about a full|תָּמִֽים׃\rb* \rb day|כְּי֥וֹם\rb*.”\f + \fr 10:13 \ft See \ref Jasher 88:64|88:64\ref*.\f*
\p \v 14 \rb There has been|הָיָ֜ה\rb* \rb no|וְלֹ֨א\rb* \rb day|כַּיּ֤וֹם\rb*\rb |הַהוּא֙\rb* \rb like it before|לְפָנָ֣יו\rb* \rb or since|וְאַחֲרָ֔יו\rb*, \rb when the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb listened|לִשְׁמֹ֥עַ\rb* \rb to the voice|בְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of a man|אִ֑ישׁ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb fought|נִלְחָ֖ם\rb* \rb for Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Then Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּ֤שָׁב\rb* \rb with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל\rb*\rb |עִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb at Gilgal|הַגִּלְגָּֽלָה׃\rb*.
\s1 The Victory at Makkedah
\p \v 16 \rb Now the|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb five|חֲמֵ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb kings|הַמְּלָכִ֣ים\rb* \rb had fled|וַיָּנֻ֕סוּ\rb* \rb and hidden|וַיֵּחָבְא֥וּ\rb* \rb in the cave|בַמְּעָרָ֖ה\rb* \rb at Makkedah|בְּמַקֵּדָֽה׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb And Joshua|לִיהוֹשֻׁ֣עַ\rb* \rb was informed|וַיֻּגַּ֖ד\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*: “\rb The five|חֲמֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb kings|הַמְּלָכִ֔ים\rb* \rb have been found|נִמְצְאוּ֙\rb*; \rb they are hiding|נֶחְבְּאִ֥ים\rb* \rb in the cave|בַּמְּעָרָ֖ה\rb* \rb at Makkedah|בְּמַקֵּדָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 18 \rb So Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Roll|גֹּ֛לּוּ\rb* \rb large|גְּדֹל֖וֹת\rb* \rb stones|אֲבָנִ֥ים\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the mouth|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb of the cave|הַמְּעָרָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and post|וְהַפְקִ֧ידוּ\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb there|עָלֶ֛יהָ\rb* \rb to guard them|לְשָׁמְרָֽם׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb But you|וְאַתֶּם֙\rb*, \rb do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb stop there|תַּעֲמֹ֔דוּ\rb*. \rb Pursue|רִדְפוּ֙\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb your enemies|אֹֽיְבֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and attack them from behind|וְזִנַּבְתֶּ֖ם\rb*.\rb |אוֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb Do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb let them|תִּתְּנ֗וּם\rb* \rb reach|לָבוֹא֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb their cities|עָ֣רֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb has delivered them|נְתָנָ֛ם\rb* \rb into your hand|בְּיֶדְכֶֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 20 \rb |וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb So Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֜עַ\rb* \rb and the Israelites|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb continued|כְּכַלּ֨וֹת\rb* \rb to inflict|לְהַכּוֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb a terrible|גְדוֹלָֽה־\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֖ד\rb* \rb slaughter|מַכָּ֥ה\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb they had finished them off|תֻּמָּ֑ם\rb*, \rb and the remaining|וְהַשְּׂרִידִים֙\rb* \rb survivors|שָׂרְד֣וּ\rb*\rb |מֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb retreated|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the fortified|הַמִּבְצָֽר׃\rb* \rb cities|עָרֵ֥י\rb*. \v 21 \rb The whole|כָל־\rb* \rb army|הָעָ֨ם\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּשֻׁבוּ֩\rb* \rb safely|בְּשָׁל֑וֹם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֛עַ\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the camp|הַמַּחֲנֶ֧ה\rb* \rb at Makkedah|מַקֵּדָ֖ה\rb*, \rb and no one|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb dared to utter|חָרַ֞ץ\rb* \rb a word|לְשֹׁנֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb against|לְאִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |לִבְנֵ֧י\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb Then Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Open|פִּתְח֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the mouth|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb of the cave|הַמְּעָרָ֑ה\rb* \rb and bring those|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb five|חֲמֵ֛שֶׁת\rb* \rb kings|הַמְּלָכִ֥ים\rb* \rb out|מִן־\rb*\rb |הַמְּעָרָֽה׃\rb* \rb to|אֵלַ֗י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb me|וְהוֹצִ֣יאוּ\rb*.” \v 23 \rb So|כֵ֔ן\rb* \rb they|וַיַּ֣עֲשׂוּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֗יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb brought|וַיֹּצִ֣יאוּ\rb* \rb the|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb five|חֲמֵ֛שֶׁת\rb* \rb kings|הַמְּלָכִ֥ים\rb* \rb out of|מִן־\rb* \rb the cave|הַמְּעָרָ֑ה\rb* —\rb |אֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb the kings|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֗ם\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb Hebron|חֶבְרוֹן֙\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Jarmuth|יַרְמ֔וּת\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Lachish|לָכִ֖ישׁ\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb and Eglon|עֶגְלֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb |וַ֠יְהִי\rb* \rb When they had brought|כְּֽהוֹצִיאָ֞ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the|הָאֵלֶּה֮\rb* \rb kings|הַמְּלָכִ֣ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁעַ֒\rb*, \rb he|יְהוֹשֻׁ֜עַ\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֨א\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb and said|וַ֠יֹּאמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb*\rb |אַנְשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb the army|הַמִּלְחָמָה֙\rb* \rb commanders|קְצִינֵ֞י\rb* \rb who had accompanied|הֶהָלְכ֣וּא\rb* \rb him|אִתּ֔וֹ\rb*, “\rb Come|קִרְב֗וּ\rb* \rb here and put|שִׂ֚ימוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your feet|רַגְלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb on|עַֽל־\rb* \rb the necks|צַוְּארֵ֖י\rb* \rb of these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb kings|הַמְּלָכִ֣ים\rb*.”
\p \rb So the commanders came forward|וַֽיִּקְרְב֔וּ\rb* \rb and put|וַיָּשִׂ֥ימוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their feet|רַגְלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb their necks|צַוְּארֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 25 “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּֽירְא֖וּ\rb*\rb |וְאַל־\rb* \rb or discouraged|תֵּחָ֑תּוּ\rb*,” \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb*. “\rb Be strong|חִזְק֣וּ\rb* \rb and courageous|וְאִמְצ֔וּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb will do|יַעֲשֶׂ֤ה\rb* \rb this|כָ֗כָה\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the enemies|אֹ֣יְבֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb fight|נִלְחָמִ֥ים\rb*.”\rb |אוֹתָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb After|אַֽחֲרֵי־\rb* \rb this|כֵן֙\rb*, \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֤עַ\rb* \rb struck down|וַיַּכֵּ֨ם\rb* \rb and killed the kings|וַיְמִיתֵ֔ם\rb*, \rb and he hung|וַיִּתְלֵ֕ם\rb* \rb their bodies on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb five|חֲמִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb trees|עֵצִ֑ים\rb*\f + \fr 10:26 \ft Or \fqa impaled their bodies on five poles\ft ; similarly in verse 27\f* \rb and left them|וַיִּֽהְי֛וּ\rb*\rb |תְּלוּיִ֥ם\rb* \rb there|עַל־\rb*\rb |הָעֵצִ֖ים\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעָֽרֶב׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb |וַיְהִ֞י\rb*\rb |לְעֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb At sunset|בּ֣וֹא\rb*\rb |הַשֶּׁ֗מֶשׁ\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb ordered|צִוָּ֤ה\rb* \rb that they be taken down|וַיֹּֽרִידוּם֙\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the trees|הָעֵצִ֔ים\rb* \rb and thrown|וַיַּ֨שְׁלִכֻ֔ם\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the cave|הַמְּעָרָ֖ה\rb* \rb in which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they had hidden|נֶחְבְּאוּ־\rb*.\rb |שָׁ֑ם\rb* \rb Then large|גְּדֹלוֹת֙\rb* \rb stones|אֲבָנִ֤ים\rb* \rb were placed|וַיָּשִׂ֜מוּ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the mouth|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb of the cave|הַמְּעָרָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and the stones|עַד־\rb*\rb |עֶ֖צֶם\rb* \rb are there to this|הַזֶּֽה׃פ\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb On that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֜עַ\rb* \rb captured|לָכַ֨ד\rb* \rb Makkedah|מַקֵּדָה֩\rb* \rb and put it|וַיַּכֶּ֣הָ\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb to the sword|חֶרֶב֮\rb*, \rb along with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb its king|מַלְכָּהּ֒\rb*. \rb He devoted to destruction|הֶחֱרִ֣ם\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֗ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb everyone|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַנֶּ֙פֶשׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in the city|בָּ֔הּ\rb*, \rb leaving|הִשְׁאִ֖יר\rb* \rb no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb survivors|שָׂרִ֑יד\rb*. \rb So he did|וַיַּ֙עַשׂ֙\rb* \rb to the king|לְמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Makkedah|מַקֵּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had done|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb to the king|לְמֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Jericho|יְרִיחֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\s1 Conquest of the Southern Cities
\p \v 29 \rb Then Joshua|יְ֠הוֹשֻׁעַ\rb* \rb and all|וְכָֽל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb moved on|וַיַּעֲבֹ֣ר\rb* \rb from Makkedah|מִמַּקֵּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb to Libnah|לִבְנָ֑ה\rb* \rb and fought|וַיִּלָּ֖חֶם\rb* \rb against|עִם־\rb* \rb Libnah|לִבְנָֽה׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb also|גַּם־\rb* \rb delivered|וַיִּתֵּן֩\rb* \rb that city|אוֹתָ֜הּ\rb* \rb and its king|מַלְכָּהּ֒\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֘ל\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Joshua put|וַיַּכֶּ֣הָ\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הַנֶּ֙פֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb to the sword|חֶ֗רֶב\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb leaving|הִשְׁאִ֥יר\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb survivors|שָׂרִ֑יד\rb*. \rb And he did|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb to the king of Libnah|לְמַלְכָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had done|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb to the king|לְמֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Jericho|יְרִיחֽוֹ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb And Joshua|יְ֠הוֹשֻׁעַ\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb moved on|וַיַּעֲבֹ֣ר\rb* \rb from Libnah|מִלִּבְנָ֖ה\rb* \rb to Lachish|לָכִ֑ישָׁה\rb*. \rb They laid siege|וַיִּ֣חַן\rb* \rb to it|עָלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb and fought|וַיִּלָּ֖חֶם\rb* \rb against it|בָּֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 32 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb delivered|וַיִּתֵּן֩\rb* \rb Lachish|לָכִ֜ישׁ\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*, \rb and Joshua captured|וַֽיִּלְכְּדָהּ֙\rb* \rb it on the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֔י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*. \rb He put|וַיַּכֶּ֣הָ\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הַנֶּ֖פֶשׁ\rb* \rb to the sword|חֶ֔רֶב\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb just as|כְּכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he had done|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb to Libnah|לְלִבְנָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 33 \rb At that time|אָ֣ז\rb* \rb Horam|הֹרָם֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Gezer|גֶּ֔זֶר\rb* \rb went|עָלָ֗ה\rb* \rb to help|לַעְזֹ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Lachish|לָכִ֑ישׁ\rb*, \rb but Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֙עַ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb struck him down|וַיַּכֵּ֤הוּ\rb* \rb along with his people|עַמּ֔וֹ\rb*,\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb leaving|הִשְׁאִֽיר־\rb* \rb no|בִּלְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb survivors|שָׂרִֽיד׃\rb*.
\p \v 34 \rb So Joshua|יְ֠הוֹשֻׁעַ\rb* \rb moved on|וַיַּעֲבֹ֣ר\rb* \rb from Lachish|מִלָּכִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb to Eglon|עֶגְלֹ֑נָה\rb*, \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֛וֹ\rb*. \rb They laid siege|וַיַּחֲנ֣וּ\rb* \rb to it|עָלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb and fought|וַיִּֽלָּחֲמ֖וּ\rb* \rb against it|עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*. \v 35 \rb That|הַהוּא֙\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֤וֹם\rb* \rb they captured Eglon|וַֽיִּלְכְּד֜וּהָ\rb* \rb and put it|וַיַּכּ֣וּהָ\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb to the sword|חֶ֔רֶב\rb*, \rb and|וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb Joshua devoted to destruction|הֶחֱרִ֑ים\rb* \rb everyone|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַנֶּ֣פֶשׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in the city|בָּ֔הּ\rb*\rb |הַה֖וּא\rb*\rb |בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*, \rb just as|כְּכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he had done|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb to Lachish|לְלָכִֽישׁ׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 36 \rb Then Joshua|יְ֠הוֹשֻׁעַ\rb* \rb and all|וְכָֽל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb from Eglon|מֵעֶגְל֖וֹנָה\rb* \rb to Hebron|חֶבְר֑וֹנָה\rb* \rb and fought|וַיִּֽלָּחֲמ֖וּ\rb* \rb against it|עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*. \v 37 \rb They captured it|וַיִּלְכְּד֣וּהָ\rb* \rb and put|וַיַּכּֽוּהָ־\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb to the sword|חֶ֠רֶב\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb its king|מַלְכָּ֨הּ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its villages|עָרֶ֜יהָ\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הַנֶּ֤פֶשׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |בָּהּ֙\rb*. \rb Joshua left|הִשְׁאִ֣יר\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb survivors|שָׂרִ֔יד\rb*, \rb just as|כְּכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he had done|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb at Eglon|לְעֶגְל֑וֹן\rb*; \rb he devoted to destruction|וַיַּחֲרֵ֣ם\rb* \rb Hebron|אוֹתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb everyone|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַנֶּ֖פֶשׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in it|בָּֽהּ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 38 \rb Finally Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֛עַ\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb turned|וַיָּ֧שָׁב\rb* \rb toward Debir|דְּבִ֑רָה\rb* \rb and fought|וַיִּלָּ֖חֶם\rb* \rb against it|עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*. \v 39 \rb And they captured Debir|וַֽיִּלְכְּדָ֞הּ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb its king|מַלְכָּ֤הּ\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its villages|עָרֶ֙יהָ֙\rb*. \rb They put them|וַיַּכּ֣וּם\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb to the sword|חֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb and devoted to destruction|וַֽיַּחֲרִ֙ימוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb everyone|כָּל־\rb*\rb |נֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in the city|בָּ֔הּ\rb*, \rb leaving|הִשְׁאִ֖יר\rb* \rb no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb survivors|שָׂרִ֑יד\rb*. \rb Joshua did to|עָשָׂ֜ה\rb* \rb Debir|לִדְבִ֙רָה֙\rb* \rb and its king|וּלְמַלְכָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb as|וְכַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had done|עָשָׂ֤ה\rb* \rb to Hebron|לְחֶבְר֗וֹן\rb* \rb and as|כֵּן־\rb* \rb he had done|עָשָׂ֛ה\rb* \rb to Libnah|לְלִבְנָ֖ה\rb* \rb and its king|וּלְמַלְכָּֽהּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 40 \rb So Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֣עַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb conquered|וַיַּכֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb region|הָאָ֡רֶץ\rb*— \rb the hill country|הָהָר֩\rb*, \rb the Negev|וְהַנֶּ֨גֶב\rb*, \rb the foothills|וְהַשְּׁפֵלָ֜ה\rb*,\f + \fr 10:40 \ft Hebrew \fqa Shephelah \ft or \fqa lowlands\ft ; that is, the western foothills of Judea\f* \rb and the slopes|וְהָאֲשֵׁד֗וֹת\rb*, \rb together with|וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb their kings|מַלְכֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*— \rb leaving|הִשְׁאִ֖יר\rb* \rb no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb survivors|שָׂרִ֑יד\rb*.\rb |וְאֵ֤ת\rb* \rb He devoted to destruction|הֶחֱרִ֔ים\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb* \rb that breathed|הַנְּשָׁמָה֙\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*, \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֔ה\rb*. \v 41 \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֛עַ\rb* \rb conquered the area|וַיַּכֵּ֧ם\rb* \rb from|מִקָּדֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb Kadesh-barnea|בַּרְנֵ֖עַ\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb Gaza|עַזָּ֑ה\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb and the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb region|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Goshen|גֹּ֖שֶׁן\rb* \rb as far as|וְעַד־\rb* \rb Gibeon|גִּבְעֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\p \v 42 \rb And|וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb because|כִּ֗י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb fought|נִלְחָ֖ם\rb* \rb for Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*, \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb* \rb captured|לָכַ֥ד\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb kings|הַמְּלָכִ֤ים\rb* \rb and their land|אַרְצָ֔ם\rb* \rb in one|אֶחָ֑ת\rb* \rb campaign|פַּ֣עַם\rb*. \v 43 \rb Then Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּ֤שָׁב\rb* \rb with|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb at Gilgal|הַגִּלְגָּֽלָה׃פ\rb*.
\c 11
\s1 Conquest of the Northern Cities
\p \v 1 \rb Now when|וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb Jabin|יָבִ֣ין\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Hazor|חָצ֑וֹר\rb* \rb heard about these things|כִּשְׁמֹ֖עַ\rb*, \rb he sent word|וַיִּשְׁלַ֗ח\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jobab|יוֹבָב֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Madon|מָד֔וֹן\rb*; \rb to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the kings|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Shimron|שִׁמְר֖וֹן\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb*\rb |מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb and Achshaph|אַכְשָֽׁף׃\rb*; \v 2 \rb to|וְֽאֶל־\rb* \rb the kings|הַמְּלָכִ֞ים\rb* \rb of the north|מִצְּפ֗וֹן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in the mountains|בָּהָ֧ר\rb*, \rb in the Arabah|וּבָעֲרָבָ֛ה\rb* \rb south|נֶ֥גֶב\rb* \rb of Chinnereth|כִּֽנֲר֖וֹת\rb*, \rb in the foothills|וּבַשְּׁפֵלָ֑ה\rb*,\f + \fr 11:2 \ft Hebrew \fqa Shephelah \ft or \fqa lowlands\ft ; that is, the western foothills of Judea; also in verse 16\f* \rb and in Naphoth-dor|וּבְנָפ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |דּ֖וֹר\rb*\f + \fr 11:2 \ft Or \fqa in the heights of Dor\ft ; \fqa Naphoth-dor \ft is a variant of \fqa Naphath-dor\ft ; see \ref Joshua 12:23|JOS 12:23\ref*.\f* \rb to the west|מִיָּֽם׃\rb*; \v 3 \rb to the Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִי֙\rb* \rb in the east|מִמִּזְרָ֣ח\rb* \rb and west|וּמִיָּ֔ם\rb*; \rb to the Amorites|וְהָאֱמֹרִ֧י\rb*, \rb Hittites|וְהַחִתִּ֛י\rb*, \rb Perizzites|וְהַפְּרִזִּ֥י\rb*, \rb and Jebusites|וְהַיְבוּסִ֖י\rb* \rb in the hill country|בָּהָ֑ר\rb*; \rb and to the Hivites|וְהַֽחִוִּי֙\rb* \rb at the foot of|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb Hermon|חֶרְמ֔וֹן\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb of Mizpah|הַמִּצְפָּֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb So these kings|הֵ֗ם\rb* \rb came out|וַיֵּצְא֣וּ\rb* \rb with|עִמָּ֔ם\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb their armies|מַֽחֲנֵיהֶם֙\rb*, \rb a multitude|עַם־\rb* \rb as numerous|רָ֕ב\rb* \rb as the sand|כַּח֛וֹל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the seashore|שְׂפַת־\rb*\rb |הַיָּ֖ם\rb*, \rb along with a great number|רַב־\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb of horses|וְס֥וּס\rb* \rb and chariots|וָרֶ֖כֶב\rb*. \v 5 \rb All|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb kings|הַמְּלָכִ֣ים\rb* \rb joined forces|וַיִּוָּ֣עֲד֔וּ\rb*\rb |וַיָּבֹ֜אוּ\rb* \rb and encamped|וַיַּחֲנ֤וּ\rb*\rb |יַחְדָּו֙\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the waters|מֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Merom|מֵר֔וֹם\rb* \rb to fight|לְהִלָּחֵ֖ם\rb* \rb against|עִם־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁעַ֮\rb*, “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָ֣א\rb* \rb of them|מִפְּנֵיהֶם֒\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb by this|הַזֹּ֗את\rb* \rb time|כָּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb tomorrow|מָחָ֞ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֞י\rb* \rb will deliver|נֹתֵ֧ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all of them|כֻּלָּ֛ם\rb* \rb slain|חֲלָלִ֖ים\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb You are to hamstring|תְּעַקֵּ֔ר\rb* \rb their horses|סוּסֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb burn up|תִּשְׂרֹ֥ף\rb*\rb |בָּאֵֽשׁ׃\rb* \rb their chariots|מַרְכְּבֹתֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb So by|עַל־\rb* \rb the waters|מֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Merom|מֵר֖וֹם\rb*, \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֡עַ\rb* \rb and his whole|וְכָל־\rb* \rb army|הַמִּלְחָמָ֨ה\rb*\rb |עִמּ֧וֹ\rb*\rb |עַם֩\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb upon them|עֲלֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb suddenly|פִּתְאֹ֑ם\rb* \rb and attacked|וַֽיִּפְּל֖וּ\rb* \rb them|בָּהֶֽם׃\rb*, \v 8 \rb and the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb delivered them|וַיִּתְּנֵ֨ם\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַֽד־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֮\rb*, \rb who struck them down|וַיַּכּוּם֒\rb* \rb and pursued them|וַֽיִּרְדְּפ֞וּם\rb* \rb all the way to|עַד־\rb* \rb Greater|רַבָּ֗ה\rb* \rb Sidon|צִיד֣וֹן\rb* \rb and Misrephoth-maim|מַ֔יִם\rb*, \rb and eastward|מִזְרָ֑חָה\rb* \rb as far as|וְעַד֙\rb*\rb |מִשְׂרְפ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |וְעַד־\rb* \rb the Valley|בִּקְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Mizpeh|מִצְפֶּ֖ה\rb*. \rb They struck them down|וַיַּכֻּ֕ם\rb*,\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb leaving|הִשְׁאִֽיר־\rb* \rb no|בִּלְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb survivors|שָׂרִֽיד׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb* \rb treated|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb them|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had told|אָֽמַר־\rb* \rb him|ל֖וֹ\rb*; \rb he hamstrung|עִקֵּ֔ר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb their horses|סוּסֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb and burned up|שָׂרַ֥ף\rb*\rb |בָּאֵֽשׁ׃ס\rb* \rb their chariots|מַרְכְּבֹתֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb At that|הַהִיא֙\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֤ת\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֜עַ\rb* \rb turned back|וַיָּ֨שָׁב\rb* \rb and captured|וַיִּלְכֹּ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Hazor|חָצ֔וֹר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and put|הִכָּ֣ה\rb* \rb its king|מַלְכָּ֖הּ\rb* \rb to the sword|בֶחָ֑רֶב\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Hazor|חָצ֣וֹר\rb* \rb was|הִ֕יא\rb* \rb formerly|לְפָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb the head|רֹ֖אשׁ\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb kingdoms|הַמַּמְלָכ֥וֹת\rb*. \v 11 \rb The Israelites put|וַ֠יַּכּוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb everyone|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַנֶּ֨פֶשׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in Hazor|בָּ֤הּ\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb to the sword|חֶ֙רֶב֙\rb*, \rb devoting them to destruction|הַֽחֲרֵ֔ם\rb*.\f + \fr 11:11 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering; also in verses 12, 20, and 21.\f* \rb Nothing|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb that breathed|נְשָׁמָ֑ה\rb* \rb remained|נוֹתַ֖ר\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Joshua burned down|שָׂרַ֥ף\rb*\rb |בָּאֵֽשׁ׃\rb* \rb Hazor itself|חָצ֖וֹר\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb |וְֽאֶת־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֛עַ\rb* \rb captured|לָכַ֧ד\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָ֠אֵלֶּה\rb*\rb |וְֽאֶת־\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |מַלְכֵיהֶ֞ם\rb* \rb kings|הַמְּלָכִֽים־\rb* \rb and their cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb and put them|וַיַּכֵּ֥ם\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb to the sword|חֶ֖רֶב\rb*. \rb He devoted them to destruction|הֶחֱרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֑ם\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb servant|עֶ֥בֶד\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֔ה\rb*. \v 13 \rb Yet|רַ֣ק\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb burn|שְׂרָפָ֖ם\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb of the cities|הֶעָרִ֗ים\rb* \rb built|הָעֹֽמְדוֹת֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb their mounds|תִּלָּ֔ם\rb*, \rb except|זוּלָתִ֛י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Hazor|חָצ֥וֹר\rb*,\rb |לְבַדָּ֖הּ\rb* \rb which Joshua|יְהוֹשֻֽׁעַ׃\rb* \rb burned|שָׂרַ֥ף\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb The Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb took for themselves|בָּזְז֥וּ\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb all|וְ֠כֹל\rb* \rb the plunder|שְׁלַ֞ל\rb* \rb and livestock|וְהַבְּהֵמָ֔ה\rb* \rb of these|הָאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb cities|הֶעָרִ֤ים\rb*, \rb but|רַ֣ק\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb they put|הִכּ֣וּ\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָאָדָ֞ם\rb* \rb to the sword|חֶ֗רֶב\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb they had completely destroyed them|הִשְׁמִדָם֙\rb*,\rb |אוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb not sparing anyone|הִשְׁאִ֖ירוּ\rb* \rb who breathed|נְשָׁמָֽה׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb As|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֤ה\rb* \rb His servant|עַבְדּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb*, \rb so|כֵּן־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֑עַ\rb*. \rb That is what|וְכֵן֙\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb* \rb did|עָשָׂ֣ה\rb*, \rb leaving nothing|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |דָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb undone|הֵסִ֣יר\rb* \rb of all|מִכֹּ֛ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb*.
\s1 Joshua Takes the Whole Land
\p \v 16 \rb So Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֜עַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֗את\rb* \rb entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb region|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb*: \rb the hill country|הָהָ֤ר\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Negev|הַנֶּ֙גֶב֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Goshen|הַגֹּ֔שֶׁן\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the western foothills|הַשְּׁפֵלָ֖ה\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Arabah|הָעֲרָבָ֑ה\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the mountains|הַ֥ר\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and their foothills|וּשְׁפֵלָתֹֽה׃\rb*, \v 17 \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb Mount|הָהָ֤ר\rb* \rb Halak|הֶֽחָלָק֙\rb*, \rb which rises|הָעוֹלֶ֣ה\rb* \rb toward Seir|שֵׂעִ֔יר\rb*, \rb as far as|וְעַד־\rb*\rb |בַּ֤עַל\rb* \rb Baal-gad|גָּד֙\rb* \rb in the Valley|בְּבִקְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Lebanon|הַלְּבָנ֔וֹן\rb* \rb at the foot of|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb Mount|הַר־\rb* \rb Hermon|חֶרְמ֑וֹן\rb*.\rb |וְאֵ֤ת\rb* \rb He captured|לָכַ֔ד\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb their kings|מַלְכֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb and struck them down|וַיַּכֵּ֖ם\rb*, \rb putting them to death|וַיְמִיתֵֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֛עַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb waged|עָשָׂ֧ה\rb* \rb war|מִלְחָמָֽה׃\rb* \rb against all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb kings|הַמְּלָכִ֥ים\rb* \rb for a long period|רַבִּ֗ים\rb* \rb of time|יָמִ֣ים\rb*. \v 19 \rb No|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |הָיְתָ֣ה\rb* \rb city|עִ֗יר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb made peace|הִשְׁלִ֙ימָה֙\rb* \rb with|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb except|בִּלְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb the Hivites|הַחִוִּ֖י\rb* \rb living|יֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb in Gibeon|גִבְע֑וֹן\rb*;\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|הַכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb others were taken|לָקְח֥וּ\rb* \rb in battle|בַמִּלְחָמָֽה׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb it was|הָיְתָ֡ה\rb* \rb of|מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb to harden|לְחַזֵּ֣ק\rb*\f + \fr 11:20 \ft Or \fqa stiffen \ft or \fqa strengthen\f*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their hearts|לִבָּם֩\rb* \rb to engage|לִקְרַ֨את\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*\rb |לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb in battle|הַמִּלְחָמָ֤ה\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb so that they would be set apart for destruction|הַֽחֲרִימָ֔ם\rb* \rb and would receive|הֱיוֹת־\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb no|לְבִלְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb mercy|תְּחִנָּ֑ה\rb*,\rb |כִּ֚י\rb*\rb |לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb being annihilated|הַשְׁמִידָ֔ם\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶֽׁה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb At that|הַהִ֗יא\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֜עַ\rb* \rb proceeded|וַיָּבֹ֨א\rb* \rb to eliminate|וַיַּכְרֵ֤ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Anakim|הָֽעֲנָקִים֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the hill country|הָהָ֤ר\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb of Hebron|חֶבְרוֹן֙\rb*,\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb Debir|דְּבִ֣ר\rb*,\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb and Anab|עֲנָ֔ב\rb*, \rb and from all|וּמִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb the hill country|הַ֣ר\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וּמִכֹּ֖ל\rb*\rb |הַ֣ר\rb* \rb and of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻֽׁעַ׃\rb* \rb devoted them to destruction|הֶחֱרִימָ֥ם\rb*, \rb along with|עִם־\rb* \rb their cities|עָרֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*. \v 22 \rb No|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb Anakim|עֲנָקִ֔ים\rb* \rb were left|נוֹתַ֣ר\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֖רֶץ\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*; \rb only|רַ֗ק\rb* \rb in Gaza|בְּעַזָּ֛ה\rb*, \rb Gath|בְּגַ֥ת\rb*, \rb and Ashdod|וּבְאַשְׁדּ֖וֹד\rb* \rb did any survive|נִשְׁאָֽרוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb So Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֜עַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb the entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb*, \rb in keeping with all|כְּ֠כֹל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb had spoken|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb to Moses|מֹשֶׁה֒\rb*. \rb And Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֨עַ\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתְּנָהּ֩\rb* \rb it as an inheritance|לְנַחֲלָ֧ה\rb* \rb to Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb according to the allotments|כְּמַחְלְקֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb to their tribes|לְשִׁבְטֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Then the land|וְהָאָ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb had rest|שָׁקְטָ֖ה\rb* \rb from war|מִמִּלְחָמָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\c 12
\s1 The Kings Defeated East of the Jordan
\p \v 1 \rb Now these are|וְאֵ֣לֶּה׀\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb whom the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb struck down|הִכּ֤וּ\rb* \rb and whose|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb lands|אַרְצָ֔ם\rb* \rb they took|וַיִּֽרְשׁ֣וּ\rb* \rb beyond|בְּעֵ֥בֶר\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb to the east|מִזְרְחָ֣ה\rb*\rb |הַשָּׁ֑מֶשׁ\rb*, \rb from the Arnon|אַרְנוֹן֙\rb* \rb Valley|מִנַּ֤חַל\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb Mount|הַ֣ר\rb* \rb Hermon|חֶרְמ֔וֹן\rb*, \rb including all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the Arabah|הָעֲרָבָ֖ה\rb* \rb eastward|מִזְרָֽחָה׃\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \v 2 \rb Sihon|סִיחוֹן֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of the Amorites|הָאֱמֹרִ֔י\rb*, \rb who lived|הַיּוֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb in Heshbon|בְּחֶשְׁבּ֑וֹן\rb*. \rb He ruled|מֹשֵׁ֡ל\rb* \rb from Aroer|מֵעֲרוֹעֵ֡ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the rim|שְׂפַת־\rb* \rb of the Arnon|אַרְנ֜וֹן\rb* \rb Valley|נַ֨חַל\rb*, \rb along the middle|וְת֤וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the valley|הַנַּ֙חַל֙\rb*, \rb up to|וְעַד֙\rb* \rb the Jabbok|יַבֹּ֣ק\rb* \rb River|הַנַּ֔חַל\rb* (\rb the border|גְּב֖וּל\rb* \rb of the|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Ammonites|עַמּֽוֹן׃\rb*), \rb that is, half|וַחֲצִ֣י\rb* \rb of Gilead|הַגִּלְעָ֔ד\rb*, \v 3 \rb as well as the Arabah|וְהָעֲרָבָה֩\rb* \rb east|מִזְרָ֗חָה\rb*\rb |וְ֠עַד\rb* \rb of the Sea|יָ֨ם\rb* \rb of Chinnereth|כִּנְר֜וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 12:3 \ft That is, the Sea of Galilee\f* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the Sea|יָ֣ם\rb* \rb of the Arabah|הָעֲרָבָ֤ה\rb* \rb (the Salt Sea|יָם־\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֙לַח֙\rb*\f + \fr 12:3 \ft That is, the Dead Sea\f*), \rb eastward|מִזְרָ֔חָה\rb* \rb through|דֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb Beth-jeshimoth|הַיְשִׁמ֑וֹת\rb*, \rb and southward|וּמִ֨תֵּימָ֔ן\rb* \rb below|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb the slopes|אַשְׁדּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of Pisgah|הַפִּסְגָּֽה׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 4 \rb And|וּגְב֗וּל\rb* \rb Og|ע֚וֹג\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Bashan|הַבָּשָׁ֔ן\rb*,\f + \fr 12:4 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa And the territory of Og king of Bashan\f* \rb one of the remnant|מִיֶּ֖תֶר\rb* \rb of the Rephaim|הָרְפָאִ֑ים\rb*, \rb who lived|הַיּוֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb in Ashtaroth|בְּעַשְׁתָּר֖וֹת\rb* \rb and Edrei|וּבְאֶדְרֶֽעִי׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb He ruled|וּ֠מֹשֵׁל\rb* \rb over Mount|בְּהַ֨ר\rb* \rb Hermon|חֶרְמ֤וֹן\rb*, \rb Salecah|וּבְסַלְכָה֙\rb*, \rb all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb of Bashan|הַבָּשָׁ֔ן\rb* \rb up to|עַד־\rb* \rb the border|גְּב֥וּל\rb* \rb of the Geshurites|הַגְּשׁוּרִ֖י\rb* \rb and Maacathites|וְהַמַּעֲכָתִ֑י\rb*, \rb and half|וַחֲצִי֙\rb* \rb of Gilead|הַגִּלְעָ֔ד\rb* \rb to the border|גְּב֖וּל\rb* \rb of Sihon|סִיח֥וֹן\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Heshbon|חֶשְׁבּֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֧ה\rb*, \rb the servant|עֶֽבֶד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*, \rb and the Israelites|וּבְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb had struck them down|הִכּ֑וּם\rb* \rb and|מֹשֶׁ֨ה\rb* \rb given|וַֽ֠יִּתְּנָהּ\rb* \rb their land as an inheritance|יְרֻשָּׁ֗ה\rb* \rb to the Reubenites|לָרֻֽאוּבֵנִי֙\rb*, \rb the Gadites|וְלַגָּדִ֔י\rb*, \rb and the half-tribe|וְלַחֲצִ֖י\rb*\rb |שֵׁ֥בֶט\rb* \rb of Manasseh|הַֽמְנַשֶּֽׁה׃ס\rb*.
\s1 The Kings Defeated West of the Jordan
\p \v 7 \rb And these are|וְאֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֡רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֜עַ\rb* \rb and the Israelites|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb conquered|הִכָּ֨ה\rb* \rb beyond|בְּעֵ֤בֶר\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּן֙\rb* \rb to the west|יָ֔מָּה\rb*,\rb |מִבַּ֤עַל\rb* \rb from Baal-gad|גָּד֙\rb* \rb in the Valley|בְּבִקְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Lebanon|הַלְּבָנ֔וֹן\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb Mount|הָהָ֥ר\rb* \rb Halak|הֶחָלָ֖ק\rb*, \rb which rises|הָעֹלֶ֣ה\rb* \rb toward Seir|שֵׂעִ֑ירָה\rb* (\rb according to the allotments|כְּמַחְלְקֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb to the tribes|לְשִׁבְטֵ֧י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb*, \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֜עַ\rb* \rb gave them|וַיִּתְּנָ֨הּ\rb* \rb as an inheritance|יְרֻשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \v 8 \rb the hill country|בָּהָ֣ר\rb*, \rb the foothills|וּבַשְּׁפֵלָ֗ה\rb*,\f + \fr 12:8 \ft Hebrew \fqa Shephelah \ft or \fqa lowlands\ft ; that is, the western foothills of Judea\f* \rb the Arabah|וּבָֽעֲרָבָה֙\rb*, \rb the slopes|וּבָ֣אֲשֵׁד֔וֹת\rb*, \rb the wilderness|וּבַמִּדְבָּ֖ר\rb*, \rb and the Negev|וּבַנֶּ֑גֶב\rb* — \rb the lands of the Hittites|הַֽחִתִּי֙\rb*, \rb Amorites|הָֽאֱמֹרִ֔י\rb*, \rb Canaanites|וְהַֽכְּנַעֲנִי֙\rb*, \rb Perizzites|הַפְּרִזִּ֔י\rb*, \rb Hivites|הַחִוִּ֖י\rb*, \rb and Jebusites|וְהַיְבוּסִֽי׃פ\rb*):
\b 
\li1 \v 9 \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Jericho|יְרִיח֖וֹ\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֑ד\rb*;
\li1 \rb the king|מֶ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Ai|הָעַ֛י\rb*, \rb which is|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb near|מִצַּ֥ד\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel|אֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 10 \rb the king|מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֔ד\rb*;
\li1 \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Hebron|חֶבְר֖וֹן\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 11 \rb the king|מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Jarmuth|יַרְמוּת֙\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֔ד\rb*;
\li1 \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Lachish|לָכִ֖ישׁ\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 12 \rb the king|מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Eglon|עֶגְלוֹן֙\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֔ד\rb*;
\li1 \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Gezer|גֶּ֖זֶר\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 13 \rb the king|מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Debir|דְּבִר֙\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֔ד\rb*;
\li1 \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Geder|גֶּ֖דֶר\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 14 \rb the king|מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Hormah|חָרְמָה֙\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֔ד\rb*;
\li1 \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Arad|עֲרָ֖ד\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 15 \rb the king|מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Libnah|לִבְנָה֙\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֔ד\rb*;
\li1 \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Adullam|עֲדֻלָּ֖ם\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 16 \rb the king|מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Makkedah|מַקֵּדָה֙\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֔ד\rb*;
\li1 \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Bethel|אֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 17 \rb the king|מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Tappuah|תַּפּ֙וּחַ֙\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֔ד\rb*;
\li1 \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Hepher|חֵ֖פֶר\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 18 \rb the king|מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Aphek|אֲפֵק֙\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֔ד\rb*;
\li1 \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Lasharon|לַשָּׁר֖וֹן\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 19 \rb the king|מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Madon|מָדוֹן֙\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֔ד\rb*;
\li1 \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Hazor|חָצ֖וֹר\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 20 \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb*\rb |שִׁמְר֤וֹן\rb* \rb of Shimron-meron|מְראוֹן֙\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֔ד\rb*;
\li1 \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Achshaph|אַכְשָׁ֖ף\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 21 \rb the king|מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Taanach|תַּעְנַךְ֙\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֔ד\rb*;
\li1 \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Megiddo|מְגִדּ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 22 \rb the king|מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Kedesh|קֶ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֔ד\rb*;
\li1 \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Jokneam|יָקְנֳעָ֥ם\rb* \rb in Carmel|לַכַּרְמֶ֖ל\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 23 \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Dor|דּ֛וֹר\rb*\rb |לְנָפַ֥ת\rb* \rb in Naphath-dor|דּ֖וֹר\rb*,\f + \fr 12:23 \ft Or \fqa in the heights of Dor\ft ; \fqa Naphath-dor \ft is a variant of \fqa Naphoth-dor\ft ; see \ref Joshua 11:2|JOS 11:2\ref*.\f* \rb one|אֶחָ֑ד\rb*;
\li1 \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Goiim|גּוֹיִ֥ם\rb* \rb in Gilgal|לְגִלְגָּ֖ל\rb*,\f + \fr 12:23 \ft Hebrew; LXX \fqa Goyim in Galilee\f* \rb one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 24 \rb and the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Tirzah|תִּרְצָ֖ה\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֑ד\rb*.
\p \rb So there were thirty-one|שְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb kings|מְלָכִ֖ים\rb* \rb in all|כָּל־\rb*.
\c 13
\s1 Lands Yet Unconquered
\r (\ref Judges 1:1–7|JDG 1:1-7\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Now Joshua|וִיהוֹשֻׁ֣עַ\rb* \rb was old|זָקֵ֔ן\rb* \rb and well along|בָּ֖א\rb* \rb in years|בַּיָּמִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֗יו\rb*, “\rb You|אַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb are old|זָקַ֙נְתָּה֙\rb* \rb and well along|בָּ֣אתָ\rb* \rb in years|בַיָּמִ֔ים\rb*, \rb but very|מְאֹ֖ד\rb* \rb much|הַרְבֵּֽה־\rb* \rb of the land|וְהָאָ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb remains|נִשְׁאֲרָ֥ה\rb* \rb to be possessed|לְרִשְׁתָּֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb This|זֹ֥את\rb* \rb is the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb that remains|הַנִּשְׁאָ֑רֶת\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb the territory|גְּלִיל֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the Philistines|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְכָל־\rb* \rb and the Geshurites|הַגְּשׁוּרִֽי׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb from|מִֽן־\rb* \rb the Shihor|הַשִּׁיח֞וֹר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר׀\rb* \rb east|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֗יִם\rb* \rb to|וְעַ֨ד\rb* \rb the territory|גְּב֤וּל\rb* \rb of Ekron|עֶקְרוֹן֙\rb* \rb on the north|צָפ֔וֹנָה\rb* \rb (considered|תֵּחָשֵׁ֑ב\rb* \rb to be Canaanite territory)|לַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֖י\rb*— \rb that of the five|חֲמֵ֣שֶׁת׀\rb* \rb Philistine|פְלִשְׁתִּ֗ים\rb* \rb rulers|סַרְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Gaza|הָעַזָּתִ֤י\rb*, \rb Ashdod|וְהָאַשְׁדּוֹדִי֙\rb*, \rb Ashkelon|הָאֶשְׁקְלוֹנִ֣י\rb*, \rb Gath|הַגִּתִּ֔י\rb*, \rb and Ekron|וְהָעֶקְרוֹנִ֖י\rb*, \rb as well as that of the Avvites|וְהָעַוִּֽים׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 4 \rb to the south|מִתֵּימָ֞ן\rb*, \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֗י\rb*, \rb from Mearah|וּמְעָרָ֛ה\rb*\f + \fr 13:4 \ft Or \fqa Arah\f* \rb of|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the Sidonians|לַצִּידֹנִ֖ים\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb Aphek|אֲפֵ֑קָה\rb*, \rb as far as|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb the border|גְּב֥וּל\rb* \rb of the Amorites|הָאֱמֹרִֽי׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 5 \rb the land|וְהָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Gebalites|הַגִּבְלִ֗י\rb*;\f + \fr 13:5 \ft Or \fqa the area of Byblos\f*
\li1 \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Lebanon|הַלְּבָנוֹן֙\rb* \rb to the east|מִזְרַ֣ח\rb*\rb |הַשֶּׁ֔מֶשׁ\rb*,\rb |מִבַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb from Baal-gad|גָּ֔ד\rb* \rb below|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb Mount|הַר־\rb* \rb Hermon|חֶרְמ֑וֹן\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb*\rb |לְב֥וֹא\rb* \rb Lebo-hamath|חֲמָֽת׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb the inhabitants|יֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the hill country|הָ֠הָר\rb* \rb from|מִֽן־\rb* \rb Lebanon|הַלְּבָנ֞וֹן\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb*\rb |מִשְׂרְפֹ֥ת\rb* \rb Misrephoth-maim|מַ֙יִם֙\rb* — \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Sidonians|צִ֣ידֹנִ֔ים\rb* — \rb I Myself|אָֽנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb will drive out|אוֹרִישֵׁ֔ם\rb* \rb before|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb Be sure to|רַ֠ק\rb* \rb divide it by lot|הַפִּלֶ֤הָ\rb* \rb as an inheritance|בְּֽנַחֲלָ֔ה\rb* \rb to Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb I have commanded you|צִוִּיתִֽיךָ׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb Now therefore|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb divide|חַלֵּ֞ק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֛את\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֧רֶץ\rb* \rb as an inheritance|בְּנַחֲלָ֖ה\rb* \rb to the nine|לְתִשְׁעַ֣ת\rb* \rb tribes|הַשְּׁבָטִ֑ים\rb* \rb and the half-tribe|וַחֲצִ֖י\rb*\rb |הַשֵּׁ֥בֶט\rb* \rb of Manasseh|הַֽמְנַשֶּֽׁה׃\rb*.”
\s1 The Inheritance East of the Jordan
\r (\ref Numbers 32:1–42|NUM 32:1-42\ref*; \ref Deuteronomy 3:12–22|DEU 3:12-22\ref*)
\p \v 8 \rb The other half of Manasseh|עִמּ֗וֹ\rb*, \rb along with the Reubenites|הָרֽאוּבֵנִי֙\rb* \rb and Gadites|וְהַגָּדִ֔י\rb*, \rb had received|לָקְח֖וּ\rb* \rb the inheritance|נַחֲלָתָ֑ם\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb had given|נָתַ֨ן\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb beyond|בְּעֵ֤בֶר\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּן֙\rb* \rb to the east|מִזְרָ֔חָה\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb the servant|עֶ֥בֶד\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb had assigned|נָתַ֣ן\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \v 9 \rb The area from Aroer|מֵעֲרוֹעֵ֡ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the rim|שְׂפַת־\rb* \rb of the Arnon|אַרְנ֜וֹן\rb* \rb Valley|נַ֨חַל\rb*, \rb along with the city|וְהָעִ֨יר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb in the middle|בְּתוֹךְ־\rb* \rb of the valley|הַנַּ֛חַל\rb*, \rb the whole|וְכָל־\rb* \rb plateau|הַמִּישֹׁ֥ר\rb* \rb of Medeba|מֵידְבָ֖א\rb* \rb as|עַד־\rb* \rb far as Dibon|דִּיבֽוֹן׃\rb*, \v 10 \rb and all|וְכֹ֗ל\rb* \rb the cities|עָרֵי֙\rb* \rb of Sihon|סִיחוֹן֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of the Amorites|הָאֱמֹרִ֔י\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Heshbon|בְּחֶשְׁבּ֑וֹן\rb*, \rb as far as|עַד־\rb* \rb the border|גְּב֖וּל\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |עַמּֽוֹן׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 11 \rb also Gilead|וְהַגִּלְעָ֞ד\rb* \rb and the territory|וּגְב֧וּל\rb* \rb of the Geshurites|הַגְּשׁוּרִ֣י\rb* \rb and Maacathites|וְהַמַּעֲכָתִ֗י\rb*, \rb all|וְכֹ֨ל\rb* \rb of Mount|הַ֥ר\rb* \rb Hermon|חֶרְמ֛וֹן\rb*, \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Bashan|הַבָּשָׁ֖ן\rb* \rb as far as|עַד־\rb* \rb Salecah|סַלְכָֽה׃\rb*— \v 12 \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb kingdom|מַמְלְכ֥וּת\rb* \rb of Og|עוֹג֙\rb* \rb in Bashan|בַּבָּשָׁ֔ן\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb had reigned|מָלַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb in Ashtaroth|בְּעַשְׁתָּר֖וֹת\rb* \rb and Edrei|וּבְאֶדְרֶ֑עִי\rb*\rb |ה֤וּא\rb* \rb and had remained|נִשְׁאַר֙\rb* \rb as a remnant|מִיֶּ֣תֶר\rb* \rb of the Rephaim|הָרְפָאִ֔ים\rb*.
\p \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb had struck them down|וַיַּכֵּ֥ם\rb* \rb and dispossessed them|וַיֹּרִשֵֽׁם׃\rb*, \v 13 \rb but the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb drive out|הוֹרִ֙ישׁוּ֙\rb* \rb the Geshurites|הַגְּשׁוּרִ֖י\rb* \rb or|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Maacathites|הַמַּעֲכָתִ֑י\rb*. \rb So Geshur|גְּשׁ֤וּר\rb* \rb and Maacath|וּמַֽעֲכָת֙\rb* \rb dwell|וַיֵּ֨שֶׁב\rb* \rb among|בְּקֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb To the tribe|לְשֵׁ֣בֶט\rb* \rb of Levi|הַלֵּוִ֔י\rb*, \rb however|רַ֚ק\rb*, \rb Moses had given|נָתַ֖ן\rb* \rb no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb inheritance|נַחֲלָ֑ה\rb*. \rb The food offerings|אִשֵּׁ֨י\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*, \rb are|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb their inheritance|נַחֲלָת֔וֹ\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb He had promised|דִּבֶּר־\rb* \rb them|לֽוֹ׃ס\rb*.
\s1 Reuben’s Inheritance
\p \v 15 \rb This is what Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb had given|וַיִּתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb to the clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb of the tribe|לְמַטֵּ֥ה\rb*\rb |בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Reuben|רְאוּבֵ֖ן\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \v 16 \rb |וַיְהִ֨י\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb The territory|הַגְּב֗וּל\rb* \rb from Aroer|מֵעֲרוֹעֵ֡ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the rim|שְׂפַת־\rb* \rb of the Arnon|אַרְנ֜וֹן\rb* \rb Valley|נַ֨חַל\rb*, \rb along with the city|וְהָעִ֨יר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb in the middle|בְּתוֹךְ־\rb* \rb of the valley|הַנַּ֛חַל\rb*, \rb to the whole|וְכָל־\rb* \rb plateau|הַמִּישֹׁ֖ר\rb* \rb beyond|עַל־\rb* \rb Medeba|מֵידְבָֽא׃\rb*, \v 17 \rb to Heshbon|חֶשְׁבּ֥וֹן\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb its cities|עָרֶ֖יהָ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb on the plateau|בַּמִּישֹׁ֑ר\rb*, \rb including Dibon|דִּיבוֹן֙\rb*,\rb |וּבָמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb Bamoth-baal|בַּ֔עַל\rb*,\rb |וּבֵ֖ית\rb*\rb |בַּ֥עַל\rb* \rb Beth-baal-meon|מְעֽוֹן׃\rb*, \v 18 \rb Jahaz|וְיַ֥הְצָה\rb*, \rb Kedemoth|וּקְדֵמֹ֖ת\rb*, \rb Mephaath|וּמֵפָֽעַת׃\rb*, \v 19 \rb Kiriathaim|וְקִרְיָתַ֣יִם\rb*, \rb Sibmah|וְשִׂבְמָ֔ה\rb*,\rb |וְצֶ֥רֶת\rb* \rb Zereth-shahar|הַשַּׁ֖חַר\rb* \rb on the hill|בְּהַ֥ר\rb* \rb in the valley|הָעֵֽמֶק׃\rb*, \v 20 \rb |וּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb Beth-peor|פְּע֛וֹר\rb*, \rb the slopes|וְאַשְׁדּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of Pisgah|הַפִּסְגָּ֖ה\rb*,\rb |וּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb and Beth-jeshimoth|הַיְשִׁמֽוֹת׃\rb*— \v 21 \rb all|וְכֹל֙\rb* \rb the cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the plateau|הַמִּישֹׁ֔ר\rb* \rb and all|וְכָֽל־\rb* \rb the kingdom|מַמְלְכ֗וּת\rb* \rb of Sihon|סִיחוֹן֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of the Amorites|הָאֱמֹרִ֔י\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Heshbon|בְּחֶשְׁבּ֑וֹן\rb* \rb until|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֹת֣וֹ׀\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb killed him|הִכָּ֨ה\rb* \rb and the chiefs|נְשִׂיאֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Midian|מִדְיָ֗ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* (\rb Evi|אֱוִ֤י\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Rekem|רֶ֙קֶם֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Zur|צ֤וּר\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Hur|חוּר֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Reba|רֶ֔בַע\rb*), \rb the princes|נְסִיכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Sihon|סִיח֔וֹן\rb* \rb who lived|יֹשְׁבֵ֖י\rb* \rb in the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 22 \rb The Israelites|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb also killed|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the diviner|הַקּוֹסֵ֑ם\rb* \rb Balaam|בִּלְעָ֥ם\rb* \rb son of Beor|בְּע֖וֹר\rb* \rb along with the others they put|הָרְג֧וּ\rb* \rb to the sword|בַּחֶ֖רֶב\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |חַלְלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb And the border|גְּבוּל֙\rb* \rb of the Reubenites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |רְאוּבֵ֔ן\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb the bank|וּגְב֑וּל\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֖ן\rb*.
\p \rb This|זֹ֣את\rb* \rb was the inheritance|נַחֲלַ֤ת\rb* \rb of the clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb of the Reubenites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |רְאוּבֵן֙\rb*, \rb including the cities|הֶעָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb and villages|וְחַצְרֵיהֶֽן׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Gad’s Inheritance
\p \v 24 \rb This is what Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb had given|וַיִּתֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb to the clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb of the tribe|לְמַטֵּה־\rb* \rb of Gad|לִבְנֵי־\rb*\rb |גָ֖ד\rb*\rb |גָ֔ד\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \v 25 \rb |וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb The territory|הַגְּב֔וּל\rb* \rb of Jazer|יַעְזֵר֙\rb*, \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Gilead|הַגִּלְעָ֔ד\rb*, \rb and half|וַחֲצִ֕י\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֑וֹן\rb* \rb as far as|עַד־\rb* \rb Aroer|עֲרוֹעֵ֕ר\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb near|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Rabbah|רַבָּֽה׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 26 \rb the territory from Heshbon|וּמֵחֶשְׁבּ֛וֹן\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb Ramath-mizpeh|רָמַ֥ת\rb*\rb |הַמִּצְפֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb and Betonim|וּבְטֹנִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and from Mahanaim|וּמִֽמַּחֲנַ֖יִם\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the border|גְּב֥וּל\rb* \rb of Debir|לִדְבִֽר׃\rb*;\f + \fr 13:26 \ft LXX, Syriac, and Vulgate; Hebrew \fqa Li-debir\ft , a variant of \fqa Lo-debar\ft ; see \ref 2 Samuel 9:4|2SA 9:4\ref*, 2 Samuel 17:27, and Amos 6:13.\f*
