\s1 Manasseh’s Eastern Inheritance
\p \v 29 \rb This is what Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb had given|וַיִּתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb to the clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחוֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb of the half-tribe|לַחֲצִ֖י\rb*\rb |שֵׁ֣בֶט\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֑ה\rb*, \rb that is|וַיְהִ֗י\rb*, \rb to half|לַחֲצִ֛י\rb* \rb the tribe|מַטֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb of the descendants|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֖ה\rb*:
\pmo \v 30 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb The territory|גְבוּלָ֗ם\rb* \rb from Mahanaim|מִמַּחֲנַ֨יִם\rb* \rb through all|כָּֽל־\rb* \rb Bashan|הַבָּשָׁ֜ן\rb*— \rb all|כָּֽל־\rb* \rb the kingdom|מַמְלְכ֣וּת׀\rb* \rb of Og|ע֣וֹג\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Bashan|הַבָּשָׁ֗ן\rb*, \rb including all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the towns|חַוֺּ֥ת\rb* \rb of Jair|יָאִ֛יר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb are in Bashan|בַּבָּשָׁ֖ן\rb*, \rb sixty|שִׁשִּׁ֥ים\rb* \rb cities|עִֽיר׃\rb*; \v 31 \rb half|וַחֲצִ֤י\rb* \rb of Gilead|הַגִּלְעָד֙\rb*; \rb and Ashtaroth|וְעַשְׁתָּר֣וֹת\rb* \rb and Edrei|וְאֶדְרֶ֔עִי\rb*, \rb the royal|מַמְלְכ֥וּת\rb* \rb cities|עָרֵ֛י\rb* \rb of Og|ע֖וֹג\rb* \rb in Bashan|בַּבָּשָׁ֑ן\rb*.
\p \rb All this was for the clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחוֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb of the descendants|לִבְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Machir|מָכִיר֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֔ה\rb*, \rb that is, half of|לַחֲצִ֥י\rb* \rb the descendants|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Machir|מָכִ֖יר\rb*.
\p \v 32 \rb These|אֵ֕לֶּה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb were the portions Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb had given them|נִחַ֥ל\rb* \rb on the plains|בְּעַֽרְב֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָ֑ב\rb* \rb beyond|מֵעֵ֛בֶר\rb* \rb the Jordan|לְיַרְדֵּ֥ן\rb*, \rb east|מִזְרָֽחָה׃ס\rb* \rb of Jericho|יְרִיח֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 33 \rb To the tribe|וּלְשֵׁ֙בֶט֙\rb* \rb of Levi|הַלֵּוִ֔י\rb*, \rb however|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb*, \rb Moses had given|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb inheritance|נַחֲלָ֑ה\rb*. \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֞ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*,\rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb is their inheritance|נַחֲלָתָ֔ם\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb He had promised|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb them|לָהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\c 14
\s1 Land Division West of the Jordan
\p \v 1 \rb Now these are the portions|וְאֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb inherited|נָחֲל֥וּ\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָ֑עַן\rb*, \rb as distributed|נִֽחֲל֜וּ\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb by Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֤ר\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb*, \rb Joshua|וִיהוֹשֻׁ֣עַ\rb* \rb son|בִּן־\rb* \rb of Nun|נ֔וּן\rb*, \rb and the heads|וְרָאשֵׁ֛י\rb* \rb of the families|אֲב֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the tribes|הַמַּטּ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |לִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb Their inheritance|נַחֲלָתָ֑ם\rb* \rb was assigned by lot|בְּגוֹרַ֖ל\rb* \rb for the nine|לְתִשְׁעַ֥ת\rb* \rb and a half|וַחֲצִ֥י\rb*\rb |הַמַּטֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb tribes|הַמַּטּ֖וֹת\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֤ה\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*. \v 3 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb* \rb had given|נָתַ֨ן\rb* \rb the inheritance|נַחֲלַ֨ת\rb* \rb east of|מֵעֵ֖בֶר\rb* \rb the Jordan|לַיַּרְדֵּ֑ן\rb* \rb to the other two|שְׁנֵ֤י\rb* \rb and a half|וַחֲצִ֣י\rb*\rb |הַמַּטֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb tribes|הַמַּטּוֹת֙\rb*. \rb But he granted|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb inheritance|נַחֲלָ֖ה\rb* \rb among them|בְּתוֹכָֽם׃\rb* \rb to the Levites|וְלַ֨לְוִיִּ֔ם\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb The descendants|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Joseph|יוֹסֵ֛ף\rb* \rb became|הָי֧וּ\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb tribes|מַטּ֖וֹת\rb*, \rb Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb and Ephraim|וְאֶפְרָ֑יִם\rb*. \rb And no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb portion|חֵ֨לֶק\rb* \rb of the land|בָּאָ֗רֶץ\rb*\rb |כִּ֤י\rb* \rb was given|נָתְנוּ֩\rb* \rb to the Levites|לַלְוִיִּ֜ם\rb*, \rb except for|אִם־\rb* \rb cities|עָרִים֙\rb* \rb in which to live|לָשֶׁ֔בֶת\rb*, \rb along with pasturelands|וּמִ֨גְרְשֵׁיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb for their flocks|לְמִקְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and herds|וּלְקִנְיָנָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb So|כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb did|עָשׂ֖וּ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֤ה\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*, \rb and they divided|וַֽיַּחְלְק֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Caleb Requests Hebron
\p \v 6 \rb Then the sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֤ה\rb* \rb approached|וַיִּגְּשׁ֨וּ\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb at Gilgal|בַּגִּלְגָּ֔ל\rb*, \rb and Caleb|כָּלֵ֥ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jephunneh|יְפֻנֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb the Kenizzite|הַקְּנִזִּ֑י\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb to him|אֶל־\rb*, “\rb You|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֡עְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָר֩\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|דִּבֶּ֨ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb the man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb at Kadesh-barnea|בַּרְנֵֽעַ׃\rb* \rb about|עַ֧ל\rb* \rb you|אֹדוֹתֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb and|וְעַ֥ל\rb* \rb me|אֹדוֹתַ֛י\rb*. \v 7 \rb I was|אָנֹכִ֗י\rb* \rb forty|אַרְבָּעִ֨ים\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֜ה\rb* \rb when Moses|מֹשֶׁ֨ה\rb* \rb the servant|עֶֽבֶד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb sent|בִּ֠שְׁלֹחַ\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֛י\rb* \rb from|מִקָּדֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb Kadesh-barnea|בַּרְנֵ֖עַ\rb* \rb to spy out|לְרַגֵּ֣ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb and I brought back|וָאָשֵׁ֤ב\rb* \rb to him|אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb an honest|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb*\rb |עִם־\rb*\rb |לְבָבִֽי׃\rb* \rb report|דָּבָ֔ר\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Although my brothers|וְאַחַי֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb went|עָל֣וּ\rb* \rb with me|עִמִּ֔י\rb* \rb made the hearts|לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb melt with fear|הִמְסִ֖יו\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb I|וְאָנֹכִ֣י\rb* \rb remained loyal|מִלֵּ֔אתִי\rb* \rb to|אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb my God|אֱלֹהָֽי׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb On that|הַהוּא֮\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb swore to me|וַיִּשָּׁבַ֣ע\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹר֒\rb*, ‘\rb Surely|אִם־\rb*\rb |לֹ֗א\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb on which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you have set foot|דָּרְכָ֤ה\rb*\rb |רַגְלְךָ֙\rb* \rb will be|תִֽהְיֶ֧ה\rb* \rb an inheritance|לְנַחֲלָ֛ה\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֨\rb* \rb and your children|וּלְבָנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָ֑ם\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you have wholly|מִלֵּ֔אתָ\rb* \rb followed|אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb my God|אֱלֹהָֽי׃\rb*.’
\p \v 10 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb behold|הִנֵּה֩\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD promised|דִּבֵּר֒\rb*, \rb He|יְהוָ֣ה׀\rb*\rb |אוֹתִי֮\rb* \rb has kept me alive|הֶחֱיָ֨ה\rb* \rb these|זֶה֩\rb* \rb forty-five|אַרְבָּעִ֨ים\rb*\rb |וְחָמֵ֜שׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֗ה\rb* \rb since|מֵ֠אָז\rb* \rb He|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb spoke|דִּבֶּ֨ר\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb word|הַדָּבָ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*, \rb while|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb wandered|הָלַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֑ר\rb*. \rb So|וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb here|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb I am today|אָנֹכִ֣י\rb*\rb |הַיּ֔וֹם\rb*, \rb eighty-five|חָמֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמוֹנִ֖ים\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָֽה׃\rb*, \v 11 \rb still|עוֹדֶ֨נִּי\rb* \rb as strong|חָזָ֗ק\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֜וֹם\rb* \rb as|כַּֽאֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb I was the day|בְּי֨וֹם\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb sent me out|שְׁלֹ֤חַ\rb*\rb |אוֹתִי֙\rb*. \rb As my strength|כְּכֹ֥חִי\rb* \rb was then|אָ֖ז\rb*, \rb so it|וּכְכֹ֣חִי\rb* \rb is now|עָ֑תָּה\rb* \rb for war|לַמִּלְחָמָ֖ה\rb*, \rb for going out|וְלָצֵ֥את\rb*, \rb and for coming in|וְלָבֽוֹא׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Now therefore|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb give|תְּנָה־\rb* \rb me|לִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb hill country|הָהָ֣ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb promised me|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb on that|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you yourself|אַתָּֽה־\rb* \rb heard|שָׁמַעְתָּ֩\rb* \rb then|בַיּ֨וֹם\rb*\rb |הַה֜וּא\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the Anakim|עֲנָקִ֣ים\rb* \rb were there|שָׁ֗ם\rb*, \rb with great|גְּדֹל֣וֹת\rb* \rb and fortified|בְּצֻר֔וֹת\rb* \rb cities|וְעָרִים֙\rb*. \rb Perhaps|אוּלַ֨י\rb* \rb with the LORD’s|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb help|אוֹתִי֙\rb* \rb I will drive them out|וְה֣וֹרַשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb has spoken|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb*.”
\p \v 13 \rb Then Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֑עַ\rb* \rb blessed|וַֽיְבָרְכֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb Caleb|לְכָלֵ֥ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jephunneh|יְפֻנֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb and gave|וַיִּתֵּ֧ן\rb* \rb him|אֶת־\rb* \rb Hebron|חֶבְר֛וֹן\rb* \rb as his inheritance|לְנַחֲלָֽה׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb Therefore|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb Hebron|חֶ֠בְרוֹן\rb* \rb belongs to|הָיְתָֽה־\rb* \rb Caleb|לְכָלֵ֨ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jephunneh|יְפֻנֶּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Kenizzite|הַקְּנִזִּי֙\rb* \rb as an inheritance|לְֽנַחֲלָ֔ה\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb because|יַ֚עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he wholly|מִלֵּ֔א\rb* \rb followed|אַחֲרֵ֕י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 15 (\rb Hebron|חֶבְר֤וֹן\rb* \rb used to be|לְפָנִים֙\rb* \rb called|וְשֵׁ֨ם\rb*\rb |קִרְיַ֣ת\rb* \rb Kiriath-arba|אַרְבַּ֔ע\rb*, \rb after Arba|ה֑וּא\rb*, \rb the greatest|הַגָּד֛וֹל\rb* \rb man|הָאָדָ֧ם\rb* \rb among the Anakim|בָּעֲנָקִ֖ים\rb*.)
\p \rb Then the land|וְהָאָ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb had rest|שָׁקְטָ֖ה\rb* \rb from war|מִמִּלְחָמָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\c 15
\s1 Judah’s Inheritance
\p \v 1 \rb Now the allotment|הַגּוֹרָ֗ל\rb* \rb for the clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb of the tribe|לְמַטֵּ֛ה\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb extended|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the border|גְּב֨וּל\rb* \rb of Edom|אֱד֧וֹם\rb*, \rb to the Wilderness|מִדְבַּר־\rb* \rb of Zin|צִ֛ן\rb*\rb |נֶ֖גְבָּה\rb* \rb at the extreme|מִקְצֵ֥ה\rb* \rb southern boundary|תֵימָֽן׃\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \v 2 \rb Their|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb southern|נֶ֔גֶב\rb* \rb border|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb started|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb at the bay|הַלָּשֹׁ֖ן\rb*\rb |הַפֹּנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb on|מִן־\rb* \rb the southern|נֶֽגְבָּה׃\rb* \rb tip|מִקְצֵ֖ה\rb* \rb of the Salt Sea|יָ֣ם\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֑לַח\rb*,\f + \fr 15:2 \ft That is, the Dead Sea; also in verse 5\f* \v 3 \rb proceeded|וְ֠יָצָא\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb south|מִנֶּ֜גֶב\rb* \rb of the Ascent|לְמַעֲלֵ֤ה\rb* \rb of Akrabbim|עַקְרַבִּים֙\rb*,\f + \fr 15:3 \ft Or \fqa the Ascent of Scorpions \ft or \fqa Scorpion Pass\f* \rb continued on|וְעָ֣בַר\rb* \rb to Zin|צִ֔נָה\rb*, \rb went over|וְעָלָ֥ה\rb* \rb to the south|מִנֶּ֖גֶב\rb*\rb |לְקָדֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb of Kadesh-barnea|בַּרְנֵ֑עַ\rb*, \rb ran past|וְעָבַ֤ר\rb* \rb Hezron|חֶצְרוֹן֙\rb* \rb up to|וְעָלָ֣ה\rb* \rb Addar|אַדָּ֔רָה\rb*, \rb and curved|וְנָסַ֖ב\rb* \rb toward Karka|הַקַּרְקָֽעָה׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb It proceeded|וְעָבַ֣ר\rb* \rb to Azmon|עַצְמ֗וֹנָה\rb*,\rb |וְיָצָא֙\rb* \rb joined the Brook|נַ֣חַל\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*,\rb |וְהָיָה\rb* \rb and ended|תֹּצְא֥וֹת\rb*\rb |הַגְּב֖וּל\rb* \rb at the Sea|יָ֑מָּה\rb*.\f + \fr 15:4 \ft That is, the Mediterranean Sea, also called the Great Sea; also in verses 11, 12, and 47\f* \rb This|זֶה־\rb* \rb was|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb their|לָכֶ֖ם\rb*\f + \fr 15:4 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa your\f* \rb southern|נֶֽגֶב׃\rb* \rb border|גְּב֥וּל\rb*.
\li1 \v 5 \rb The eastern|קֵ֙דְמָה֙\rb* \rb border|וּגְב֥וּל\rb* \rb was the Salt Sea|יָ֣ם\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֔לַח\rb* \rb as far as|עַד־\rb* \rb the mouth|קְצֵ֖ה\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֑ן\rb*.
\li1 \rb The northern|צָפ֙וֹנָה֙\rb* \rb border started|וּגְב֞וּל\rb* \rb from|לִפְאַ֤ת\rb* \rb the bay|מִלְּשׁ֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the sea|הַיָּ֔ם\rb* \rb at the mouth|מִקְצֵ֖ה\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּֽן׃\rb*, \v 6 \rb went up|וְעָלָ֤ה\rb*\rb |הַגְּבוּל֙\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb to Beth-hoglah|חָגְלָ֔ה\rb*, \rb proceeded|וְעָבַ֕ר\rb* \rb north|מִצְּפ֖וֹן\rb*\rb |לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of Beth-arabah|הָעֲרָבָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and went up|וְעָלָ֣ה\rb*\rb |הַגְּב֔וּל\rb* \rb to the Stone|אֶ֥בֶן\rb* \rb of Bohan|בֹּ֖הַן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Reuben|רְאוּבֵֽן׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb Then the border|הַגְּב֥וּל׀\rb* \rb went up|וְעָלָ֨ה\rb* \rb to Debir|דְּבִרָה֮\rb* \rb from the Valley|מֵעֵ֣מֶק\rb* \rb of Achor|עָכוֹר֒\rb*, \rb turning|פֹּנֶ֣ה\rb* \rb north|וְצָפ֜וֹנָה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Gilgal|הַגִּלְגָּ֗ל\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb faces|נֹ֙כַח֙\rb* \rb the Ascent|לְמַעֲלֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of Adummim|אֲדֻמִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb south|מִנֶּ֖גֶב\rb* \rb of the ravine|לַנָּ֑חַל\rb*. \rb It|הַגְּבוּל֙\rb* \rb continued|וְעָבַ֤ר\rb* \rb along|אֶל־\rb* \rb the waters|מֵי־\rb*\rb |עֵ֣ין\rb* \rb of En-shemesh|שֶׁ֔מֶשׁ\rb* \rb and came out|וְהָי֥וּ\rb*\rb |תֹצְאֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb*\rb |עֵ֥ין\rb* \rb En-rogel|רֹגֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb From there the border|הַגְּב֜וּל\rb* \rb went up|וְעָלָ֨ה\rb* \rb the Valley of Ben-hinnom|גֵּ֣י\rb*\rb |בֶן־\rb*\rb |הִנֹּ֗ם\rb* \rb along|אֶל־\rb* \rb the southern|מִנֶּ֔גֶב\rb* \rb slope|כֶּ֤תֶף\rb* \rb of the Jebusites|הַיְבוּסִי֙\rb* \rb (that is|הִ֖יא\rb*, \rb Jerusalem|יְרֽוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*) \rb and ascended|וְעָלָ֨ה\rb*\rb |הַגְּב֜וּל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the top|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of the hill|הָהָ֗ר\rb* \rb that|אֲ֠שֶׁר\rb* \rb faces|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb the Valley of Hinnom|גֵֽי־\rb*\rb |הִנֹּם֙\rb* \rb on the west|יָ֔מָּה\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb at the northern|צָפֹֽנָה׃\rb* \rb end|בִּקְצֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of the Valley|עֵֽמֶק־\rb* \rb of Rephaim|רְפָאִ֖ים\rb*. \v 9 \rb From the hilltop|מֵרֹ֣אשׁ\rb*\rb |הָהָ֗ר\rb* \rb the border|הַגְּב֜וּל\rb* \rb curved|וְתָאַ֨ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the spring|מַעְיַן֙\rb* \rb of the Waters|מֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Nephtoah|נֶפְתּ֔וֹחַ\rb*, \rb proceeded|וְיָצָ֖א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Mount|הַר־\rb* \rb Ephron|עֶפְר֑וֹן\rb*, \rb and then bent around|וְתָאַ֤ר\rb*\rb |הַגְּבוּל֙\rb* \rb toward Baalah|בַּעֲלָ֔ה\rb* \rb (that is|הִ֖יא\rb*,\rb |קִרְיַ֥ת\rb* \rb Kiriath-jearim)|יְעָרִֽים׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb The border|הַגְּב֨וּל\rb* \rb curled|וְנָסַב֩\rb* \rb westward|יָ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb from Baalah|מִבַּעֲלָ֥ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Mount|הַ֣ר\rb* \rb Seir|שֵׂעִ֔יר\rb*, \rb ran|וְעָבַ֕ר\rb* \rb along|אֶל־\rb* \rb the northern|מִצָּפ֖וֹנָה\rb* \rb slope|כֶּ֧תֶף\rb* \rb of Mount|הַר־\rb* \rb Jearim|יְעָרִ֛ים\rb* \rb (that is|הִ֣יא\rb*, \rb Chesalon|כְסָל֑וֹן\rb*), \rb went down|וְיָרַ֥ד\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb to Beth-shemesh|שֶׁ֖מֶשׁ\rb*, \rb and crossed|וְעָבַ֥ר\rb* \rb to Timnah|תִּמְנָֽה׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb Then it|הַגְּב֜וּל\rb* \rb went out|וְיָצָ֨א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the northern|צָפוֹנָה֒\rb* \rb slope|כֶּ֣תֶף\rb* \rb of Ekron|עֶקְרוֹן֮\rb*, \rb curved|וְתָאַ֤ר\rb*\rb |הַגְּבוּל֙\rb* \rb toward Shikkeron|שִׁכְּר֔וֹנָה\rb*, \rb proceeded|וְעָבַ֥ר\rb* \rb to Mount|הַר־\rb* \rb Baalah|הַֽבַּעֲלָ֖ה\rb*, \rb went on|וְיָצָ֣א\rb* \rb to Jabneel|יַבְנְאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and ended|וְהָי֛וּ\rb*\rb |תֹּצְא֥וֹת\rb*\rb |הַגְּב֖וּל\rb* \rb at the Sea|יָֽמָּה׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 12 \rb And the western|יָ֔ם\rb* \rb border|וּגְב֣וּל\rb* \rb was the coastline|וּגְב֑וּל\rb* \rb of the Great|הַגָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb Sea|הַיָּ֥מָּה\rb*.
\p \rb These|זֶ֠ה\rb* \rb are the boundaries|גְּב֧וּל\rb* \rb around|סָבִ֖יב\rb* \rb the clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb of the descendants|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֛ה\rb*.
\s1 Caleb’s Portion and Conquest
\r (\ref Judges 1:8–26|JDG 1:8-26\ref*)
\p \v 13 \rb According|אֶל־\rb* \rb to the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb command|פִּ֥י\rb* \rb to him|לִֽיהוֹשֻׁ֑עַ\rb*, \rb Joshua gave|נָ֤תַן\rb* \rb Caleb|וּלְכָלֵ֣ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jephunneh|יְפֻנֶּ֗ה\rb* \rb a portion|חֵ֙לֶק֙\rb* \rb among|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* —\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |קִרְיַ֥ת\rb* \rb Kiriath-arba|אַרְבַּ֛ע\rb*, \rb that is|הִ֥יא\rb*, \rb Hebron|חֶבְרֽוֹן׃\rb*. (\rb Arba was the forefather|אֲבִ֥י\rb* \rb of Anak|הָעֲנָ֖ק\rb*.) \v 14 \rb And Caleb|כָּלֵ֔ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb drove out|וַיֹּ֤רֶשׁ\rb* \rb from there|מִשָּׁם֙\rb* \rb the three|שְׁלוֹשָׁ֖ה\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Anak|הָעֲנָ֑ק\rb* — \rb the descendants of|אֶת־\rb* \rb Sheshai|שֵׁשַׁ֤י\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Ahiman|אֲחִימַן֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Talmai|תַּלְמַ֔י\rb*, \rb the children|יְלִידֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Anak|הָעֲנָֽק׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb From there|מִשָּׁ֔ם\rb* \rb he marched|וַיַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the inhabitants|יֹשְׁבֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Debir|דְּבִ֑ר\rb*\rb |דְּבִ֥ר\rb* (\rb formerly|לְפָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb known as|וְשֵׁם־\rb*\rb |קִרְיַת־\rb* \rb Kiriath-sepher|סֵֽפֶר׃\rb*). \v 16 \rb And Caleb|כָּלֵ֔ב\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb To the man who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb strikes down|יַכֶּ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |קִרְיַת־\rb* \rb Kiriath-sepher|סֵ֖פֶר\rb* \rb and captures it|וּלְכָדָ֑הּ\rb*, \rb I will give|וְנָתַ֥תִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my daughter|בִתִּ֖י\rb* \rb Acsah|עַכְסָ֥ה\rb* \rb in marriage|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃\rb*.” \v 17 \rb So Othniel|עָתְנִיאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Caleb’s|כָלֵ֑ב\rb* \rb brother|אֲחִ֣י\rb* \rb Kenaz|קְנַ֖ז\rb* \rb captured the city|וַֽיִּלְכְּדָ֛הּ\rb*, \rb and Caleb gave|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his daughter|בִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Acsah|עַכְסָ֥ה\rb* \rb to him|ל֛וֹ\rb* \rb in marriage|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb One day|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb Acsah came to Othniel|בְּבוֹאָ֗הּ\rb* \rb and urged him|וַתְּסִיתֵ֙הוּ֙\rb*\f + \fr 15:18 \ft Hebrew and some LXX manuscripts; other LXX manuscripts \fqa and he urged her\ft ; see \ref Judges 1:14|JDG 1:14\ref*.\f* \rb to ask|לִשְׁא֤וֹל\rb* \rb her father|אָבִ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb for|מֵֽאֵת־\rb* \rb a field|שָׂדֶ֔ה\rb*. \rb When she got off|וַתִּצְנַ֖ח\rb*\rb |מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb her donkey|הַחֲמ֑וֹר\rb*, \rb Caleb|כָּלֵ֖ב\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּֽאמֶר־\rb* \rb her|לָ֥הּ\rb*, “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb do you desire|לָּֽךְ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 19 “\rb Give|תְּנָה־\rb* \rb me|לִּ֣י\rb* \rb a blessing|בְרָכָ֗ה\rb*,” \rb she answered|וַתֹּ֜אמֶר\rb*. “\rb Since|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you have given me|נְתַתָּ֔נִי\rb* \rb land|אֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb in the Negev|הַנֶּ֙גֶב֙\rb*, \rb give me|וְנָתַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb springs|גֻּלֹּ֣ת\rb* \rb of water|מָ֑יִם\rb* \rb as well|לִ֖י\rb*.”
\p \rb So Caleb gave|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb her|לָ֗הּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb both the upper|עִלִּיּ֔וֹת\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb*\rb |גֻּלֹּ֥ת\rb* \rb and lower|תַּחְתִּיּֽוֹת׃פ\rb* \rb springs|גֻּלֹּ֣ת\rb*.
\s1 The Cities of Judah
\p \v 20 \rb This|זֹ֗את\rb* \rb is the inheritance|נַחֲלַ֛ת\rb* \rb of the clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb of the tribe|מַטֵּ֥ה\rb*\rb |בְנֵי־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb*. \v 21 \rb These were|וַיִּֽהְי֣וּ\rb* \rb the southernmost|מִקְצֵה֙\rb* \rb cities|הֶעָרִ֗ים\rb* \rb of the tribe|לְמַטֵּ֣ה\rb*\rb |בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb in the Negev|בַּנֶּ֑גְבָּה\rb* \rb toward|אֶל־\rb* \rb the border|גְּב֥וּל\rb* \rb of Edom|אֱד֖וֹם\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Kabzeel|קַבְצְאֵ֥ל\rb*, \rb Eder|וְעֵ֖דֶר\rb*, \rb Jagur|וְיָגֽוּר׃\rb*, \v 22 \rb Kinah|וְקִינָ֥ה\rb*, \rb Dimonah|וְדִֽימוֹנָ֖ה\rb*, \rb Adadah|וְעַדְעָדָֽה׃\rb*, \v 23 \rb Kedesh|וְקֶ֥דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb Hazor|וְחָצ֖וֹר\rb*, \rb Ithnan|וְיִתְנָֽן׃\rb*, \v 24 \rb Ziph|זִ֥יף\rb*, \rb Telem|וָטֶ֖לֶם\rb*, \rb Bealoth|וּבְעָלֽוֹת׃\rb*, \v 25 \rb |וְחָצ֤וֹר׀\rb* \rb Hazor-hadattah|חֲדַתָּה֙\rb*, \rb Kerioth-hezron|וּקְרִיּ֔וֹת\rb*\rb |חֶצְר֖וֹן\rb* \rb (that is|הִ֥יא\rb*, \rb Hazor|חָצֽוֹר׃\rb*), \v 26 \rb Amam|אֲמָ֥ם\rb*, \rb Shema|וּשְׁמַ֖ע\rb*, \rb Moladah|וּמוֹלָדָֽה׃\rb*, \v 27 \rb |וַחֲצַ֥ר\rb* \rb Hazar-gaddah|גַּדָּ֛ה\rb*, \rb Heshmon|וְחֶשְׁמ֖וֹן\rb*,\rb |וּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb Beth-pelet|פָּֽלֶט׃\rb*, \v 28 \rb |וַחֲצַ֥ר\rb* \rb Hazar-shual|שׁוּעָ֛ל\rb*,\rb |וּבְאֵ֥ר\rb* \rb Beersheba|שֶׁ֖בַע\rb*, \rb Biziothiah|וּבִזְיוֹתְיָֽה׃\rb*, \v 29 \rb Baalah|בַּעֲלָ֥ה\rb*, \rb Iim|וְעִיִּ֖ים\rb*, \rb Ezem|וָעָֽצֶם׃\rb*, \v 30 \rb Eltolad|וְאֶלְתּוֹלַ֥ד\rb*, \rb Chesil|וּכְסִ֖יל\rb*, \rb Hormah|וְחָרְמָֽה׃\rb*, \v 31 \rb Ziklag|וְצִֽקְלַ֥ג\rb*, \rb Madmannah|וּמַדְמַנָּ֖ה\rb*, \rb Sansannah|וְסַנְסַנָּֽה׃\rb*, \v 32 \rb Lebaoth|וּלְבָא֥וֹת\rb*, \rb Shilhim|וְשִׁלְחִ֖ים\rb*, \rb Ain|וְעַ֣יִן\rb*, \rb and Rimmon|וְרִמּ֑וֹן\rb*— \rb twenty-nine|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וָתֵ֖שַׁע\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֛ים\rb* \rb in all|כָּל־\rb*, \rb along with their villages|וְחַצְרֵיהֶֽן׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 33 \rb These were in the foothills|בַּשְּׁפֵלָ֑ה\rb*:\f + \fr 15:33 \ft Hebrew \fqa Shephelah \ft or \fqa lowlands\ft ; that is, the western foothills of Judea\f*
\b 
\li1 \rb Eshtaol|אֶשְׁתָּא֥וֹל\rb*, \rb Zorah|וְצָרְעָ֖ה\rb*, \rb Ashnah|וְאַשְׁנָֽה׃\rb*, \v 34 \rb Zanoah|וְזָנ֙וֹחַ֙\rb*,\rb |וְעֵ֣ין\rb* \rb En-gannim|גַּנִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb Tappuah|תַּפּ֖וּחַ\rb*, \rb Enam|וְהָעֵינָֽם׃\rb*, \v 35 \rb Jarmuth|יַרְמוּת֙\rb*, \rb Adullam|וַעֲדֻלָּ֔ם\rb*, \rb Socoh|שׂוֹכֹ֖ה\rb*, \rb Azekah|וַעֲזֵקָֽה׃\rb*, \v 36 \rb Shaaraim|וְשַׁעֲרַ֙יִם֙\rb*, \rb Adithaim|וַעֲדִיתַ֔יִם\rb*, \rb and Gederah|וְהַגְּדֵרָ֖ה\rb* \rb (or Gederothaim)|וּגְדֵרֹתָ֑יִם\rb*— \rb fourteen|אַרְבַּֽע־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֥ים\rb*, \rb along with their villages|וְחַצְרֵיהֶֽן׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 37 \rb Zenan|צְנָ֥ן\rb*, \rb Hadashah|וַחֲדָשָׁ֖ה\rb*,\rb |וּמִגְדַּל־\rb* \rb Migdal-gad|גָּֽד׃\rb*, \v 38 \rb Dilan|וְדִלְעָ֥ן\rb*, \rb Mizpeh|וְהַמִּצְפֶּ֖ה\rb*, \rb Joktheel|וְיָקְתְאֵֽל׃\rb*, \v 39 \rb Lachish|לָכִ֥ישׁ\rb*, \rb Bozkath|וּבָצְקַ֖ת\rb*, \rb Eglon|וְעֶגְלֽוֹן׃\rb*, \v 40 \rb Cabbon|וְכַבּ֥וֹן\rb*, \rb Lahmas|וְלַחְמָ֖ס\rb*, \rb Chitlish|וְכִתְלִֽישׁ׃\rb*, \v 41 \rb Gederoth|וּגְדֵר֕וֹת\rb*,\rb |בֵּית־\rb* \rb Beth-dagon|דָּג֥וֹן\rb*, \rb Naamah|וְנַעֲמָ֖ה\rb*, \rb and Makkedah|וּמַקֵּדָ֑ה\rb*— \rb sixteen|שֵׁשׁ־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֥ים\rb*, \rb along with their villages|וְחַצְרֵיהֶֽן׃ס\rb*.
\li1 \v 42 \rb Libnah|לִבְנָ֥ה\rb*, \rb Ether|וָעֶ֖תֶר\rb*, \rb Ashan|וְעָשָֽׁן׃\rb*, \v 43 \rb Iphtah|וְיִפְתָּ֥ח\rb*, \rb Ashnah|וְאַשְׁנָ֖ה\rb*, \rb Nezib|וּנְצִֽיב׃\rb*, \v 44 \rb Keilah|וּקְעִילָ֥ה\rb*, \rb Achzib|וְאַכְזִ֖יב\rb*, \rb and Mareshah|וּמָֽרֵאשָׁ֑ה\rb*— \rb nine|תֵּ֖שַׁע\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֥ים\rb*, \rb along with their villages|וְחַצְרֵיהֶֽן׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 45 \rb Ekron|עֶקְר֥וֹן\rb*, \rb with its towns|וּבְנֹתֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb and villages|וַחֲצֵרֶֽיהָ׃\rb*; \v 46 \rb from Ekron|מֵעֶקְר֖וֹן\rb* \rb to the sea|וָיָ֑מָּה\rb*, \rb all|כֹּ֛ל\rb* \rb the cities|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb near|עַל־\rb*\rb |יַ֥ד\rb* \rb Ashdod|אַשְׁדּ֖וֹד\rb*, \rb along with their villages|וְחַצְרֵיהֶֽן׃\rb*; \v 47 \rb Ashdod|אַשְׁדּ֞וֹד\rb*, \rb with its towns|בְּנוֹתֶ֣יהָ\rb* \rb and villages|וַחֲצֵרֶ֗יהָ\rb*; \rb Gaza|עַזָּ֥ה\rb*, \rb with its towns|בְּנוֹתֶ֥יהָ\rb* \rb and villages|וַחֲצֵרֶ֖יהָ\rb*, \rb as far as|עַד־\rb* \rb the Brook|נַ֣חַל\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and the coastline|וּגְבֽוּל׃ס\rb* \rb of the Great|הַגָּבוֹל\rb* \rb Sea|וְהַיָּ֥ם\rb*.
\p \v 48 \rb These were in the hill country|וּבָהָ֑ר\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Shamir|שָׁמִ֥יר\rb*, \rb Jattir|וְיַתִּ֖יר\rb*, \rb Socoh|וְשׂוֹכֹֽה׃\rb*, \v 49 \rb Dannah|וְדַנָּ֥ה\rb*,\rb |וְקִרְיַת־\rb* \rb Kiriath-sannah|סַנָּ֖ה\rb* \rb (that is|הִ֥יא\rb*, \rb Debir|דְבִֽר׃\rb*), \v 50 \rb Anab|וַעֲנָ֥ב\rb*, \rb Eshtemoh|וְאֶשְׁתְּמֹ֖ה\rb*, \rb Anim|וְעָנִֽים׃\rb*, \v 51 \rb Goshen|וְגֹ֥שֶׁן\rb*, \rb Holon|וְחֹלֹ֖ן\rb*, \rb and Giloh|וְגִלֹ֑ה\rb*— \rb eleven|אַֽחַת־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֥ים\rb*, \rb along with their villages|וְחַצְרֵיהֶֽן׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 52 \rb Arab|אֲרַ֥ב\rb*, \rb Dumah|וְרוּמָ֖ה\rb*, \rb Eshan|וְאֶשְׁעָֽן׃\rb*, \v 53 \rb Janim|וְיָנִים\rb*,\rb |וּבֵית־\rb* \rb Beth-tappuah|תַּפּ֖וּחַ\rb*, \rb Aphekah|וַאֲפֵֽקָה׃\rb*, \v 54 \rb Humtah|וְחֻמְטָ֗ה\rb*,\rb |וְקִרְיַ֥ת\rb* \rb Kiriath-arba|אַרְבַּ֛ע\rb* \rb (that is|הִ֥יא\rb*, \rb Hebron|חֶבְר֖וֹן\rb*), \rb and Zior|וְצִיעֹ֑ר\rb*— \rb nine|תֵּ֖שַׁע\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֥ים\rb*, \rb along with their villages|וְחַצְרֵיהֶֽן׃ס\rb*.
\li1 \v 55 \rb Maon|מָע֥וֹן׀\rb*, \rb Carmel|כַּרְמֶ֖ל\rb*, \rb Ziph|וָזִ֥יף\rb*, \rb Juttah|וְיוּטָּֽה׃\rb*, \v 56 \rb Jezreel|וְיִזְרְעֶ֥אל\rb*, \rb Jokdeam|וְיָקְדְעָ֖ם\rb*, \rb Zanoah|וְזָנֽוֹחַ׃\rb*, \v 57 \rb Kain|הַקַּ֖יִן\rb*, \rb Gibeah|גִּבְעָ֣ה\rb*, \rb and Timnah|וְתִמְנָ֑ה\rb*— \rb ten|עֶ֖שֶׂר\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֥ים\rb*, \rb along with their villages|וְחַצְרֵיהֶֽן׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 58 \rb Halhul|חַלְח֥וּל\rb*,\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Beth-zur|צ֖וּר\rb*, \rb Gedor|וּגְדֽוֹר׃\rb*, \v 59 \rb Maarath|וּמַעֲרָ֥ת\rb*,\rb |וּבֵית־\rb* \rb Beth-anoth|עֲנ֖וֹת\rb*, \rb and Eltekon|וְאֶלְתְּקֹ֑ן\rb*— \rb six|שֵׁ֖שׁ\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֥ים\rb*, \rb along with their villages|וְחַצְרֵיהֶֽן׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 60 \rb |קִרְיַת־\rb* \rb Kiriath-baal|בַּ֗עַל\rb* \rb (that is|הִ֛יא\rb*,\rb |קִרְיַ֥ת\rb* \rb Kiriath-jearim|יְעָרִ֖ים\rb*), \rb and Rabbah|וְהָֽרַבָּ֑ה\rb*— \rb two|שְׁתַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֥ים\rb*, \rb along with their villages|וְחַצְרֵיהֶֽן׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 61 \rb These were in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֑ר\rb*:\rb |בֵּ֚ית\rb*
\b 
\li1 \rb Beth-arabah|הָעֲרָבָ֔ה\rb*, \rb Middin|מִדִּ֖ין\rb*, \rb Secacah|וּסְכָכָֽה׃\rb*, \v 62 \rb Nibshan|וְהַנִּבְשָׁ֥ן\rb*,\rb |וְעִיר־\rb* \rb the City of Salt|הַמֶּ֖לַח\rb*,\rb |וְעֵ֣ין\rb* \rb and En-gedi|גֶּ֑דִי\rb*— \rb six|שֵׁ֖שׁ\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֥ים\rb*, \rb along with their villages|וְחַצְרֵיהֶֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 63 \rb But the descendants|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb could|יוּכְלוּ\rb* \rb not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb drive out|לְהֽוֹרִישָׁ֑ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Jebusites|הַיְבוּסִי֙\rb* \rb living|יוֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|יְרֽוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*. \rb So to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃פ\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb the Jebusites|הַיְבוּסִ֜י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb live|וַיֵּ֨שֶׁב\rb* \rb there|בִּיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb among the descendants|בְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb*.
\c 16
\s1 Ephraim’s Inheritance
\p \v 1 \rb The allotment|הַגּוֹרָ֜ל\rb* \rb for the descendants|לִבְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Joseph|יוֹסֵף֙\rb* \rb extended|וַיֵּצֵ֨א\rb* \rb from the Jordan|מִיַּרְדֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb at Jericho|יְרִיח֔וֹ\rb* \rb to the waters|לְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Jericho|יְרִיח֖וֹ\rb* \rb on the east|מִזְרָ֑חָה\rb*, \rb through the wilderness|הַמִּדְבָּ֗ר\rb* \rb that goes up|עֹלֶ֧ה\rb* \rb from Jericho|מִירִיח֛וֹ\rb* \rb into the hill country|בָּהָ֖ר\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Bethel|אֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb It went on|וְיָצָ֥א\rb* \rb from|מִבֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel|אֵ֖ל\rb* \rb (that is, Luz|ל֑וּזָה\rb*)\f + \fr 16:2 \ft LXX (See also \ref Joshua 18:13|JOS 18:13\ref*); Hebrew \fqa from Bethel to Luz\f* \rb and proceeded|וְעָבַ֛ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the border|גְּב֥וּל\rb* \rb of the Archites|הָאַרְכִּ֖י\rb* \rb in Ataroth|עֲטָרֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb Then it descended|וְיָֽרַד־\rb* \rb westward|יָ֜מָּה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the border|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb of the Japhletites|הַיַּפְלֵטִ֗י\rb* \rb as|עַ֣ד\rb* \rb far as the border|גְּב֧וּל\rb* \rb of|בֵּית־\rb* \rb Lower|תַּחְתּ֖וֹן\rb* \rb Beth-horon|חוֹרֹ֛ן\rb* \rb and on to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb Gezer|גָּ֑זֶר\rb*, \rb and it ended|וְהָי֥וּ\rb*\rb |תֹצְאֹתוֹ\rb* \rb at the Sea|יָֽמָּה׃\rb*.\f + \fr 16:3 \ft That is, the Mediterranean Sea, also called the Great Sea; also in verses 6 and 8\f*
\p \v 4 \rb So Ephraim|וְאֶפְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb and Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֥ה\rb*, \rb the sons|בְנֵי־\rb* \rb of Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb*, \rb received their inheritance|וַיִּנְחֲל֥וּ\rb*. \v 5 \rb This was|וַיְהִ֛י\rb* \rb the territory|גְּב֥וּל\rb* \rb of the descendants|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb by their clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָ֑ם\rb*:\rb |וַיְהִ֞י\rb*
\pmo \rb The border|גְּב֤וּל\rb* \rb of their inheritance|נַחֲלָתָם֙\rb* \rb went from Ataroth-addar|אַדָּ֔ר\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb in the east|מִזְרָ֔חָה\rb* \rb to Upper|עֶלְיֽוֹן׃\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb Beth-horon|חוֹרֹ֖ן\rb* \v 6 \rb and out toward|וְיָצָ֨א\rb*\rb |הַגְּב֜וּל\rb* \rb the Sea|הַיָּ֗מָּה\rb*. \rb From Michmethath|הַֽמִּכְמְתָת֙\rb* \rb on the north|מִצָּפ֔וֹן\rb* \rb it|הַגְּב֛וּל\rb* \rb turned|וְנָסַ֧ב\rb* \rb eastward|מִזְרָ֖חָה\rb*\rb |תַּאֲנַ֣ת\rb* \rb toward Taanath-shiloh|שִׁלֹ֑ה\rb* \rb and passed by|וְעָבַ֣ר\rb* \rb it|אוֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb to Janoah|יָנֽוֹחָה׃\rb* \rb on the east|מִמִּזְרַ֖ח\rb*. \v 7 \rb From Janoah|מִיָּנ֖וֹחָה\rb* \rb it went down|וְיָרַ֥ד\rb* \rb to Ataroth|עֲטָר֣וֹת\rb* \rb and Naarah|וְנַעֲרָ֑תָה\rb*, \rb and then reached|וּפָגַע֙\rb* \rb Jericho|בִּֽירִיח֔וֹ\rb* \rb and came out|וְיָצָ֖א\rb* \rb at the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּֽן׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb From Tappuah|מִתַּפּ֜וּחַ\rb* \rb the border|הַגְּב֥וּל\rb* \rb went|יֵלֵ֨ךְ\rb* \rb westward|יָ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb to the Brook|נַ֣חַל\rb* \rb of Kanah|קָנָ֔ה\rb* \rb and ended|וְהָי֥וּ\rb*\rb |תֹצְאֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb at the Sea|הַיָּ֑מָּה\rb*.
\p \rb This|זֹ֗את\rb* \rb was the inheritance|נַחֲלַ֛ת\rb* \rb of the clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb of the tribe|מַטֵּ֥ה\rb*\rb |בְנֵי־\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֖יִם\rb*, \v 9 \rb |וְהֶעָרִ֗ים\rb* \rb along with all|כָּֽל־\rb* \rb the cities|הֶעָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb and villages|וְחַצְרֵיהֶֽן׃\rb* \rb set apart|הַמִּבְדָּלוֹת֙\rb* \rb for the descendants|לִבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb within|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb the inheritance|נַחֲלַ֣ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֑ה\rb*. \v 10 \rb But they did not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb drive out|הוֹרִ֔ישׁוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb who lived|הַיּוֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb in Gezer|בְּגָ֑זֶר\rb*. \rb So the Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֜י\rb* \rb dwell|וַיֵּ֨שֶׁב\rb* \rb among|בְּקֶ֤רֶב\rb* \rb the Ephraimites|אֶפְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb but they are|וַיְהִ֖י\rb* \rb forced|לְמַס־\rb* \rb laborers|עֹבֵֽד׃פ\rb*.
\c 17
\s1 Manasseh’s Western Inheritance
\p \v 1 \rb Now this was|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb the allotment|הַגּוֹרָל֙\rb* \rb for the tribe|לְמַטֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֔ה\rb*\rb |כִּי־\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb as Joseph’s|יוֹסֵ֑ף\rb* \rb firstborn son|בְּכ֣וֹר\rb*, \rb namely for Machir|לְמָכִיר֩\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְּכ֨וֹר\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֜ה\rb* \rb and father|אֲבִ֣י\rb* \rb of the Gileadites|הַגִּלְעָ֗ד\rb*, \rb who had received|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb Gilead|הַגִּלְעָ֥ד\rb* \rb and Bashan|וְהַבָּשָֽׁן׃\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Machir|ה֤וּא\rb* \rb was|הָיָה֙\rb* \rb a man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of war|מִלְחָמָ֔ה\rb*. \v 2 \rb So this allotment was|וַ֠יְהִי\rb* \rb for the rest|הַנּוֹתָרִים֮\rb* \rb of the descendants|לִבְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָם֒\rb* — \rb the clans|לִבְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Abiezer|אֲבִיעֶ֜זֶר\rb*,\f + \fr 17:2 \fqa Abiezer \ft is a variant of \fqa Iezer\ft ; see \ref Numbers 26:30|NUM 26:30\ref*.\f*\rb |וְלִבְנֵי־\rb* \rb Helek|חֵ֗לֶק\rb*,\rb |וְלִבְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb Asriel|אַשְׂרִיאֵל֙\rb*,\rb |וְלִבְנֵי־\rb* \rb Shechem|שֶׁ֔כֶם\rb*,\rb |וְלִבְנֵי־\rb* \rb Hepher|חֵ֖פֶר\rb*,\rb |וְלִבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb and Shemida|שְׁמִידָ֑ע\rb*. \rb These|אֵ֠לֶּה\rb* \rb are the other male|הַזְּכָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb descendants|בְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֧ה\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Joseph|יוֹסֵ֛ף\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb But Zelophehad|וְלִצְלָפְחָד֩\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Hepher|חֵ֨פֶר\rb* (\rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Gilead|גִּלְעָ֜ד\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Machir|מָכִ֣יר\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֗ה\rb*) \rb had|הָ֥יוּ\rb*\rb |ל֛וֹ\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb but|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb only|אִם־\rb* \rb daughters|בָּנ֑וֹת\rb*. \rb These|וְאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb are the names|שְׁמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of his daughters|בְּנֹתָ֔יו\rb*: \rb Mahlah|מַחְלָ֣ה\rb*, \rb Noah|וְנֹעָ֔ה\rb*, \rb Hoglah|חָגְלָ֥ה\rb*, \rb Milcah|מִלְכָּ֖ה\rb*, \rb and Tirzah|וְתִרְצָֽה׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb They approached|וַתִּקְרַ֡בְנָה\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵי֩\rb* \rb Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֨ר\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb*,\rb |וְלִפְנֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֣עַ\rb* \rb son|בִּן־\rb* \rb of Nun|נ֗וּן\rb*,\rb |וְלִפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb and the leaders|הַנְּשִׂיאִים֙\rb*, \rb and said|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb The LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb commanded|צִוָּ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb to give|לָֽתֶת־\rb* \rb us|לָ֥נוּ\rb* \rb an inheritance|נַחֲלָ֖ה\rb* \rb among|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb our brothers|אַחֵ֑ינוּ\rb*.”
\p \rb So Joshua gave|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb an inheritance|נַֽחֲלָ֔ה\rb* \rb among|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb their father’s|אֲבִיהֶֽן׃\rb* \rb brothers|אֲחֵ֥י\rb*, \rb in keeping with|אֶל־\rb* \rb the command of|פִּ֤י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*. \v 5 \rb Thus ten|עֲשָׂרָ֑ה\rb* \rb shares|חַבְלֵֽי־\rb* \rb fell|וַיִּפְּל֥וּ\rb* \rb to Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֖ה\rb*, \rb in addition to|לְבַ֞ד\rb* \rb the land|מֵאֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb of Gilead|הַגִּלְעָד֙\rb* \rb and Bashan|וְהַבָּשָׁ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb beyond|מֵעֵ֥בֶר\rb* \rb the Jordan|לַיַּרְדֵּֽן׃\rb*, \v 6 \rb because|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb the daughters|בְּנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb received|נָחֲל֥וּ\rb* \rb an inheritance|נַחֲלָ֖ה\rb* \rb among|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb his sons|בָּנָ֑יו\rb*. \rb And the land|וְאֶ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb of Gilead|הַגִּלְעָ֔ד\rb* \rb belonged to|הָיְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb the rest|הַנּֽוֹתָרִֽים׃\rb* \rb of the sons|לִבְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֖ה\rb*.
\b 
\li1 \v 7 \rb Now the border|גְבוּל־\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁה֙\rb* \rb went|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb from Asher|מֵֽאָשֵׁ֔ר\rb* \rb to Michmethath|הַֽמִּכְמְתָ֔ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb near|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Shechem|שְׁכֶ֑ם\rb*,\rb |הַגְּבוּל֙\rb* \rb then|וְהָלַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb southward|אֶל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֔ין\rb* \rb to include|אֶל־\rb* \rb the inhabitants|יֹשְׁבֵ֖י\rb*\rb |עֵ֥ין\rb* \rb of En-tappuah|תַּפּֽוּחַ׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb The region|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Tappuah|תַּפּ֑וּחַ\rb* \rb belonged to|הָיְתָ֖ה\rb* \rb Manasseh|לִמְנַשֶּׁ֕ה\rb*, \rb but Tappuah itself|וְתַפּ֛וּחַ\rb*, \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the border|גְּב֥וּל\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֖ה\rb*, \rb belonged to|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Ephraim|אֶפְרָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb From there the border|הַגְּבוּל֩\rb* \rb continued|וְיָרַ֣ד\rb* \rb southward|נֶ֣גְבָּה\rb* \rb to the Brook|נַ֨חַל\rb* \rb of Kanah|קָנָ֜ה\rb*.\rb |לַנַּ֗חַל\rb* \rb There were cities|עָרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |הָאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb belonging to Ephraim|לְאֶפְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb among|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb the cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֑ה\rb*, \rb but the border|וּגְב֤וּל\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁה֙\rb* \rb was on the north side|מִצְּפ֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the brook|לַנַּ֔חַל\rb* \rb and ended|וַיְהִ֥י\rb*\rb |תֹצְאֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb at the Sea|הַיָּֽמָּה׃\rb*.\f + \fr 17:9 \ft That is, the Mediterranean Sea, also called the Great Sea; also in verse 10\f* \v 10 \rb Ephraim’s territory|לְאֶפְרַ֗יִם\rb* \rb was to the south|נֶ֣גְבָּה\rb*, \rb and Manasseh’s|לִמְנַשֶּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to the north|וְצָפ֙וֹנָה֙\rb*, \rb having the Sea|הַיָּ֖ם\rb* \rb as its border|גְּבוּל֑וֹ\rb* \rb and adjoining|יִפְגְּע֣וּן\rb* \rb Asher|וּבְאָשֵׁר֙\rb* \rb on the north|מִצָּפ֔וֹן\rb* \rb and Issachar|וּבְיִשָּׂשכָ֖ר\rb* \rb on the east|מִמִּזְרָֽח׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 11 \rb Within Issachar|בְּיִשָּׂשכָ֣ר\rb* \rb and Asher|וּבְאָשֵׁ֗ר\rb*\rb |בֵּית־\rb*, \rb Manasseh|לִמְנַשֶּׁ֜ה\rb* \rb was assigned|וַיְהִ֨י\rb* \rb Beth-shean|שְׁאָ֣ן\rb*\rb |וּ֠בְנוֹתֶיהָ\rb*, \rb Ibleam|וְיִבְלְעָ֨ם\rb*,\rb |וּבְנוֹתֶ֜יהָ\rb*\rb |וְֽאֶת־\rb*\rb |יֹשְׁבֵ֧י\rb* \rb Dor|דֹ֣אר\rb*\rb |וּבְנוֹתֶ֗יהָ\rb* \rb (that is,|שְׁלֹ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb Naphath|הַנָּֽפֶת׃\rb*),\rb |וְיֹשְׁבֵ֤י\rb*\rb |עֵֽין־\rb* \rb Endor|דֹּר֙\rb*\rb |וּבְנֹתֶ֔יהָ\rb*,\rb |וְיֹשְׁבֵ֤י\rb* \rb Taanach|תַעְנַךְ֙\rb*\rb |וּבְנֹתֶ֔יהָ\rb*, \rb and|וְיֹשְׁבֵ֥י\rb* \rb Megiddo|מְגִדּ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb each with their surrounding settlements|וּבְנוֹתֶ֑יהָ\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb But the descendants|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb were unable|יָכְלוּ֙\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb to occupy|לְהוֹרִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb cities|הֶֽעָרִ֣ים\rb*, \rb because the Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֔י\rb* \rb were determined|וַיּ֙וֹאֶל֙\rb* \rb to stay|לָשֶׁ֖בֶת\rb* \rb in this|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb land|בָּאָ֥רֶץ\rb*. \v 13 \rb However|וַֽיְהִ֗י\rb*, \rb when|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb grew stronger|חָֽזְקוּ֙\rb*, \rb they put|וַיִּתְּנ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb to forced labor|לָמַ֑ס\rb*; \rb but they failed|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to drive them out|וְהוֹרֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb completely|הוֹרִישֽׁוֹ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb Then the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb* \rb said|וַֽיְדַבְּרוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶת־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* “\rb Why|מַדּוּעַ֩\rb* \rb have you given|נָתַ֨תָּה\rb* \rb us|לִּ֜י\rb* \rb only|אֶחָד֙\rb*\rb |וְחֶ֣בֶל\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb portion|גּוֹרָ֤ל\rb* \rb as an inheritance|נַחֲלָ֗ה\rb*? \rb We|וַֽאֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb have many|רָ֔ב\rb* \rb people|עַם־\rb*, \rb because|עַ֥ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb*\rb |כֹּ֖ה\rb* \rb has blessed us abundantly|בֵּֽרְכַ֥נִי\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֗עַ\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶ֜ם\rb*, “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb have so many|רַ֤ב\rb* \rb people|עַם־\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the hill country|הַר־\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb is too small|אָ֥ץ\rb* \rb for you|לְךָ֖\rb*, \rb go|עֲלֵ֣ה\rb* \rb to|לְךָ֣\rb* \rb the forest|הַיַּ֔עְרָה\rb* \rb and clear|וּבֵרֵאתָ֤\rb* \rb for yourself|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb an area|שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Perizzites|הַפְּרִזִּ֖י\rb* \rb and the Rephaim|וְהָֽרְפָאִ֑ים\rb*.”
\p \v 16 “\rb The hill country|הָהָ֑ר\rb* \rb is not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb enough|יִמָּ֥צֵא\rb* \rb for us|לָ֖נוּ\rb*,” \rb they|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb*, “\rb and all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִי֙\rb* \rb who live|הַיֹּשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb in the valley|הָעֵ֔מֶק\rb*\rb |לַֽאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb have iron|בַּרְזֶ֗ל\rb* \rb chariots|וְרֶ֣כֶב\rb*, \rb both in Beth-shean|שְׁאָן֙\rb* \rb with its towns|וּבְנוֹתֶ֔יהָ\rb*\rb |וְלַֽאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb and in the Valley|בְּעֵ֥מֶק\rb* \rb of Jezreel|יִזְרְעֶֽאל׃\rb*.”
\p \v 17 \rb So Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb* — \rb to Ephraim|לְאֶפְרַ֥יִם\rb* \rb and Manasseh|וְלִמְנַשֶּׁ֖ה\rb* —\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “You have many|רַ֣ב\rb*\rb |אַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb people|עַם־\rb* \rb and great|גָּדוֹל֙\rb*\rb |לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb strength|וְכֹ֤חַ\rb*. \rb You shall not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb have|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |לְךָ֖\rb* \rb just one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb allotment|גּוֹרָ֥ל\rb*, \v 18 \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the hill country|הַ֤ר\rb* \rb will be|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb yours as well|לָּךְ֙\rb*.\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb It|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb is a forest|יַ֣עַר\rb*; \rb clear it|וּבֵ֣רֵאת֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and its farthest limits|תֹּֽצְאֹתָ֑יו\rb* \rb will be|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb yours|לְךָ֖\rb*. \rb Although|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the Canaanites have iron|בַּרְזֶל֙\rb* \rb chariots|רֶ֤כֶב\rb* \rb and although|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they are strong|חָזָ֖ק\rb*, \rb you can|הֽוּא׃פ\rb* \rb drive them out|תוֹרִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֗י\rb*.”
\c 18
\s1 The Remainder Divided
\p \v 1 \rb Then the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַ֤ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb assembled|וַיִּקָּ֨הֲל֜וּ\rb* \rb at Shiloh|שִׁלֹ֔ה\rb* \rb and set up|וַיַּשְׁכִּ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb And though the land|וְהָאָ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb was subdued|נִכְבְּשָׁ֖ה\rb* \rb before them|לִפְנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*, \v 2 \rb there were still|וַיִּוָּֽתְרוּ֙\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעָ֖ה\rb* \rb tribes|שְׁבָטִֽים׃\rb*\rb |בִּבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb yet received|חָלְק֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their inheritance|נַֽחֲלָתָ֑ם\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb So Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, “\rb How long|עַד־\rb*\rb |אָ֙נָה֙\rb* \rb will you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb put off|מִתְרַפִּ֔ים\rb* \rb entering|לָבוֹא֙\rb* \rb and possessing|לָרֶ֣שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of your fathers|אֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*, \rb has given|נָתַ֣ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֔ם\rb*? \v 4 \rb Appoint|הָב֥וּ\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֥ה\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb from each tribe|לַשָּׁ֑בֶט\rb*, \rb and I will send them out|וְאֶשְׁלָחֵ֗ם\rb*\rb |וְיָקֻ֜מוּ\rb* \rb to survey|וְיִֽתְהַלְּכ֥וּ\rb* \rb the land|בָאָ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb and map it out|וְיִכְתְּב֥וּ\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֛הּ\rb*, \rb according to|לְפִ֥י\rb* \rb the inheritance of each|נַֽחֲלָתָ֖ם\rb*. \rb Then they will return|וְיָבֹ֥אוּ\rb* \rb to me|אֵלָֽי׃\rb* \v 5 \rb and divide|וְהִֽתְחַלְּק֥וּ\rb* \rb the land|אֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb into seven|לְשִׁבְעָ֣ה\rb* \rb portions|חֲלָקִ֑ים\rb*. \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֞ה\rb* \rb shall remain|יַעֲמֹ֤ד\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb their territory|גְּבוּלוֹ֙\rb* \rb in the south|מִנֶּ֔גֶב\rb*, \rb and the house|וּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of Joseph|יוֹסֵ֛ף\rb* \rb shall remain|יַעַמְד֥וּ\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb their territory|גְּבוּלָ֖ם\rb* \rb in the north|מִצָּפֽוֹן׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb When you|וְאַתֶּ֞ם\rb* \rb have mapped out|תִּכְתְּב֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the seven|שִׁבְעָ֣ה\rb* \rb portions|חֲלָקִ֔ים\rb* \rb of land|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb and brought|וַֽהֲבֵאתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb it to me|אֵלַ֖י\rb*,\rb |הֵ֑נָּה\rb* \rb I will cast|וְיָרִ֨יתִי\rb* \rb lots|גּוֹרָל֙\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb here|פֹּ֔ה\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb The Levites|לַלְוִיִּם֙\rb*, \rb however|כִּ֠י\rb*, \rb have no|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb portion|חֵ֤לֶק\rb* \rb among you|בְּקִרְבְּכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb their inheritance|נַחֲלָת֑וֹ\rb* \rb is the priesthood|כְהֻנַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*. \rb And Gad|וְגָ֡ד\rb*, \rb Reuben|וּרְאוּבֵ֡ן\rb*, \rb and half|וַחֲצִי֩\rb* \rb the tribe|שֵׁ֨בֶט\rb* \rb of Manasseh|הַֽמְנַשֶּׁ֜ה\rb* \rb have already received|לָקְח֣וּ\rb* \rb the inheritance|נַחֲלָתָ֗ם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb the servant|עֶ֥בֶד\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb gave|נָתַ֣ן\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb beyond|מֵעֵ֤בֶר\rb* \rb the Jordan|לַיַּרְדֵּן֙\rb* \rb to the east|מִזְרָ֔חָה\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb As the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּקֻ֥מוּ\rb* \rb to go out|וַיֵּלֵ֑כוּ\rb*, \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֡עַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb commanded|וַיְצַ֣ו\rb* \rb them|הַהֹלְכִים֩\rb* \rb to map out|לִכְתֹּ֨ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֜רֶץ\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb*, “\rb Go|לְ֠כוּ\rb* \rb and survey|וְהִתְהַלְּכ֨וּ\rb* \rb the land|בָאָ֜רֶץ\rb*, \rb map it out|וְכִתְב֤וּ\rb*,\rb |אוֹתָהּ֙\rb* \rb and return|וְשׁ֣וּבוּ\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*. \rb Then I will cast|אַשְׁלִ֨יךְ\rb* \rb lots|גּוֹרָ֛ל\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb here|וּ֠פֹה\rb* \rb in Shiloh|בְּשִׁלֹֽה׃\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb So the men|הָֽאֲנָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb departed|וַיֵּלְכ֤וּ\rb* \rb and went throughout|וַיַּעַבְר֣וּ\rb* \rb the land|בָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb mapping it|וַיִּכְתְּב֧וּהָ\rb* \rb city by city|לֶֽעָרִ֛ים\rb* \rb into seven|לְשִׁבְעָ֥ה\rb* \rb portions|חֲלָקִ֖ים\rb*. \rb Then they returned|וַיָּבֹ֧אוּ\rb* \rb with the document|סֵ֑פֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֛עַ\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb in Shiloh|שִׁלֹֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb And Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֧עַ\rb* \rb cast|וַיַּשְׁלֵךְ֩\rb* \rb lots|גּוֹרָ֛ל\rb* \rb for them|לָהֶ֨ם\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb at Shiloh|בְּשִׁלֹ֖ה\rb*, \rb where|שָׁ֨ם\rb* \rb he|יְהוֹשֻׁ֧עַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb distributed|וַיְחַלֶּק־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb to the Israelites|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb according to their divisions|כְּמַחְלְקֹתָֽם׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Benjamin’s Inheritance
\p \v 11 \rb The first lot|גּוֹרַ֛ל\rb* \rb came up|וַיַּ֗עַל\rb* \rb for the clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb of the tribe|מַטֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb of Benjamin|בִנְיָמִ֖ן\rb*\rb |בְנֵֽי־\rb*. \rb Their allotted|גּֽוֹרָלָ֔ם\rb* \rb territory|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb lay|וַיֵּצֵא֙\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֚ין\rb* \rb the tribes|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and|וּבֵ֖ין\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵֽף׃\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \v 12 \rb On the north|צָפ֖וֹנָה\rb* \rb side|לִפְאַ֥ת\rb* \rb their border|הַגְּב֛וּל\rb* \rb began|וַיְהִ֨י\rb* \rb at|מִן־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֑ן\rb*, \rb went up|וְעָלָ֣ה\rb*\rb |הַגְּבוּל֩\rb* \rb past|אֶל־\rb* \rb the northern|מִצָּפ֗וֹן\rb* \rb slope|כֶּ֨תֶף\rb* \rb of Jericho|יְרִיח֜וֹ\rb*, \rb headed|וְעָלָ֤ה\rb* \rb west|יָ֔מָּה\rb* \rb through the hill country|בָהָר֙\rb*, \rb and came out|וְהָיָה\rb*\rb |תֹּֽצְאֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb at the wilderness|מִדְבַּ֖רָה\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Beth-aven|אָֽוֶן׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb From there|מִשָּׁ֨ם\rb* \rb the border|הַגְּב֜וּל\rb* \rb crossed over|וְעָבַר֩\rb*\rb |ל֗וּזָה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the southern|נֶ֔גְבָּה\rb* \rb slope|כֶּ֤תֶף\rb* \rb of Luz|ל֙וּזָה֙\rb* \rb (that is|הִ֖יא\rb*,\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel|אֵ֑ל\rb*)\rb |הַגְּבוּל֙\rb* \rb and went down|וְיָרַ֤ד\rb*\rb |עַטְר֣וֹת\rb* \rb to Ataroth-addar|אַדָּ֔ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the hill|הָהָ֕ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb south|מִנֶּ֥גֶב\rb* \rb of|לְבֵית־\rb* \rb Lower|תַּחְתּֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb Beth-horon|חֹר֖וֹן\rb*.
