\s1 Simeon’s Inheritance
\p \v 1 \rb The second|הַשֵּׁנִי֙\rb* \rb lot|הַגּוֹרָ֤ל\rb* \rb came out|וַיֵּצֵ֞א\rb* \rb for the clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחוֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb of the tribe|לְמַטֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb of Simeon|לְשִׁמְע֔וֹן\rb*\rb |שִׁמְע֖וֹן\rb*\rb |בְנֵֽי־\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Their inheritance|נַֽחֲלָתָ֔ם\rb* \rb lay|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb within|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb the territory|נַחֲלַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*\rb |בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \v 2 \rb |וַיְהִ֥י\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and included|בְּנַֽחֲלָתָ֑ם\rb*\rb |בְּאֵֽר־\rb* \rb Beersheba|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb (or Sheba)|וְשֶׁ֖בַע\rb*, \rb Moladah|וּמוֹלָדָֽה׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb |וַחֲצַ֥ר\rb* \rb Hazar-shual|שׁוּעָ֛ל\rb*, \rb Balah|וּבָלָ֖ה\rb*, \rb Ezem|וָעָֽצֶם׃\rb*, \v 4 \rb Eltolad|וְאֶלְתּוֹלַ֥ד\rb*, \rb Bethul|וּבְת֖וּל\rb*, \rb Hormah|וְחָרְמָֽה׃\rb*, \v 5 \rb Ziklag|וְצִֽקְלַ֥ג\rb*,\rb |וּבֵית־\rb* \rb Beth-marcaboth|הַמַּרְכָּב֖וֹת\rb*,\rb |וַחֲצַ֥ר\rb* \rb Hazar-susah|סוּסָֽה׃\rb*, \v 6 \rb |וּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb Beth-lebaoth|לְבָא֖וֹת\rb*, \rb and Sharuhen|וְשָֽׁרוּחֶ֑ן\rb*— \rb thirteen|שְׁלֹשׁ־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֥ים\rb*, \rb along with their villages|וְחַצְרֵיהֶֽן׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 7 \rb Ain|עַ֥יִן׀\rb*, \rb Rimmon|רִמּ֖וֹן\rb*, \rb Ether|וָעֶ֣תֶר\rb*, \rb and Ashan|וְעָשָׁ֑ן\rb*— \rb four|אַרְבַּ֖ע\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֥ים\rb*, \rb along with their villages|וְחַצְרֵיהֶֽן׃\rb*, \v 8 \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the villages|הַֽחֲצֵרִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb surrounding|סְבִיבוֹת֙\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb cities|הֶֽעָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb as|עַד־\rb*\rb |בַּֽעֲלַ֥ת\rb* \rb far as Baalath-beer|בְּאֵ֖ר\rb* (\rb Ramah|רָ֣אמַת\rb* \rb of the Negev|נֶ֑גֶב\rb*).
\p \rb This|זֹ֗את\rb* \rb was the inheritance|נַחֲלַ֛ת\rb* \rb of the clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb of the tribe|מַטֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb of Simeon|שִׁמְע֖וֹן\rb*\rb |בְנֵֽי־\rb*. \v 9 \rb The inheritance|נַחֲלַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the Simeonites|שִׁמְע֑וֹן\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb was taken from the territory|מֵחֶ֙בֶל֙\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the share|חֵ֤לֶק\rb* \rb for Judah’s|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb descendants|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֞ה\rb* \rb too large|רַ֣ב\rb* \rb for them|מֵהֶ֔ם\rb*. \rb So the Simeonites|שִׁמְע֖וֹן\rb*\rb |בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb received an inheritance|נַחֲלָתָֽם׃פ\rb* \rb within|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb Judah’s portion|וַיִּנְחֲל֥וּ\rb*.
\s1 Zebulun’s Inheritance
\p \v 10 \rb The third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֔י\rb* \rb lot|הַגּוֹרָ֣ל\rb* \rb came up|וַיַּ֙עַל֙\rb* \rb for the clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb of the tribe|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Zebulun|זְבוּלֻ֖ן\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb The border|גְּב֥וּל\rb* \rb of their inheritance|נַחֲלָתָ֖ם\rb* \rb stretched|וַיְהִ֛י\rb* \rb as far as|עַד־\rb* \rb Sarid|שָׂרִֽיד׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb It|גְבוּלָ֧ם׀\rb* \rb went up|וְעָלָ֨ה\rb* \rb westward|לַיָּ֛מָּה\rb* \rb to Maralah|וּמַרְעֲלָ֖ה\rb*, \rb reached|וּפָגַ֣ע\rb* \rb Dabbesheth|בְּדַבָּ֑שֶׁת\rb*, \rb and met|וּפָגַע֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the brook|הַנַּ֔חַל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb east|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Jokneam|יָקְנְעָֽם׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb From Sarid|מִשָּׂרִ֗יד\rb* \rb it turned|וְשָׁ֣ב\rb* \rb eastward|קֵ֚דְמָה\rb*\rb |מִזְרַ֣ח\rb*\rb |הַשֶּׁ֔מֶשׁ\rb* \rb along|עַל־\rb* \rb the border|גְּב֥וּל\rb*\rb |כִּסְלֹ֖ת\rb* \rb of Chisloth-tabor|תָּבֹ֑ר\rb* \rb and went|וְיָצָ֥א\rb* \rb on to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Daberath|הַדָּֽבְרַ֖ת\rb* \rb and up|וְעָלָ֥ה\rb* \rb to Japhia|יָפִֽיעַ׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb From there|וּמִשָּׁ֤ם\rb* \rb it crossed|עָבַר֙\rb* \rb eastward|קֵ֣דְמָה\rb*\rb |מִזְרָ֔חָה\rb*\rb |גִּתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb to Gath-hepher|חֵ֖פֶר\rb*\rb |עִתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb and to Eth-kazin|קָצִ֑ין\rb*; \rb it extended|וְיָצָ֛א\rb* \rb to Rimmon|רִמּ֥וֹן\rb* \rb and curved|הַמְּתֹאָ֖ר\rb* \rb around toward Neah|הַנֵּעָֽה׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb Then the border|הַגְּב֔וּל\rb* \rb circled around|וְנָסַ֤ב\rb* \rb the north side|מִצְּפ֖וֹן\rb* \rb of Neah|אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb to Hannathon|חַנָּתֹ֑ן\rb* \rb and ended|וְהָיוּ֙\rb*\rb |תֹּֽצְאֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb at the Valley|גֵּ֖י\rb*\rb |יִפְתַּח־\rb* \rb of Iphtah-el|אֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb It also included Kattath|וְקַטָּ֤ת\rb*, \rb Nahalal|וְנַֽהֲלָל֙\rb*, \rb Shimron|וְשִׁמְר֔וֹן\rb*, \rb Idalah|וְיִדְאֲלָ֖ה\rb*,\rb |וּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb and Bethlehem|לָ֑חֶם\rb*. \rb There were twelve|שְׁתֵּים־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֥ים\rb*, \rb along with their villages|וְחַצְרֵיהֶֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb This|זֹ֛את\rb* \rb was the inheritance|נַחֲלַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחוֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb of the tribe|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Zebulun|זְבוּלֻ֖ן\rb*, \rb including these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb cities|הֶֽעָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb and their villages|וְחַצְרֵיהֶֽן׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Issachar’s Inheritance
\p \v 17 \rb The fourth|הָֽרְבִיעִ֑י\rb* \rb lot|הַגּוֹרָ֣ל\rb* \rb came out|יָצָ֖א\rb* \rb for the clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחוֹתָֽם׃\rb*\rb |לְיִ֨שָּׂשכָ֔ר\rb* \rb of the tribe|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Issachar|יִשָּׂשכָ֖ר\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \v 18 \rb Their territory|גְּבוּלָ֑ם\rb* \rb included|וַיְהִ֖י\rb* \rb Jezreel|יִזְרְעֶ֥אלָה\rb*, \rb Chesulloth|וְהַכְּסוּלֹ֖ת\rb*, \rb Shunem|וְשׁוּנֵֽם׃\rb*, \v 19 \rb Hapharaim|וַחֲפָרַ֥יִם\rb*, \rb Shion|וְשִׁיאֹ֖ן\rb*, \rb Anaharath|וַאֲנָחֲרַֽת׃\rb*, \v 20 \rb Rabbith|וְהָֽרַבִּ֥ית\rb*, \rb Kishion|וְקִשְׁי֖וֹן\rb*, \rb Ebez|וָאָֽבֶץ׃\rb*, \v 21 \rb Remeth|וְרֶ֧מֶת\rb*,\rb |וְעֵין־\rb* \rb En-gannim|גַּנִּ֛ים\rb*,\rb |וְעֵ֥ין\rb* \rb En-haddah|חַדָּ֖ה\rb*,\rb |וּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb and Beth-pazzez|פַּצֵּֽץ׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb The border|הַגְּב֨וּל\rb* \rb reached|וּפָגַע֩\rb* \rb Tabor|בְּתָב֤וֹר\rb*, \rb Shahazumah|וְשַׁחֲצוּמָה\rb*,\rb |וּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb and Beth-shemesh|שֶׁ֔מֶשׁ\rb*, \rb and ended|וְהָי֛וּ\rb*\rb |תֹּצְא֥וֹת\rb*\rb |גְּבוּלָ֖ם\rb* \rb at the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֑ן\rb*. \rb There were sixteen|שֵׁשׁ־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֥ים\rb*, \rb along with their villages|וְחַצְרֵיהֶֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb This|זֹ֗את\rb* \rb was the inheritance|נַחֲלַ֛ת\rb* \rb of the clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb of the tribe|מַטֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb of Issachar|יִשָּׂשכָ֖ר\rb*\rb |בְנֵֽי־\rb*, \rb including these cities|הֶעָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb and their villages|וְחַצְרֵיהֶֽן׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Asher’s Inheritance
\p \v 24 \rb The fifth|הַֽחֲמִישִׁ֔י\rb* \rb lot|הַגּוֹרָ֣ל\rb* \rb came out|וַיֵּצֵא֙\rb* \rb for the clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחוֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb of the tribe|לְמַטֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb of Asher|אָשֵׁ֖ר\rb*\rb |בְנֵֽי־\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \v 25 \rb Their territory|גְּבוּלָ֑ם\rb* \rb included|וַיְהִ֖י\rb* \rb Helkath|חֶלְקַ֥ת\rb*, \rb Hali|וַחֲלִ֖י\rb*, \rb Beten|וָבֶ֥טֶן\rb*, \rb Achshaph|וְאַכְשָֽׁף׃\rb*, \v 26 \rb Allammelech|וְאַֽלַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb*, \rb Amad|וְעַמְעָ֖ד\rb*, \rb and Mishal|וּמִשְׁאָ֑ל\rb*. \rb On the west|הַיָּ֔מָּה\rb* \rb the border touched|וּפָגַ֤ע\rb*\rb |וּבְשִׁיח֖וֹר\rb* \rb Carmel|בְּכַרְמֶל֙\rb* \rb and Shihor-libnath|לִבְנָֽת׃\rb*, \v 27 \rb then turned|וְשָׁ֨ב\rb* \rb eastward|מִזְרַ֣ח\rb*\rb |הַשֶּׁמֶשׁ֮\rb* \rb toward|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb Beth-dagon|דָּגֹן֒\rb*, \rb touched|וּפָגַ֣ע\rb* \rb Zebulun|בִּ֠זְבֻלוּן\rb* \rb and the Valley|וּבְגֵ֨י\rb*\rb |יִפְתַּח־\rb* \rb of Iphtah-el|אֵ֥ל\rb*, \rb and went north|צָפ֛וֹנָה\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb to Beth-emek|הָעֵ֖מֶק\rb* \rb and Neiel|וּנְעִיאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb passing|וְיָצָ֥א\rb* \rb Cabul|כָּב֖וּל\rb* \rb on the left|מִשְּׂמֹֽאל׃\rb*. \v 28 \rb It went on to Ebron|וְעֶבְרֹ֥ן\rb*,\f + \fr 19:28 \ft Some Hebrew manuscripts \fqa Abdon\ft ; see \ref Joshua 21:30|JOS 21:30\ref*.\f* \rb Rehob|וּרְחֹ֖ב\rb*, \rb Hammon|וְחַמּ֣וֹן\rb*, \rb and Kanah|וְקָנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb as|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb far as Greater|רַבָּֽה׃\rb* \rb Sidon|צִיד֥וֹן\rb*. \v 29 \rb The border|הַגְּבוּל֙\rb* \rb then turned back|וְשָׁ֤ב\rb* \rb toward Ramah|הָֽרָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb as far as|וְעַד־\rb* \rb the fortified|מִבְצַר־\rb* \rb city|עִ֖יר\rb* \rb of Tyre|צֹ֑ר\rb*,\rb |הַגְּבוּל֙\rb* \rb turned|וְשָׁ֤ב\rb* \rb toward Hosah|חֹסָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and came out|וְיִהְיוּ\rb*\rb |תֹצְאֹתָ֛יו\rb* \rb at the Sea|הַיָּ֖מָּה\rb*\f + \fr 19:29 \ft That is, the Mediterranean Sea, also called the Great Sea\f* \rb in the region|מֵחֶ֥בֶל\rb* \rb of Achzib|אַכְזִֽיבָה׃\rb*, \v 30 \rb Ummah|וְעֻמָ֥ה\rb*, \rb Aphek|וַאֲפֵ֖ק\rb*, \rb and Rehob|וּרְחֹ֑ב\rb*. \rb There were twenty-two|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁתַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֛ים\rb*, \rb along with their villages|וְחַצְרֵיהֶֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb This|זֹ֗את\rb* \rb was the inheritance|נַחֲלַ֛ת\rb* \rb of the clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb of the tribe|מַטֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb of Asher|אָשֵׁ֖ר\rb*\rb |בְנֵֽי־\rb*, \rb including these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb cities|הֶעָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb and their villages|וְחַצְרֵיהֶֽן׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Naphtali’s Inheritance
\p \v 32 \rb The sixth|הַשִּׁשִּׁ֑י\rb* \rb lot|הַגּוֹרָ֣ל\rb* \rb came out|יָצָ֖א\rb* \rb for the clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb of the tribe|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Naphtali|נַפְתָּלִ֖י\rb*\rb |נַפְתָּלִ֔י\rb*\rb |לִבְנֵ֣י\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \v 33 \rb Their border|גְבוּלָ֗ם\rb* \rb started|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb at Heleph|מֵחֵ֨לֶף\rb* \rb and the great tree|מֵֽאֵל֜וֹן\rb* \rb of Zaanannim|בְּצַעֲנַנִּ֗ים\rb*,\rb |וַאֲדָמִ֥י\rb* \rb passing Adami-nekeb|הַנֶּ֛קֶב\rb* \rb and Jabneel|וְיַבְנְאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb as far as|עַד־\rb* \rb Lakkum|לַקּ֑וּם\rb* \rb and ending|וַיְהִ֥י\rb*\rb |תֹצְאֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb at the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּֽן׃\rb*. \v 34 \rb Then the border|הַגְּב֥וּל\rb* \rb turned|וְשָׁ֨ב\rb* \rb westward|יָ֙מָּה֙\rb*\rb |אַזְנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb to Aznoth-tabor|תָּב֔וֹר\rb* \rb and ran|וְיָצָ֥א\rb* \rb from there|מִשָּׁ֖ם\rb* \rb to Hukkok|חוּקֹ֑קָה\rb*, \rb touching|וּפָגַ֨ע\rb* \rb Zebulun|בִּזְבֻל֜וּן\rb* \rb on the south side|מִנֶּ֗גֶב\rb*, \rb Asher|וּבְאָשֵׁר֙\rb*\rb |פָּגַ֣ע\rb* \rb on the west|מִיָּ֔ם\rb*, \rb and Judah|וּבִ֣יהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb at the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֖ן\rb*\f + \fr 19:34 \ft Hebrew; LXX \fqa west, and the Jordan\f* \rb on the east|מִזְרַ֥ח\rb*\rb |הַשָּֽׁמֶשׁ׃\rb*. \v 35 \rb The fortified|מִבְצָ֑ר\rb* \rb cities|וְעָרֵ֖י\rb* \rb were Ziddim|הַצִּדִּ֣ים\rb*, \rb Zer|צֵ֔ר\rb*, \rb Hammath|וְחַמַּ֖ת\rb*, \rb Rakkath|רַקַּ֥ת\rb*, \rb Chinnereth|וְכִנָּֽרֶת׃\rb*, \v 36 \rb Adamah|וַאֲדָמָ֥ה\rb*, \rb Ramah|וְהָרָמָ֖ה\rb*, \rb Hazor|וְחָצֽוֹר׃\rb*, \v 37 \rb Kedesh|וְקֶ֥דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb Edrei|וְאֶדְרֶ֖עִי\rb*,\rb |וְעֵ֥ין\rb* \rb En-hazor|חָצֽוֹר׃\rb*, \v 38 \rb Iron|וְיִרְאוֹן֙\rb*,\rb |וּמִגְדַּל־\rb* \rb Migdal-el|אֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb Horem|חֳרֵ֥ם\rb*,\rb |וּבֵית־\rb* \rb Beth-anath|עֲנָ֖ת\rb*,\rb |וּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb and Beth-shemesh|שָׁ֑מֶשׁ\rb*. \rb There were nineteen|תְּשַֽׁע־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֥ים\rb*, \rb along with their villages|וְחַצְרֵיהֶֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 39 \rb This|זֹ֗את\rb* \rb was the inheritance|נַחֲלַ֛ת\rb* \rb of the clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb of the tribe|מַטֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb of Naphtali|נַפְתָּלִ֖י\rb*\rb |בְנֵֽי־\rb*, \rb including these cities|הֶעָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb and their villages|וְחַצְרֵיהֶֽן׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Dan’s Inheritance
\p \v 40 \rb The seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִֽי׃\rb* \rb lot|הַגּוֹרָ֥ל\rb* \rb came out|יָצָ֖א\rb* \rb for the clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb of the tribe|לְמַטֵּ֥ה\rb*\rb |בְנֵי־\rb* \rb of Dan|דָ֖ן\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \v 41 \rb |וַיְהִ֖י\rb* \rb The territory|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb of their inheritance|נַחֲלָתָ֑ם\rb* \rb included Zorah|צָרְעָ֥ה\rb*, \rb Eshtaol|וְאֶשְׁתָּא֖וֹל\rb*,\rb |וְעִ֥יר\rb* \rb Ir-shemesh|שָֽׁמֶשׁ׃\rb*, \v 42 \rb Shaalabbin|וְשַֽׁעֲלַבִּ֥ין\rb*, \rb Aijalon|וְאַיָּל֖וֹן\rb*, \rb Ithlah|וְיִתְלָֽה׃\rb*, \v 43 \rb Elon|וְאֵיל֥וֹן\rb*, \rb Timnah|וְתִמְנָ֖תָה\rb*, \rb Ekron|וְעֶקְרֽוֹן׃\rb*, \v 44 \rb Eltekeh|וְאֶלְתְּקֵ֥ה\rb*, \rb Gibbethon|וְגִבְּת֖וֹן\rb*, \rb Baalath|וּבַעֲלָֽת׃\rb*, \v 45 \rb Jehud|וִיהֻ֥ד\rb*,\rb |וּבְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb Bene-berak|בְרַ֖ק\rb*,\rb |וְגַת־\rb* \rb Gath-rimmon|רִמּֽוֹן׃\rb*, \v 46 \rb |וּמֵ֥י\rb* \rb Me-jarkon|הַיַּרְק֖וֹן\rb*, \rb and Rakkon|וְהָֽרַקּ֑וֹן\rb*, \rb including|עִֽם־\rb* \rb the territory|הַגְּב֖וּל\rb* \rb across from|מ֥וּל\rb* \rb Joppa|יָפֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 47 (\rb Later, when the territory|גְבוּל־\rb* \rb of the Danites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |דָ֖ן\rb*\rb |מֵהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb was lost|וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb to them|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |דָ֠ן\rb*, \rb they went up|וַיַּעֲל֣וּ\rb* \rb and fought|וַיִּלָּחֲמ֨וּ\rb* \rb against|עִם־\rb* \rb Leshem|לֶ֜שֶׁם\rb*, \rb captured it|וַיִּלְכְּד֥וּ\rb*,\rb |אוֹתָ֣הּ׀\rb* \rb and put it|וַיַּכּ֧וּ\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֣הּ\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb to the sword|חֶ֗רֶב\rb*. \rb So they took possession|וַיִּֽרְשׁ֤וּ\rb* \rb of Leshem|אוֹתָהּ֙\rb*, \rb settled|וַיֵּ֣שְׁבוּ\rb* \rb there|בָ֔הּ\rb*, \rb and renamed|וַיִּקְרְא֤וּ\rb* \rb it|לְלֶ֙שֶׁם֙\rb* \rb after|כְּשֵׁ֖ם\rb* \rb their father|אֲבִיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb Dan|דָּ֔ן\rb*\rb |דָּ֥ן\rb*.)
\p \v 48 \rb This|זֹ֗את\rb* \rb was the inheritance|נַחֲלַ֛ת\rb* \rb of the clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb of the tribe|מַטֵּ֥ה\rb*\rb |בְנֵי־\rb* \rb of Dan|דָ֖ן\rb*, \rb including these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb cities|הֶֽעָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb and their villages|וְחַצְרֵיהֶֽן׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Joshua’s Inheritance
\p \v 49 \rb When they had finished|וַיְכַלּ֥וּ\rb* \rb distributing|לִנְחֹל־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb into its territories|לִגְבֽוּלֹתֶ֑יהָ\rb*, \rb the Israelites|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֧ל\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתְּנ֨וּ\rb* \rb Joshua|לִיהוֹשֻׁ֥עַ\rb* \rb son|בִּן־\rb* \rb of Nun|נ֖וּן\rb* \rb an inheritance|נַחֲלָ֛ה\rb* \rb among them|בְּתוֹכָֽם׃\rb*, \v 50 \rb as|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb had commanded|פִּ֨י\rb*. \rb They gave|נָ֣תְנוּ\rb* \rb him|ל֗וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִיר֙\rb* \rb of Timnath-serah|סֶ֖רַח\rb*\f + \fr 19:50 \fqa Timnath-serah \ft is also known as \fqa Timnath-heres\ft ; see \ref Judges 2:9|JDG 2:9\ref*.\f* \rb in the hill country|בְּהַ֣ר\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרָ֑יִם\rb*, \rb as|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he requested|שָׁאָ֔ל\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |תִּמְנַת־\rb* \rb He rebuilt|וַיִּבְנֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb and settled|וַיֵּ֥שֶׁב\rb* \rb in it|בָּֽהּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 51 \rb These are|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb the inheritances|הַנְּחָלֹ֡ת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֣ר\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֣ן׀\rb*, \rb Joshua|וִיהוֹשֻׁ֪עַ\rb* \rb son|בִּן־\rb* \rb of Nun|נ֟וּן\rb*, \rb and the heads|וְרָאשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of the families|הָֽאָב֣וֹת\rb* \rb distributed|נִחֲל֣וּ\rb* \rb by lot|בְּגוֹרָ֤ל׀\rb* \rb to the tribes|לְמַטּוֹת֩\rb*\rb |בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֨ל׀\rb* \rb at Shiloh|בְּשִׁלֹה֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb*. \rb So they finished|וַיְכַלּ֕וּ\rb* \rb dividing up|מֵֽחַלֵּ֖ק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃פ\rb*.
\c 20
\s1 Six Cities of Refuge
\r (\ref Numbers 35:9–34|NUM 35:9-34\ref*; \ref Deuteronomy 4:41–43|DEU 4:41-43\ref*; \ref Deuteronomy 19:1–14|DEU 19:1-14\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Tell|דַּבֵּ֛ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb to designate|תְּנ֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of refuge|הַמִּקְלָ֔ט\rb*, \rb as|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I instructed|דִּבַּ֥רְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb you through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb so that anyone|רוֹצֵ֔חַ\rb* \rb who kills|מַכֵּה־\rb* \rb another|נֶ֥פֶשׁ\rb* \rb unintentionally|בִּשְׁגָגָ֖ה\rb* \rb or accidentally|בִּבְלִי־\rb*\rb |דָ֑עַת\rb* \rb may flee|לָנ֥וּס\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֙מָּה֙\rb*. \rb These will be|וְהָי֤וּ\rb* \rb your|לָכֶם֙\rb* \rb refuge|לְמִקְלָ֔ט\rb* \rb from the avenger|מִגֹּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb of blood|הַדָּֽם׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb When someone flees|וְנָ֞ס\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb one|אַחַ֣ת׀\rb* \rb of these|הָאֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb cities|מֵהֶעָרִ֣ים\rb*, \rb stands|וְעָמַד֙\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֚תַח\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb*, \rb and states|וְדִבֶּ֛ר\rb*\rb |בְּאָזְנֵ֛י\rb* \rb his case|דְּבָרָ֑יו\rb* \rb before its elders|זִקְנֵ֥י־\rb*\rb |הַהִ֖יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הָעִֽיר\rb*, \rb they are to bring|וְאָסְפ֨וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֤וֹ\rb* \rb into the city|הָעִ֙ירָה֙\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and give|וְנָתְנוּ־\rb* \rb him|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb a place|מָק֖וֹם\rb* \rb to live|וְיָשַׁ֥ב\rb* \rb among them|עִמָּֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Now if|וְכִ֨י\rb* \rb the avenger|גֹּאֵ֤ל\rb* \rb of blood|הַדָּם֙\rb*\rb |אַֽחֲרָ֔יו\rb* \rb pursues him|יִרְדֹּ֜ף\rb*, \rb they must not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb surrender|יַסְגִּ֥רוּ\rb* \rb the manslayer|הָרֹצֵ֖חַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb into his hand|בְּיָד֑וֹ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb that man killed|הִכָּ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his neighbor|רֵעֵ֔הוּ\rb* \rb accidentally|בִבְלִי־\rb*\rb |דַ֙עַת֙\rb* \rb without|וְלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |מִתְּמ֥וֹל\rb* \rb prior|שִׁלְשֽׁוֹם׃\rb* \rb malice|שֹׂנֵ֥א\rb*\rb |ה֛וּא\rb*. \v 6 \rb He is to stay|וְיָשַׁ֣ב׀\rb* \rb in that|הַהִ֗יא\rb* \rb city|בָּעִ֣יר\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb he stands|עָמְד֞וֹ\rb* \rb trial|לַמִּשְׁפָּ֔ט\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb the assembly|הָֽעֵדָה֙\rb* \rb and until|עַד־\rb* \rb the death|מוֹת֙\rb* \rb of the high|הַגָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb priest|הַכֹּהֵ֣ן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb serving|יִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb at that|הָהֵ֑ם\rb* \rb time|בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb*. \rb Then|אָ֣ז׀\rb* \rb the manslayer|הָרוֹצֵ֗חַ\rb*\rb |וּבָ֤א\rb* \rb may return|יָשׁ֣וּב\rb* \rb to his own home|בֵּית֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the city|עִירוֹ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb from which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he fled|נָ֥ס\rb*\rb |מִשָּֽׁם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb So they set apart|וַיַּקְדִּ֜שׁוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Kedesh|קֶ֤דֶשׁ\rb* \rb in Galilee|בַּגָּלִיל֙\rb* \rb in the hill country|בְּהַ֣ר\rb* \rb of Naphtali|נַפְתָּלִ֔י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*, \rb Shechem|שְׁכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in the hill country|בְּהַ֣ר\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרָ֑יִם\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |קִרְיַ֥ת\rb* \rb and Kiriath-arba|אַרְבַּ֛ע\rb* \rb (that is|הִ֥יא\rb*, \rb Hebron|חֶבְר֖וֹן\rb*) \rb in the hill country|בְּהַ֥ר\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb And beyond|וּמֵעֵ֜בֶר\rb* \rb the Jordan|לְיַרְדֵּ֤ן\rb*, \rb east|מִזְרָ֔חָה\rb* \rb of Jericho|יְרִיחוֹ֙\rb*, \rb they designated|נָתְנ֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Bezer|בֶּ֧צֶר\rb* \rb on the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֛ר\rb* \rb plateau|בַּמִּישֹׁ֖ר\rb* \rb from the tribe|מִמַּטֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb of Reuben|רְאוּבֵ֑ן\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Ramoth|רָאמֹ֤ת\rb* \rb in Gilead|בַּגִּלְעָד֙\rb* \rb from the tribe|מִמַּטֵּה־\rb* \rb of Gad|גָ֔ד\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Golan|גָּלוֹן\rb* \rb in Bashan|בַּבָּשָׁ֖ן\rb* \rb from the tribe|מִמַּטֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּֽׁה׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb These|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb are|הָיוּ֩\rb* \rb the cities|עָרֵ֨י\rb* \rb appointed|הַמּֽוּעָדָ֜ה\rb* \rb for all|לְכֹ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb and foreigners|וְלַגֵּר֙\rb*\rb |הַגָּ֣ר\rb* \rb among them|בְּתוֹכָ֔ם\rb*, \rb so that anyone|כָּל־\rb* \rb who kills|מַכֵּה־\rb* \rb a person|נֶ֖פֶשׁ\rb* \rb unintentionally|בִּשְׁגָגָ֑ה\rb* \rb may flee|לָנ֣וּס\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֔מָּה\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb die|יָמ֗וּת\rb* \rb by the hand|בְּיַד֙\rb* \rb of the avenger|גֹּאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb of blood|הַדָּ֔ם\rb* \rb prior|עַד־\rb* \rb to standing trial|עָמְד֖וֹ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the assembly|הָעֵדָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\c 21
\s1 Forty-Eight Cities for the Levites
\r (\ref Numbers 35:1–8|NUM 35:1-8\ref*; \ref 1 Chronicles 6:54–81|1CH 6:54-81\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Now the family|אֲב֣וֹת\rb* \rb heads|רָאשֵׁי֙\rb* \rb of the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb approached|וַֽיִּגְּשׁ֗וּ\rb* \rb Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָר֙\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb*,\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb* \rb son|בִּן־\rb* \rb of Nun|נ֑וּן\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the heads|רָאשֵׁ֛י\rb*\rb |אֲב֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the other tribes|הַמַּטּ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |לִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 2 \rb at Shiloh|בְּשִׁלֹ֗ה\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנַ֙עַן֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb and said|וַיְדַבְּר֨וּ\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶ֜ם\rb*, “\rb The LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb commanded|צִוָּ֣ה\rb* \rb through|בְיַד־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb that we be given|לָֽתֶת־\rb*\rb |לָ֥נוּ\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb in which to live|לָשָׁ֑בֶת\rb*, \rb together with pasturelands|וּמִגְרְשֵׁיהֶ֖ן\rb* \rb for our livestock|לִבְהֶמְתֵּֽנוּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb So by|אֶל־\rb* \rb the command|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*, \rb the Israelites|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֧ל\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתְּנ֨וּ\rb* \rb the Levites|לַלְוִיִּ֛ם\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb cities|הֶעָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb their pasturelands|מִגְרְשֵׁיהֶֽן׃\rb* \rb out of their own inheritance|מִנַּחֲלָתָ֖ם\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \v 4 \rb The first lot|הַגּוֹרָ֖ל\rb* \rb came out|וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb for the Kohathite|הַקְּהָתִ֑י\rb* \rb clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹ֣ת\rb*. \rb The Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֗ם\rb* \rb who were descendants|לִבְנֵי֩\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֨ן\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb* \rb received|וַיְהִ֡י\rb* \rb thirteen|שְׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵֽה׃ס\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb by lot|בַּגּוֹרָ֔ל\rb* \rb from the tribes|מִמַּטֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb of Judah|יְ֠הוּדָה\rb*,\rb |וּמִמַּטֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb Simeon|הַשִּׁמְעֹנִ֜י\rb*,\rb |וּמִמַּטֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb and Benjamin|בִנְיָמִן֙\rb*.
\li1 \v 5 \rb The remaining|הַנּוֹתָרִ֗ים\rb* \rb descendants|וְלִבְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Kohath|קְהָ֜ת\rb* \rb received ten|עָֽשֶׂר׃ס\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb by lot|בַּגּוֹרָ֖ל\rb*\rb |מִמִּשְׁפְּחֹ֣ת\rb* \rb from the tribes|מַטֵּֽה־\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶ֠פְרַיִם\rb*, \rb Dan|דָ֞ן\rb*, \rb and|וּמֵחֲצִ֨י\rb* \rb the half-tribe|מַטֵּ֧ה\rb*\rb |וּֽמִמַּטֵּה־\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֛ה\rb*.
\li1 \v 6 \rb The descendants|וְלִבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Gershon|גֵרְשׁ֗וֹן\rb* \rb received thirteen|שְׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵֽה׃ס\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb by lot|בַּגּוֹרָ֔ל\rb*\rb |מִמִּשְׁפְּח֣וֹת\rb* \rb from the tribes|מַטֵּֽה־\rb* \rb of Issachar|יִשָּׂשכָ֣ר\rb*,\rb |וּמִמַּטֵּֽה־\rb* \rb Asher|אָ֠שֵׁר\rb*,\rb |וּמִמַּטֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb Naphtali|נַפְתָּלִ֜י\rb*, \rb and the half-tribe|וּ֠מֵחֲצִי\rb*\rb |מַטֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֤ה\rb* \rb in Bashan|בַבָּשָׁן֙\rb*.
\li1 \v 7 \rb And the descendants|לִבְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Merari|מְרָרִ֜י\rb* \rb received twelve|שְׁתֵּ֥ים\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵֽה׃\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָ֗ם\rb* \rb from the tribes|מִמַּטֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb of Reuben|רְאוּבֵ֤ן\rb*,\rb |וּמִמַּטֵּה־\rb* \rb Gad|גָד֙\rb*,\rb |וּמִמַּטֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb and Zebulun|זְבוּלֻ֔ן\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb So the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb allotted|וַיִּתְּנ֤וּ\rb*\rb |בַּגּוֹרָֽל׃פ\rb* \rb to the Levites|לַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb cities|הֶעָרִ֥ים\rb*, \rb together with their pasturelands|מִגְרְשֵׁיהֶ֑ן\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֧ה\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb*.
