\li1 \v 38 \rb And from the tribe|וּמִמַּטֵּה־\rb* \rb of Gad they were given|גָ֗ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Ramoth|רָמֹ֥ת\rb* \rb in Gilead|בַּגִּלְעָ֖ד\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb a city|עִיר֙\rb* \rb of refuge|מִקְלַ֣ט\rb* \rb for the manslayer|הָרֹצֵ֔חַ\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |מִגְרָשֶׁ֑הָ\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb Mahanaim|מַחֲנַ֖יִם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |מִגְרָשֶֽׁהָ׃\rb*, \v 39 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Heshbon|חֶשְׁבּוֹן֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |מִגְרָשֶׁ֔הָ\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and Jazer|יַעְזֵ֖ר\rb*— \rb four|אַרְבַּֽע׃\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb in all|כָּל־\rb*, \rb together with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb their pasturelands|מִגְרָשֶׁ֑הָ\rb*.
\li1 \v 40 \rb In all|כָּל־\rb*,\rb |הֶ֨עָרִ֜ים\rb* \rb twelve|שְׁתֵּ֥ים\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵֽה׃\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb were|וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb allotted|גּוֹרָלָ֔ם\rb* \rb to the clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb of Merari|מְרָרִי֙\rb*\rb |לִבְנֵ֤י\rb*, \rb the remaining|הַנּוֹתָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb Levite|הַלְוִיִּ֑ם\rb* \rb clans|מִמִּשְׁפְּח֣וֹת\rb*.
\p \v 41 \rb For the Levites, then|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb*, \rb there were forty-eight|אַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמֹנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb in all|כֹּ֚ל\rb*, \rb together with their pasturelands|וּמִגְרְשֵׁיהֶֽן׃\rb*, \rb within|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb the territory|אֲחֻזַּ֣ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |עָרִ֛ים\rb*. \v 42 \rb Each|הֶעָרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |עִ֣יר\rb* \rb of these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb cities|עִ֔יר\rb* \rb had|תִּֽהְיֶ֙ינָה֙\rb* \rb its own surrounding|סְבִיבֹתֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb pasturelands|וּמִגְרָשֶׁ֖יהָ\rb*; \rb this was true|כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb for all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃ס\rb* \rb cities|הֶעָרִ֥ים\rb*.
\p \v 43 \rb Thus the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He had sworn|נִשְׁבַּ֖ע\rb* \rb to give|לָתֵ֣ת\rb* \rb their fathers|לַאֲבוֹתָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and they took possession of it|וַיִּרָשׁ֖וּהָ\rb* \rb and settled|וַיֵּ֥שְׁבוּ\rb* \rb in it|בָֽהּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 44 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb gave them rest|וַיָּ֨נַח\rb*\rb |לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb on every side|מִסָּבִ֔יב\rb*, \rb just as|כְּכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb He had sworn|נִשְׁבַּ֖ע\rb* \rb to their fathers|לַאֲבוֹתָ֑ם\rb*. \rb None|וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |אִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb of their enemies|אֹ֣יְבֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb could stand|עָ֨מַד\rb* \rb against them|בִּפְנֵיהֶם֙\rb*, \rb for the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb delivered|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb their enemies|אֹ֣יְבֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb into their hand|בְּיָדָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 45 \rb Not one|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb of all|מִכֹּל֙\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb good|הַטּ֔וֹב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb promises|דָּבָ֔ר\rb*\rb |דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb had failed|נָפַ֣ל\rb*; \rb everything|הַכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb was fulfilled|בָּֽא׃פ\rb*.
\c 22
\s1 The Eastern Tribes Return Home
\p \v 1 \rb Then|אָ֚ז\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb* \rb summoned|יִקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb the Reubenites|לָרֽאוּבֵנִ֖י\rb*, \rb the Gadites|וְלַגָּדִ֑י\rb*, \rb and the half-tribe|וְלַחֲצִ֖י\rb*\rb |מַטֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּֽׁה׃\rb* \v 2 \rb and told them|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*,\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* “\rb You|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb have done|שְׁמַרְתֶּ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb the servant|עֶ֣בֶד\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb commanded|צִוָּ֣ה\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and you have obeyed|וַתִּשְׁמְע֣וּ\rb* \rb my voice|בְקוֹלִ֔י\rb* \rb in all|לְכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I commanded|צִוִּ֖יתִי\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb All this time|יָמִ֣ים\rb*\rb |רַבִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |זֶ֚ה\rb* \rb you have not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb deserted|עֲזַבְתֶּ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your brothers|אֲחֵיכֶ֗ם\rb*, \rb up to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this very day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֑ה\rb*, \rb but have kept|וּשְׁמַרְתֶּ֕ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the charge|מִשְׁמֶ֕רֶת\rb* \rb given you|מִצְוַ֖ת\rb* \rb by the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb And now that|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb has given your brothers|לַֽאֲחֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb rest|הֵנִ֨יחַ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb He promised|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֑ם\rb*,\rb |וְעַתָּ֡ה\rb* \rb you may return|פְּנוּ֩\rb*\rb |וּלְכ֨וּ\rb* \rb to|לָכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb your homes|לְאָהֳלֵיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֙רֶץ֙\rb*\rb |אֲחֻזַּתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר׀\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb the servant|עֶ֣בֶד\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb gave|נָתַ֣ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb across|בְּעֵ֖בֶר\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּֽן׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb But|רַ֣ק׀\rb* \rb be very|מְאֹ֗ד\rb* \rb careful|שִׁמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb to observe|לַעֲשׂ֨וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the commandment|הַמִּצְוָ֣ה\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the law|הַתּוֹרָה֮\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb the servant|עֶֽבֶד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֒\rb* \rb gave you|צִוָּ֣ה\rb*:\rb |אֶתְכֶם֮\rb* \rb to love|לְ֠אַהֲבָה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֜ם\rb*, \rb to walk|וְלָלֶ֧כֶת\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb His ways|דְּרָכָ֛יו\rb*, \rb to keep|וְלִשְׁמֹ֥ר\rb* \rb His commandments|מִצְוֺתָ֖יו\rb*, \rb to hold fast|וּלְדָבְקָה־\rb* \rb to Him|ב֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and to serve Him|וּלְעָבְד֕וֹ\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your heart|לְבַבְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and with all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb your soul|נַפְשְׁכֶֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 6 \rb So Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֑עַ\rb* \rb blessed them|וַֽיְבָרְכֵ֖ם\rb* \rb and sent them on their way|וַֽיְשַׁלְּחֵ֔ם\rb*, \rb and they went|וַיֵּלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb their homes|אָהֳלֵיהֶֽם׃ס\rb*. \v 7 (\rb To the half-tribe|וְלַחֲצִ֣י׀\rb*\rb |שֵׁ֣בֶט\rb* \rb of Manasseh|הַֽמְנַשֶּׁ֗ה\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁה֮\rb* \rb had given land|נָתַ֣ן\rb* \rb in Bashan|בַּבָּשָׁן֒\rb*, \rb and to the other half|וּלְחֶצְי֗וֹ\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb gave land|נָתַ֤ן\rb* \rb on the west|יָ֑מָּה\rb*\rb |וְ֠גַם\rb* \rb side|מֵעֵבֶר\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb among|עִם־\rb* \rb their brothers|אֲחֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*.) \rb When|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֛עַ\rb* \rb sent them|שִׁלְּחָ֧ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb their homes|אָהֳלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb he blessed them|וַיְבָרֲכֵֽם׃\rb*, \v 8 \rb saying|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Return|שׁ֤וּבוּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb to|אֲלֵיהֶ֜ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb your homes|אָֽהֳלֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb with your great|רַבִּ֜ים\rb* \rb wealth|בִּנְכָסִ֨ים\rb*, \rb with immense|רַב־\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb herds of livestock|וּבְמִקְנֶ֣ה\rb*, \rb with silver|בְּכֶ֨סֶף\rb*, \rb gold|וּבְזָהָ֜ב\rb*, \rb bronze|וּבִנְחֹ֧שֶׁת\rb*, \rb iron|וּבְבַרְזֶ֛ל\rb*, \rb and very many|הַרְבֵּ֣ה\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb clothes|וּבִשְׂלָמ֖וֹת\rb*. \rb Divide|חִלְק֥וּ\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb your brothers|אֲחֵיכֶֽם׃פ\rb* \rb the spoil|שְׁלַל־\rb* \rb of your enemies|אֹיְבֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*.”
\s1 The Altar of Witness
\p \v 9 \rb |וַיָּשֻׁ֣בוּ\rb* \rb So the Reubenites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |רְאוּבֵ֨ן\rb*, \rb the Gadites|וּבְנֵי־\rb*\rb |גָ֜ד\rb*, \rb and the half-tribe|וַחֲצִ֣י׀\rb*\rb |שֵׁ֣בֶט\rb* \rb of Manasseh|הַֽמְנַשֶּׁ֗ה\rb*\rb |מֵאֵת֙\rb* \rb left|וַיֵּלְכ֡וּ\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb at Shiloh|מִשִּׁלֹ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָ֑עַן\rb* \rb to return|לָלֶ֜כֶת\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb their own land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Gilead|הַגִּלְעָ֗ד\rb*,\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |אֶ֤רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֲחֻזָּתָם֙\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they had acquired|נֹֽאחֲזוּ־\rb* \rb according to|עַל־\rb* \rb the command|פִּ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb And when they came|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Geliloth|גְּלִיל֣וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 22:10 \ft Or \fqa to the circle of stones \ft or \fqa to the region\ft ; similarly in verse 11\f* \rb near the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָ֑עַן\rb*, \rb the Reubenites|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |רְאוּבֵ֣ן\rb*, \rb the Gadites|וּבְנֵי־\rb*\rb |גָ֡ד\rb*, \rb and the half-tribe|וַחֲצִ֣י\rb*\rb |שֵׁבֶט֩\rb* \rb of Manasseh|הַֽמְנַשֶּׁ֨ה\rb* \rb built|וַיִּבְנ֣וּ\rb*\rb |גָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb an imposing|לְמַרְאֶֽה׃\rb* \rb altar|מִזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֤ם\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb*\rb |מִזְבֵּ֥חַ\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb Then the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb received|וַיִּשְׁמְע֥וּ\rb* \rb the report|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*: “\rb Behold|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb*, \rb the Reubenites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |רְאוּבֵ֣ן\rb*, \rb the Gadites|וּבְנֵי־\rb*\rb |גָ֡ד\rb*, \rb and the half-tribe|וַחֲצִי֩\rb*\rb |שֵׁ֨בֶט\rb* \rb of Manasseh|הַֽמְנַשֶּׁ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb have built|בָנ֣וּ\rb* \rb an altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֗חַ\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the border|מוּל֙\rb* \rb of the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנַ֔עַן\rb*, \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb Geliloth|גְּלִילוֹת֙\rb* \rb near the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelite|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb side|עֵ֖בֶר\rb*.” \v 12 \rb And when they|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb heard this|וַֽיִּשְׁמְע֖וּ\rb*, \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַ֤ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb assembled|וַיִּקָּ֨הֲל֜וּ\rb* \rb at Shiloh|שִׁלֹ֔ה\rb* \rb to go|לַעֲל֥וֹת\rb* \rb to war|לַצָּבָֽא׃פ\rb* \rb against them|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb The Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלְח֨וּ\rb* \rb Phinehas|פִּינְחָ֖ס\rb* \rb son of|בֶּן־\rb* \rb Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֥ר\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵֽן׃\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Gilead|הַגִּלְעָ֑ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*, \rb to|אֶל־\rb*\rb |בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the Reubenites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |רְאוּבֵ֧ן\rb*, \rb the Gadites|גָ֛ד\rb*,\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and the half-tribe|חֲצִ֥י\rb*\rb |שֵֽׁבֶט־\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֖ה\rb*. \v 14 \rb With him|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb they sent ten|וַעֲשָׂרָ֤ה\rb* \rb chiefs|נְשִׂאִים֙\rb* — \rb one|אֶחָ֜ד\rb*\rb |נָשִׂ֤יא\rb*\rb |אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb family|לְבֵ֣ית\rb*\rb |אָ֔ב\rb* \rb leader|נָשִׂ֨יא\rb* \rb from each|לְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb tribe|מַטּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb each|וְאִ֨ישׁ\rb*\rb |הֵ֖מָּה\rb* \rb the head|רֹ֧אשׁ\rb* \rb of a family|בֵּית־\rb*\rb |אֲבוֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb among the clans|לְאַלְפֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb They went|וַיָּבֹ֜אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Reubenites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |רְאוּבֵ֧ן\rb*, \rb the Gadites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |גָ֛ד\rb*,\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and the half-tribe|חֲצִ֥י\rb*\rb |שֵֽׁבֶט־\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb in the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Gilead|הַגִּלְעָ֑ד\rb* \rb and said|וַיְדַבְּר֥וּ\rb* \rb to them|אִתָּ֖ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 16 “\rb This is what|כֹּ֣ה\rb* \rb the whole|כֹּ֣ל׀\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמְר֞וּ\rb*: ‘\rb What|מָֽה־\rb* \rb is this|הַזֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb breach of faith|מְעַלְתֶּם֙\rb* \rb you have committed|הַמַּ֤עַל\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb against the God|בֵּאלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb by turning away|לָשׁ֣וּב\rb* \rb from|מֵאַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and building|בִּבְנֽוֹתְכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb for yourselves|לָכֶם֙\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb*, \rb that you might rebel|לִמְרָדְכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb against the LORD|בַּיהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb this day|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb*?
\p \v 17 \rb Was not the sin|עֲוֺ֣ן\rb* \rb of Peor|פְּע֔וֹר\rb* \rb enough|הַמְעַט־\rb* \rb for us|לָ֙נוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*, \rb from which|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb we have not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb cleansed|הִטַּהַ֙רְנוּ֙\rb* \rb ourselves|מִמֶּ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*? \rb It even brought|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb a plague|הַנֶּ֖גֶף\rb* \rb upon the congregation|בַּעֲדַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb And now|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb*, \rb would you|וְאַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb turn away|תָּשֻׁ֣בוּ\rb* \rb from|מֵאַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*?\rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb If you|אַתֶּ֞ם\rb* \rb rebel|תִּמְרְד֤וּ\rb* \rb today|הַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb against the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb tomorrow|וּמָחָ֕ר\rb* \rb He will be angry|יִקְצֹֽף׃\rb* \rb with|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb indeed|וְאַ֨ךְ\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of your inheritance|אֲחֻזַּתְכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb is unclean|טְמֵאָ֜ה\rb*, \rb then cross over|עִבְר֨וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֨רֶץ\rb* \rb of the LORD’s|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb possession|אֲחֻזַּ֤ת\rb*, \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb tabernacle|מִשְׁכַּ֣ן\rb* \rb stands|שָֽׁכַן־\rb*,\rb |שָׁם֙\rb* \rb and take possession|וְהֵאָחֲז֖וּ\rb* \rb of it among us|בְּתוֹכֵ֑נוּ\rb*. \rb But do not|אַל־\rb* \rb rebel|תִּמְרֹ֗דוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֹתָ֙נוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |תִּמְרֹ֔דוּ\rb* \rb against the LORD|וּבַֽיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb or against us by building|בִּבְנֹֽתְכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb for yourselves|לָכֶם֙\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb* \rb other than|מִֽבַּלְעֲדֵ֔י\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֖ח\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb Was not|הֲל֣וֹא׀\rb* \rb Achan|עָכָ֣ן\rb*\f + \fr 22:20 \fqa Achan \ft means \fqa troubler\ft ; also called \fqa Achar\ft in \ref 1 Chronicles 2:7|1CH 2:7\ref*.\f* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zerah|זֶ֗רַח\rb* \rb unfaithful|מָ֤עַל\rb* \rb regarding|מַ֙עַל֙\rb* \rb what was set apart for destruction|בַּחֵ֔רֶם\rb*,\f + \fr 22:20 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering.\f* \rb bringing wrath|קָ֑צֶף\rb* \rb upon|וְעַֽל־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*?\rb |הָ֣יָה\rb* \rb Yet it was not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb only|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb Achan|וְהוּא֙\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb who perished|גָוַ֖ע\rb* \rb because of his sin|בַּעֲוֺנֽוֹ׃פ\rb*!’”
\p \v 21 \rb Then the Reubenites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |רְאוּבֵ֣ן\rb*, \rb the Gadites|וּבְנֵי־\rb*\rb |גָ֔ד\rb*, \rb and the half-tribe|וַחֲצִ֖י\rb*\rb |שֵׁ֣בֶט\rb* \rb of Manasseh|הַֽמְנַשֶּׁ֑ה\rb*\rb |וַֽיְדַבְּר֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb answered|וַֽיַּעֲנוּ֙\rb* \rb the leaders|רָאשֵׁ֖י\rb* \rb of the clans|אַלְפֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*: \v 22 “\rb The LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*, \rb the Mighty One|אֵל֩׀\rb*, \rb is God|אֱלֹהִ֨ים׀\rb*! \rb The LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb the Mighty One|אֵ֣ל׀\rb*, \rb is God|אֱלֹהִ֤ים׀\rb*! \rb He|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb knows|יֹדֵ֔עַ\rb*, \rb and may Israel|וְיִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb also know|יֵדָ֑ע\rb*. \rb If this|אִם־\rb* \rb was in rebellion|בְּמֶ֤רֶד\rb*\rb |וְאִם־\rb* \rb or breach of faith|בְּמַ֙עַל֙\rb* \rb against the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb spare us|תּוֹשִׁיעֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb If we have built|לִבְנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb for ourselves|לָ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb* \rb to turn away|לָשׁ֖וּב\rb* \rb from|מֵאַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb Him|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and|וְאִם־\rb* \rb to offer|לְהַעֲל֨וֹת\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עוֹלָ֣ה\rb* \rb and grain offerings|וּמִנְחָ֗ה\rb* \rb on it|עָלָ֜יו\rb*, \rb or|וְאִם־\rb* \rb to sacrifice|לַעֲשׂ֤וֹת\rb* \rb peace|שְׁלָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb offerings|זִבְחֵ֣י\rb* \rb on it|עָלָיו֙\rb*, \rb may the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb Himself|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb hold us accountable|יְבַקֵּֽשׁ׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb But in fact|וְאִם־\rb* \rb we have done|עָשִׂ֥ינוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|זֹ֖את\rb*\rb |מִדָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb for fear|מִדְּאָגָה֙\rb* \rb that in the future|מָחָ֗ר\rb*\rb |יֹאמְר֨וּ\rb* \rb your descendants|בְנֵיכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb might say|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb to ours|לְבָנֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* ‘\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb have you to do|לָּכֶ֕ם\rb* \rb with the LORD|וְלַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*? \v 25 \rb For the LORD|יְ֠הוָה\rb* \rb has made|נָֽתַן־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb a border|וּגְב֣וּל\rb* \rb between us|בֵּינֵ֨נוּ\rb* \rb and you|וּבֵינֵיכֶ֜ם\rb*\rb |בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb Reubenites|רְאוּבֵ֤ן\rb* \rb and|וּבְנֵי־\rb* \rb Gadites|גָד֙\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb You have no|אֵין־\rb* \rb share|חֵ֖לֶק\rb* \rb in the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֑ה\rb*!’ \rb So your descendants could cause|בְנֵיכֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb ours|בָּנֵ֔ינוּ\rb*\rb |לְבִלְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb to stop|וְהִשְׁבִּ֤יתוּ\rb* \rb fearing|יְרֹ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb That is why we said|וַנֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, ‘\rb Let us take action|נַעֲשֶׂה־\rb*\rb |נָּ֣א\rb* \rb and build|לִבְנ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb an altar for ourselves|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb*, \rb but not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb for burnt offerings|לְעוֹלָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb or sacrifices|לְזָֽבַח׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb Rather|כִּי֩\rb*, \rb let it be|ה֜וּא\rb* \rb a witness|עֵ֨ד\rb* \rb between us|בֵּינֵ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb and you|וּבֵינֵיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb and|וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb the generations|דֹּרוֹתֵינוּ֮\rb* \rb to come|אַחֲרֵינוּ֒\rb*, \rb that we will worship|לַעֲבֹ֞ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |עֲבֹדַ֤ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb in His presence|לְפָנָ֔יו\rb* \rb with our burnt offerings|בְּעֹלוֹתֵ֥ינוּ\rb*, \rb sacrifices|וּבִזְבָחֵ֖ינוּ\rb*, \rb and peace offerings|וּבִשְׁלָמֵ֑ינוּ\rb*.’ \rb Then in the future|מָחָר֙\rb*, \rb your descendants|בְנֵיכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb cannot|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb say|יֹאמְר֨וּ\rb* \rb to ours|לְבָנֵ֔ינוּ\rb*, ‘\rb You have no|אֵין־\rb* \rb share|חֵ֖לֶק\rb* \rb in the LORD|בַּיהוָֽה׃\rb*!’
\p \v 28 \rb Therefore we said|וַנֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*\rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb*, ‘\rb If they ever|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb say this|יֹאמְר֥וּ\rb* \rb to us|אֵלֵ֛ינוּ\rb* \rb or|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb to our descendants|דֹּרֹתֵ֖ינוּ\rb*\rb |מָחָ֑ר\rb*, \rb we will answer|וְאָמַ֡רְנוּ\rb*: \rb Look at|רְא֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the replica|תַּבְנִית֩\rb* \rb of the altar|מִזְבַּ֨ח\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb our fathers|אֲבוֹתֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb made|עָשׂ֣וּ\rb*, \rb not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb for burnt offerings|לְעוֹלָה֙\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb or sacrifices|לְזֶ֔בַח\rb*, \rb but|כִּי־\rb* \rb as a witness|עֵ֣ד\rb*\rb |ה֔וּא\rb* \rb between us|בֵּינֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb and you|וּבֵינֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.’
\p \v 29 \rb Far be it|חָלִילָה֩\rb* \rb from us|לָּ֨נוּ\rb* \rb to rebel|לִמְרֹ֣ד\rb* \rb against the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and turn away|וְלָשׁ֤וּב\rb* \rb from|מִמֶּ֜נּוּ\rb*\rb |מֵאַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb Him|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb today|הַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb by building|לִבְנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb* \rb for burnt offerings|לְעֹלָ֖ה\rb*, \rb grain offerings|לְמִנְחָ֣ה\rb*, \rb or sacrifices|וּלְזָ֑בַח\rb*, \rb other than|מִלְּבַ֗ד\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּח֙\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ\rb*, \rb which stands|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb His tabernacle|מִשְׁכָּנֽוֹ׃פ\rb*.”
\p \v 30 \rb When Phinehas|פִּֽינְחָ֣ס\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb and the chiefs|וּנְשִׂיאֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the congregation|הָעֵדָ֜ה\rb* — \rb the heads|וְרָאשֵׁ֨י\rb* \rb of Israel’s|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb clans|אַלְפֵ֤י\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb were with him|אִתּ֔וֹ\rb* —\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַ֨דְּבָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֞ע\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb the descendants|בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of Reuben|רְאוּבֵ֥ן\rb*,\rb |וּבְנֵי־\rb* \rb Gad|גָ֖ד\rb*,\rb |וּבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb and Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֑ה\rb* \rb had to say|דִּבְּר֛וּ\rb*, \rb they were satisfied|וַיִּיטַ֖ב\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 31 \rb Phinehas|פִּֽינְחָ֣ס\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֣ר\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֡ן\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the descendants|בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of Reuben|רְאוּבֵ֨ן\rb*,\rb |וְאֶל־\rb*\rb |בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb Gad|גָ֜ד\rb*,\rb |וְאֶל־\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb and Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֗ה\rb*, “\rb Today|הַיּ֤וֹם׀\rb* \rb we know|יָדַ֙עְנוּ֙\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb is among us|בְתוֹכֵ֣נוּ\rb*, \rb because|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb you have not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb committed|מְעַלְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb breach of faith|הַמַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb against Him|בַּֽיהוָ֖ה\rb*. \rb Consequently|אָ֗ז\rb*, \rb you have delivered|הִצַּלְתֶּ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 32 \rb Then Phinehas|פִּֽינְחָ֣ס\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֣ר\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֣ן׀\rb*, \rb together with the other leaders|וְהַנְּשִׂיאִ֡ים\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֣ת\rb*, \rb returned|וַיָּ֣שָׁב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנַ֖עַן\rb* \rb and brought back|וַיָּשִׁ֥בוּ\rb* \rb a report regarding|דָּבָֽר׃\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb the Reubenites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |רְאוּבֵן֩\rb*\rb |וּמֵאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb and Gadites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |גָ֜ד\rb* \rb in the land|מֵאֶ֧רֶץ\rb* \rb of Gilead|הַגִּלְעָ֛ד\rb*. \v 33 \rb The Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb were satisfied|וַיִּיטַ֣ב\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֵי֙\rb* \rb with the report|הַדָּבָ֗ר\rb*, \rb and they|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb blessed|וַיְבָרֲכ֥וּ\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb and spoke|אָמְר֗וּ\rb* \rb no|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb more about going|לַעֲל֤וֹת\rb* \rb to war|לַצָּבָ֔א\rb* \rb against them|עֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb to destroy|לְשַׁחֵת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the Reubenites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |רְאוּבֵ֥ן\rb* \rb and Gadites|וּבְנֵי־\rb*\rb |גָ֖ד\rb* \rb lived|יֹשְׁבִ֥ים\rb*. \v 34 \rb So the Reubenites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |רְאוּבֵ֥ן\rb* \rb and Gadites|וּבְנֵי־\rb*\rb |גָ֖ד\rb* \rb named|וַֽיִּקְרְא֛וּ\rb* \rb the altar Witness|לַמִּזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb*, \rb for they said|כִּ֣י\rb*,\f + \fr 22:34 \ft Literally \fqa named the altar, for\f* “\rb It|הוּא֙\rb* \rb is a witness|עֵ֥ד\rb* \rb between us|בֵּֽינֹתֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb is God|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃פ\rb*.”
\c 23
\s1 Joshua’s Charge to Leaders
\p \v 1 \rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb A long|רַבִּ֔ים\rb* \rb time|מִיָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb after|אַ֠חֲרֵי\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb had given Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb rest|הֵנִ֨יחַ\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the enemies|אֹיְבֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb around them|מִסָּבִ֑יב\rb*, \rb when Joshua|וִיהוֹשֻׁ֣עַ\rb* \rb was old|זָקֵ֔ן\rb* \rb and well along|בָּ֖א\rb* \rb in years|בַּיָּמִֽים׃\rb*, \v 2 \rb he|יְהוֹשֻׁ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb including its elders|לִזְקֵנָיו֙\rb*, \rb leaders|וּלְרָאשָׁ֔יו\rb*, \rb judges|וּלְשֹׁפְטָ֖יו\rb*, \rb and officers|וּלְשֹֽׁטְרָ֑יו\rb*. “\rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am old|זָקַ֔נְתִּי\rb* \rb and well along|בָּ֖אתִי\rb* \rb in years|בַּיָּמִֽים׃\rb*,” \rb he said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb*, \v 3 “\rb and you|וְאַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb have seen|רְאִיתֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֵת֩\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb has done|עָשָׂ֜ה\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb nations|הַגּוֹיִ֥ם\rb* \rb for your sake|מִפְּנֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb it|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb was the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb who fought|הַנִּלְחָ֥ם\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb See|רְאוּ֩\rb*, \rb I have allotted|הִפַּ֨לְתִּי\rb* \rb as an inheritance|בְּנַחֲלָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb to your tribes|לְשִׁבְטֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb remaining|הַנִּשְׁאָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb nations|הַ֠גּוֹיִם\rb*, \rb including all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have already cut off|הִכְרַ֔תִּי\rb*, \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb westward|מְב֥וֹא\rb*\rb |הַשָּֽׁמֶשׁ׃\rb* \rb to the Great Sea|וְהַיָּ֥ם\rb*\rb |הַגָּד֖וֹל\rb*.\f + \fr 23:4 \ft That is, the Mediterranean Sea\f* \v 5 \rb The LORD|וַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |ה֚וּא\rb* \rb will push them|יֶהְדֳּפֵ֣ם\rb* \rb out of your way|מִפְּנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and drive them out|וְהוֹרִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb before you|אֹתָ֖ם\rb*\rb |מִלִּפְנֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb so that you can take possession of|וִֽירִשְׁתֶּם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their land|אַרְצָ֔ם\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb promised|דִּבֶּ֛ר\rb* \rb you|לָכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Be very|מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb strong, then|וַחֲזַקְתֶּ֣ם\rb*, \rb so that you can keep|לִשְׁמֹ֣ר\rb* \rb and obey|וְלַעֲשׂ֔וֹת\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that is written|הַכָּת֔וּב\rb* \rb in the Book|בְּסֵ֖פֶר\rb* \rb of the Law|תּוֹרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Moses|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb*, \rb not|לְבִלְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb turning aside|סוּר־\rb* \rb from it|מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb to the right|יָמִ֥ין\rb* \rb or to the left|וּשְׂמֹֽאול׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb So you are not|לְבִלְתִּי־\rb* \rb to associate|בוֹא֙\rb* \rb with these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb nations|בַּגּוֹיִ֣ם\rb* \rb that remain|הַנִּשְׁאָרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb among you|אִתְּכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb You must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb call on|תַזְכִּ֙ירוּ֙\rb* \rb the names|וּבְשֵׁ֨ם\rb* \rb of their gods|אֱלֹהֵיהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb swear by them|תַשְׁבִּ֔יעוּ\rb*, \rb and you must not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb serve them|תַעַבְד֔וּם\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb bow down|תִֽשְׁתַּחֲו֖וּ\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb Instead|כִּ֛י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb*, \rb you shall hold fast|תִּדְבָּ֑קוּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|בַּיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you have done|עֲשִׂיתֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb The LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb has driven out|וַיּ֤וֹרֶשׁ\rb* \rb great|גְּדֹלִ֣ים\rb* \rb and powerful|וַעֲצוּמִ֑ים\rb*\rb |וְאַתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb nations|גּוֹיִ֖ם\rb* \rb before you|מִפְּנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb one|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb can stand|עָ֤מַד\rb* \rb against you|בִּפְנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*. \v 10 \rb |אִישׁ־\rb* \rb One|אֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb of you|מִכֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb can put|יִרְדָּף־\rb* \rb a thousand to flight|אָ֑לֶף\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |ה֚וּא\rb* \rb fights|הַנִּלְחָ֣ם\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb He promised|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb*. \v 11 \rb Therefore watch|וְנִשְׁמַרְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb yourselves|לְנַפְשֹֽׁתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb carefully|מְאֹ֖ד\rb*, \rb that you love|לְאַהֲבָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb For|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you turn away|שׁ֣וֹב\rb*\rb |תָּשׁ֗וּבוּ\rb* \rb and cling|וּדְבַקְתֶּם֙\rb* \rb to the rest|בְּיֶ֙תֶר֙\rb* \rb of these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb nations|הַגּוֹיִ֣ם\rb* \rb that remain|הַנִּשְׁאָרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb among you|אִתְּכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and if you intermarry|וְהִֽתְחַתַּנְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb and associate|וּבָאתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb with them|וְהֵ֥ם\rb*, \v 13 \rb know for sure|יָד֙וֹעַ֙\rb*\rb |תֵּֽדְע֔וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּי֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb will no|לֹ֨א\rb* \rb longer|יוֹסִ֜יף\rb* \rb drive out|לְהוֹרִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb nations|הַגּוֹיִ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb before you|מִלִּפְנֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Instead, they will become|וְהָי֨וּ\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb a snare|לְפַ֣ח\rb* \rb and a trap|וּלְמוֹקֵ֗שׁ\rb*, \rb a scourge|וּלְשֹׁטֵ֤ט\rb* \rb in your sides|בְּצִדֵּיכֶם֙\rb* \rb and thorns|וְלִצְנִנִ֣ים\rb* \rb in your eyes|בְּעֵינֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb you perish|אֲבָדְכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb from|מֵ֠עַל\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb good|הַטּוֹבָה֙\rb* \rb land|הָאֲדָמָ֤ה\rb* \rb 