\c 24
\s1 Joshua Reviews Israel’s History
\p \v 1 \rb Then Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֛עַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb assembled|וַיֶּאֶסֹ֧ף\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb at Shechem|שְׁכֶ֑מָה\rb*. \rb He summoned|וַיִּקְרָא֩\rb* \rb the elders|לְזִקְנֵ֨י\rb*, \rb leaders|וּלְרָאשָׁ֗יו\rb*, \rb judges|וּלְשֹֽׁפְטָיו֙\rb*, \rb and officers|וּלְשֹׁ֣טְרָ֔יו\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb*, \rb and they presented|וַיִּֽתְיַצְּב֖וּ\rb* \rb themselves before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb And Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֜עַ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֗ם\rb*, “\rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb*, \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: ‘\rb Long ago|מֵֽעוֹלָ֔ם\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶם֙\rb*, \rb including Terah|תֶּ֛רַח\rb* \rb the father|אֲבִ֥י\rb* \rb of Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb*\rb |וַאֲבִ֣י\rb* \rb and Nahor|נָח֑וֹר\rb*, \rb lived|יָשְׁב֤וּ\rb* \rb beyond|בְּעֵ֣בֶר\rb* \rb the Euphrates|הַנָּהָ֗ר\rb*\f + \fr 24:2 \ft Hebrew \fqa the River\ft ; also in verses 3, 14, and 15\f* \rb and worshiped|וַיַּעַבְד֖וּ\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִֽים׃\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb*. \v 3 \rb But I took|וָ֠אֶקַּח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your father|אֲבִיכֶ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָם֙\rb* \rb from beyond|מֵעֵ֣בֶר\rb* \rb the Euphrates|הַנָּהָ֔ר\rb* \rb and led|וָאוֹלֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb him|אוֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb through all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָ֑עַן\rb*, \rb and I multiplied|וָאֶרֶב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his descendants|זַרְע֔וֹ\rb*. \rb I gave|וָֽאֶתֶּן־\rb* \rb him|ל֖וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָֽק׃\rb*, \v 4 \rb and to Isaac|לְיִצְחָ֔ק\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb I gave|וָאֶתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Esau|עֵשָׂ֑ו\rb*. \rb I gave|וָאֶתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb Esau|לְעֵשָׂ֜ו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Mount|הַ֤ר\rb* \rb Seir|שֵׂעִיר֙\rb* \rb to possess|לָרֶ֣שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אוֹת֔וֹ\rb*, \rb but Jacob|וְיַעֲקֹ֥ב\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבָנָ֖יו\rb* \rb went down|יָרְד֥וּ\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Then I sent|וָאֶשְׁלַ֞ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֤ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb and Aaron|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb*, \rb and I afflicted|וָאֶגֹּ֣ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb by what|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I did|עָשִׂ֖יתִי\rb* \rb there|בְּקִרְבּ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and afterward|וְאַחַ֖ר\rb* \rb I brought you out|הוֹצֵ֥אתִי\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb When I brought|וָֽאוֹצִ֤יא\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb out of Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and you reached|וַתָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb the Red Sea|הַיָּ֑מָּה\rb*,\f + \fr 24:6 \ft Or \fqa the Sea of Reeds\f* \rb the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֜יִם\rb* \rb pursued|וַיִּרְדְּפ֨וּ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֧י\rb* \rb them|אֲבוֹתֵיכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb with chariots|בְּרֶ֥כֶב\rb* \rb and horsemen|וּבְפָרָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb as far as the Red Sea|יַם־\rb*\rb |סֽוּף׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb So your fathers cried out|וַיִּצְעֲק֣וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb and He put|וַיָּ֨שֶׂם\rb* \rb darkness|מַֽאֲפֵ֜ל\rb* \rb between|בֵּינֵיכֶ֣ם׀\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb you and the Egyptians|הַמִּצְרִ֗ים\rb*, \rb over whom|עָלָ֤יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb He brought|וַיָּבֵ֨א\rb* \rb the sea|הַיָּם֙\rb* \rb and engulfed them|וַיְכַסֵּ֔הוּ\rb*. \rb Your very eyes|עֵינֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb saw|וַתִּרְאֶ֙ינָה֙\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I did|עָשִׂ֖יתִי\rb* \rb to the Egyptians|בְּמִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*. \rb Then you lived|וַתֵּשְׁב֥וּ\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַמִּדְבָּ֖ר\rb* \rb for a long|רַבִּֽים׃\rb* \rb time|יָמִ֥ים\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Later, I brought|וָאָבִאָה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb you to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Amorites|הָאֱמֹרִי֙\rb* \rb who lived|הַיּוֹשֵׁב֙\rb* \rb beyond|בְּעֵ֣בֶר\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb*. \rb They fought|וַיִּֽלָּחֲמ֖וּ\rb* \rb against you|אִתְּכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb but I delivered|וָאֶתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֤ם\rb* \rb into your hand|בְּיֶדְכֶם֙\rb*, \rb that you should possess|וַתִּֽירְשׁ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their land|אַרְצָ֔ם\rb* \rb when I destroyed them|וָאַשְׁמִידֵ֖ם\rb* \rb before you|מִפְּנֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb Then Balak|בָּלָ֤ק\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zippor|צִפּוֹר֙\rb*, \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָ֔ב\rb*, \rb set out|וַיָּ֨קָם\rb* \rb to fight|וַיִּלָּ֖חֶם\rb* \rb against Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb He sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֗ח\rb*\rb |וַיִּקְרָ֛א\rb* \rb for Balaam|לְבִלְעָ֥ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Beor|בְּע֖וֹר\rb* \rb to curse you|לְקַלֵּ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb*, \v 10 \rb but I would|אָבִ֖יתִי\rb* \rb not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb listen|לִשְׁמֹ֣עַ\rb* \rb to Balaam|לְבִלְעָ֑ם\rb*. \rb So he blessed you again and again|וַיְבָ֤רֶךְ\rb*\rb |בָּרוֹךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and I delivered|וָאַצִּ֥ל\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb from his hand|מִיָּדֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb After this, you crossed|וַתַּעַבְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּן֮\rb* \rb and came|וַתָּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jericho|יְרִיחוֹ֒\rb*. \rb The people|בַּעֲלֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Jericho|יְ֠רִיחוֹ\rb* \rb fought|וַיִּלָּחֲמ֣וּ\rb* \rb against you|בָכֶ֣ם\rb*, \rb as did the Amorites|הָֽאֱמֹרִ֨י\rb*, \rb Perizzites|וְהַפְּרִזִּ֜י\rb*, \rb Canaanites|וְהַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֗י\rb*, \rb Hittites|וְהַֽחִתִּי֙\rb*, \rb Girgashites|וְהַגִּרְגָּשִׁ֔י\rb*, \rb Hivites|הַֽחִוִּ֖י\rb*, \rb and Jebusites|וְהַיְבוּסִ֑י\rb*, \rb and I delivered|וָאֶתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb into your hand|בְּיֶדְכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb I sent|וָאֶשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb the hornet|הַצִּרְעָ֔ה\rb* \rb ahead of you|לִפְנֵיכֶם֙\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and it drove out|וַתְּגָ֤רֶשׁ\rb*\rb |אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb the two|שְׁנֵ֖י\rb* \rb Amorite|הָאֱמֹרִ֑י\rb* \rb kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb before you|מִפְּנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb but not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb by your own sword|בְחַרְבְּךָ֖\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb or bow|בְקַשְׁתֶּֽךָ׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb So I gave|וָאֶתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֣רֶץ׀\rb* \rb on which|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb you did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb toil|יָגַ֣עְתָּ\rb* \rb and cities|וְעָרִים֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb build|בְנִיתֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and now you live|וַתֵּשְׁב֖וּ\rb* \rb in them|בָּהֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |אַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb and eat|אֹכְלִֽים׃\rb* \rb from vineyards|כְּרָמִ֤ים\rb* \rb and olive groves|וְזֵיתִים֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb plant|נְטַעְתֶּ֔ם\rb*.’
\s1 Choose Whom You Will Serve
\r (\ref Deuteronomy 10:12–22|DEU 10:12-22\ref*)
\p \v 14 \rb Now, therefore|וְעַתָּ֞ה\rb*, \rb fear|יְר֧אוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb and serve|וְעִבְד֥וּ\rb* \rb Him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb in sincerity|בְּתָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb and truth|וּבֶֽאֱמֶ֑ת\rb*; \rb cast aside|וְהָסִ֣ירוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the gods|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבוֹתֵיכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb served|עָבְד֨וּ\rb* \rb beyond|בְּעֵ֤בֶר\rb* \rb the Euphrates|הַנָּהָר֙\rb* \rb and in Egypt|וּבְמִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*, \rb and serve|וְעִבְד֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb But if|וְאִם֩\rb* \rb it is unpleasing|רַ֨ע\rb* \rb in your sight|בְּֽעֵינֵיכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb to serve|לַעֲבֹ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb then choose|בַּחֲר֨וּ\rb* \rb for yourselves|לָכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb this day|הַיּוֹם֮\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb whom|מִ֣י\rb* \rb you will serve|תַעֲבֹדוּן֒\rb*, \rb whether the|אִ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֞ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבוֹתֵיכֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb served|עָבְד֣וּ\rb* \rb beyond|בְּעֵבֶר\rb* \rb the Euphrates|הַנָּהָ֔ר\rb*, \rb or|וְאִם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the gods|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Amorites|הָאֱמֹרִ֔י\rb* \rb in whose|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb land|בְּאַרְצָ֑ם\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb are living|יֹשְׁבִ֣ים\rb*. \rb As for me|וְאָנֹכִ֣י\rb* \rb and my house|וּבֵיתִ֔י\rb*, \rb we will serve|נַעֲבֹ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*!”
\p \v 16 \rb The people|הָעָם֙\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֔אמֶר\rb* \rb replied|וַיַּ֤עַן\rb*, “\rb Far be it|חָלִ֣ילָה\rb* \rb from us|לָּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb to forsake|מֵעֲזֹ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb to serve|לַעֲבֹ֖ד\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִֽים׃\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb*! \v 17 \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ\rb*\rb |הוּא֩\rb* \rb brought|הַמַּעֲלֶ֨ה\rb* \rb us|אֹתָ֧נוּ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb our fathers|אֲבוֹתֵ֛ינוּ\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb*, \rb out of the house|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of slavery|עֲבָדִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and|וַאֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb performed|עָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb great|הַגְּדֹלוֹת֙\rb* \rb signs|הָאֹת֤וֹת\rb* \rb before our eyes|לְעֵינֵ֗ינוּ\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb He also protected us|וַֽיִּשְׁמְרֵ֗נוּ\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb our journey|הַדֶּ֙רֶךְ֙\rb* \rb and among all|וּבְכֹל֙\rb* \rb the nations|הָֽעַמִּ֔ים\rb* \rb through which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb we traveled|עָבַ֖רְנוּ\rb*\rb |בְּקִרְבָּֽם׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb drove out|וַיְגָ֨רֶשׁ\rb* \rb before us|מִפָּנֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the nations|הָעַמִּ֗ים\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb including the Amorites|הָאֱמֹרִ֛י\rb* \rb who lived|יֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb in the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*. \rb We|אֲנַ֙חְנוּ֙\rb* \rb too|גַּם־\rb* \rb will serve|נַעֲבֹ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb He|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb is our God|אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃ס\rb*!”
\p \v 19 \rb But Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֜עַ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֗ם\rb*, “\rb You are not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb able|תֽוּכְלוּ֙\rb* \rb to serve|לַעֲבֹ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb He|ה֑וּא\rb* \rb is a holy|קְדֹשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb*; \rb He|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb is a jealous|קַנּ֣וֹא\rb* \rb God|אֵֽל־\rb*; \rb He will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb forgive|יִשָּׂ֥א\rb* \rb your rebellion|לְפִשְׁעֲכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb or your sins|וּלְחַטֹּאותֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb If|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you forsake|תַֽעַזְבוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and serve|וַעֲבַדְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb foreign|נֵכָ֑ר\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb*, \rb He will turn|וְשָׁ֨ב\rb* \rb and bring disaster|וְהֵרַ֤ע\rb* \rb on you|לָכֶם֙\rb* \rb and consume|וְכִלָּ֣ה\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb even after|אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb He has been good|הֵיטִ֥יב\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 21 “\rb No|לֹ֕א\rb*!”\rb |כִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |יְהוֹשֻׁ֑עַ\rb*. “\rb We will serve|נַעֲבֹֽד׃\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*!”
\p \v 22 \rb Then Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֜עַ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb them|הָעָ֗ם\rb*, “\rb You|אַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb are witnesses|עֵדִ֤ים\rb* \rb against yourselves|בָּכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֞ם\rb* \rb have chosen|בְּחַרְתֶּ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to serve|לַעֲבֹ֣ד\rb*\rb |אוֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*.”
\p “\rb We are witnesses|עֵדִֽים׃\rb*!” \rb they said|וַיֹּאמְר֖וּ\rb*.
\p \v 23 “\rb Now, therefore,” he said,|וְעַתָּ֕ה\rb* “\rb get rid of|הָסִ֛ירוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the foreign|הַנֵּכָ֖ר\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb among you|בְּקִרְבְּכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and incline|וְהַטּוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your hearts|לְבַבְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.”
\p \v 24 \rb So the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמְר֥וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֑עַ\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* “\rb We will serve|נַעֲבֹ֔ד\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb and obey|נִשְׁמָֽע׃\rb* \rb His voice|וּבְקוֹל֖וֹ\rb*.”
\p \v 25 \rb On that|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֧עַ\rb* \rb made|וַיִּכְרֹ֨ת\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִ֛ית\rb* \rb for the people|לָעָ֖ם\rb*, \rb and there at Shechem|בִּשְׁכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb he established|וַיָּ֥שֶׂם\rb* \rb for them|ל֛וֹ\rb* \rb a statute|חֹ֥ק\rb* \rb and ordinance|וּמִשְׁפָּ֖ט\rb*. \v 26 \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֙עַ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb recorded|וַיִּכְתֹּ֤ב\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb things|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb in the Book|בְּסֵ֖פֶר\rb* \rb of the Law|תּוֹרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*. \rb Then he took|וַיִּקַּח֙\rb* \rb a large|גְּדוֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb stone|אֶ֣בֶן\rb* \rb and set it up|וַיְקִימֶ֣הָ\rb* \rb there|שָּׁ֔ם\rb* \rb under|תַּ֚חַת\rb* \rb the oak|הָֽאַלָּ֔ה\rb*\f + \fr 24:26 \ft Or \fqa terebinth\f* \rb that was|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb near the sanctuary|בְּמִקְדַּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*. \v 27 \rb And Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֜עַ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֗ם\rb*, “\rb You see|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּאת֙\rb* \rb stone|הָאֶ֤בֶן\rb*. \rb It will be|תִּֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb a witness|לְעֵדָ֔ה\rb* \rb against us|בָּ֣נוּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb it|הִ֣יא\rb* \rb has heard|שָׁמְעָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|אִמְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb has spoken|דִּבֶּ֖ר\rb* \rb to us|עִמָּ֑נוּ\rb*, \rb and it will be|וְהָיְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb a witness|לְעֵדָ֔ה\rb* \rb against you|בָכֶם֙\rb* \rb if you ever|פֶּֽן־\rb* \rb deny|תְּכַחֲשׁ֖וּן\rb* \rb your God|בֵּאלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 28 \rb Then Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֙עַ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sent the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb away|וַיְשַׁלַּ֤ח\rb*, \rb each|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb to his own inheritance|לְנַחֲלָתֽוֹ׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Joshua’s Death and Burial
\r (\ref Judges 2:6–9|JDG 2:6-9\ref*)
\p \v 29 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb Some time later|אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb*\rb |הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb*\rb |הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb*, \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֥עַ\rb* \rb son|בִּן־\rb* \rb of Nun|נ֖וּן\rb*, \rb the servant|עֶ֣בֶד\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb died|וַיָּ֛מָת\rb* \rb at the age|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנִֽים׃\rb* \rb of 110|מֵאָ֥ה\rb*. \v 30 \rb And they buried|וַיִּקְבְּר֤וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb in the land|בִּגְב֣וּל\rb* \rb of his inheritance|נַחֲלָת֔וֹ\rb*,\rb |בְּתִמְנַת־\rb* \rb at Timnath-serah|סֶ֖רַח\rb*\f + \fr 24:30 \fqa Timnath-serah \ft is also known as \fqa Timnath-heres\ft ; see \ref Judges 2:9|JDG 2:9\ref*.\f*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in the hill country|בְּהַר־\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרָ֑יִם\rb*, \rb north|מִצְּפ֖וֹן\rb* \rb of Mount|לְהַר־\rb* \rb Gaash|גָּֽעַשׁ׃\rb*. \v 31 \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had served|וַיַּעֲבֹ֤ד\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb throughout|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֑עַ\rb* \rb and|וְכֹ֣ל׀\rb*\rb |יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the elders|הַזְּקֵנִ֗ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb outlived|הֶאֱרִ֤יכוּ\rb*\rb |יָמִים֙\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb him|יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb* \rb and|וַאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb who had experienced|יָדְע֗וּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the works|מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had done|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb for Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 32 \rb And|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the bones|עַצְמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Joseph|י֠וֹסֵף\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֥ל׀\rb* \rb had brought up|הֶעֱל֨וּ\rb* \rb out of Egypt|מִמִּצְרַיִם֮\rb*, \rb were buried|קָבְר֣וּ\rb* \rb at Shechem|בִשְׁכֶם֒\rb* \rb in the plot|בְּחֶלְקַ֣ת\rb* \rb of land|הַשָּׂדֶ֗ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֛ב\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb had purchased|קָנָ֧ה\rb* \rb from the sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Hamor|חֲמ֥וֹר\rb*, \rb Shechem’s|שְׁכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb father|אֲבִֽי־\rb*, \rb for a hundred|בְּמֵאָ֣ה\rb* \rb pieces of silver|קְשִׂיטָ֑ה\rb*.\f + \fr 24:32 \ft Hebrew \fqa a hundred kesitahs\ft ; the value or weight of the kesitah is no longer known.\f* \rb So it became|וַיִּֽהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb an inheritance|לְנַחֲלָֽה׃\rb* \rb for Joseph’s|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb descendants|לִבְנֵֽי־\rb*.
\p \v 33 \rb Eleazar|וְאֶלְעָזָ֥ר\rb* \rb son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb also died|מֵ֑ת\rb*, \rb and they buried|וַיִּקְבְּר֣וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֗וֹ\rb* \rb at Gibeah|בְּגִבְעַת֙\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had been given|נִתַּן־\rb* \rb to his|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb son|בְּנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Phinehas|פִּֽינְחָ֣ס\rb* \rb in the hill country|בְּהַ֥ר\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרָֽיִם׃\rb*.
